{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N6ia7wYDyxDNtjpDPAbqsd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n2\t\n3\tCard: The Dawning Archaic — `{10}` Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7.\n4\tOracle text:\n5\t- This spell costs `{1}` less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard.\n6\t- Reach\n7\t- Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\n8\t\n9\t## File\n10\t\n11\t`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n12\t\n13\tImports follow the project convention (`cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl`, `engine.card`,\n14\t`engine.types`, `engine.events`, `test_utils`). Test classes follow the FDN\n15\t`tests.py` style (`TestX` grouping by behaviour).\n16\t\n17\t### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties — static card data\n18\t- `test_is_creature` — card is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n19\t- `test_name` — name is exactly \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n20\t- `test_mana_cost_is_ten_generic` — mana cost equals `{10}` (10 generic).\n21\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 7/7.\n22\t- `test_is_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (type line \"Legendary Creature\").\n23\t- `test_is_avatar` — subtype includes \"Avatar\".\n24\t- `test_has_reach` — has `Keyword.REACH`.\n25\t- `test_no_flying` — does NOT have `Keyword.FLYING` (guards against an over-broad\n26\t  keyword set; Reach is the only printed keyword).\n27\t\n28\t### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction — \"costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard\"\n29\tModelled via `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` (the engine queries this and clamps\n30\tto printed generic in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n31\t- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — empty graveyard yields 0.\n32\t- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` — one instant in graveyard yields 1.\n33\t- `test_counts_both_instants_and_sorceries` — 2 instants + 1 sorcery yields 3\n34\t  (verifies both card types count, not just instants).\n35\t- `test_ignores_non_instant_sorcery_cards` — creatures in the graveyard are not\n36\t  counted; only the single instant contributes.\n37\t- `test_ignores_opponent_graveyard` — \"in *your* graveyard\": the opponent's\n38\t  instants/sorceries do not reduce the cost.\n39\t- `test_reduction_never_negative` — reduction is a non-negative integer.\n40\t- `test_large_graveyard_can_exceed_printed_generic` — with 12 instants the raw\n41\t  per-card reduction is at least the printed generic of 10 (clamping is the\n42\t  engine's job, tested separately).\n43\t\n44\t### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReductionPayment — engine clamping at payment time\n45\tExercises `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`, the public API the cast pipeline\n46\tuses, so the contract covers the end-to-end payable reduction.\n47\t- `test_engine_clamps_reduction_to_generic` — 15 instants ⇒ clamped to 10.\n48\t- `test_engine_reduction_matches_count_when_below_generic` — 1 instant + 1\n49\t  sorcery ⇒ 2 (below the cap, so unclamped).\n50\t\n51\t### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackTrigger — \"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks…\"\n52\tModelled via `register_triggers` wiring an `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger keyed\n53\tto this creature (same pattern as FDN attack-trigger cards, e.g. fdn_8).\n54\t- `test_registers_attack_trigger` — registering adds exactly one trigger for this\n55\t  source.\n56\t- `test_trigger_watches_attacks_event` — the registered trigger's `event_type`\n57\t  is `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n58\t- `test_trigger_controller_is_card_controller` — trigger controller is the card's\n59\t  controller (\"*you* may cast\").\n60\t- `test_trigger_condition_fires_for_self` — condition accepts an attack event that\n61\t  names this creature (or is unconditioned).\n62\t- `test_trigger_condition_ignores_other_attacker` — condition rejects an attack\n63\t  event for a different creature; a condition-less trigger is treated as a\n64\t  failure since the ability is keyed to *this* creature attacking.\n65\t\n66\t### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackTriggerEffect — event firing reaches the stack\n67\t- `test_attack_event_pushes_trigger_onto_stack` — firing an `AttacksTriggeredEvent`\n68\t  for this creature pushes the triggered ability onto the stack.\n69\t- `test_unrelated_attack_event_does_not_push_trigger` — firing the event for a\n70\t  different attacker leaves the stack empty.\n71\t\n72\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n73\t\n74\t- **Full resolution of \"cast target instant or sorcery from graveyard without\n75\t  paying its mana cost\"** — exercising the on-stack effect that lets the player\n76\t  choose a graveyard spell and cast it free would require driving the\n77\t  `DeterministicPlayer` \"you may\" / target-choice pipeline through the trigger\n78\t  effect, which depends on implementation-internal details (how the card surfaces\n79\t  the target choice and invokes `cast_spell_free`). Testing it here would couple\n80\t  the contract to a specific implementation shape. The trigger registration,\n81\t  conditioning, and stack-push are covered instead, which pin the observable\n82\t  contract. See `untestable.json` for the residual requirements escalated to the\n83\t  Coordinator/Implementer.\n84\t\n85\t- **\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"** — this is\n86\t  a replacement effect that only applies to the *cast* spell after it resolves;\n87\t  asserting it requires the free-cast pipeline above to run first, so it is\n88\t  escalated rather than tested with a brittle setup.\n89\t\n90\t- **Legend rule / state-based actions** — handled by the engine's SBA layer\n91\t  (covered by `engine_tests/`), not card-specific behaviour. Out of scope.\n92\t\n93\t- **Reach combat interaction** (blocking fliers) — Reach's combat semantics are\n94\t  engine behaviour; the card contract here is only that the keyword is present.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"ee527fc4-ab8d-4c48-bcb3-cc0cb350386c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:29:33.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n\nCard: The Dawning Archaic — `{10}` Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7.\nOracle text:\n- This spell costs `{1}` less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard.\n- Reach\n- Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\n\n## File\n\n`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n\nImports follow the project convention (`cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl`, `engine.card`,\n`engine.types`, `engine.events`, `test_utils`). Test classes follow the FDN\n`tests.py` style (`TestX` grouping by behaviour).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties — static card data\n- `test_is_creature` — card is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_name` — name is exactly \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n- `test_mana_cost_is_ten_generic` — mana cost equals `{10}` (10 generic).\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 7/7.\n- `test_is_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (type line \"Legendary Creature\").\n- `test_is_avatar` — subtype includes \"Avatar\".\n- `test_has_reach` — has `Keyword.REACH`.\n- `test_no_flying` — does NOT have `Keyword.FLYING` (guards against an over-broad\n  keyword set; Reach is the only printed keyword).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction — \"costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard\"\nModelled via `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` (the engine queries this and clamps\nto printed generic in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — empty graveyard yields 0.\n- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` — one instant in graveyard yields 1.\n- `test_counts_both_instants_and_sorceries` — 2 instants + 1 sorcery yields 3\n  (verifies both card types count, not just instants).\n- `test_ignores_non_instant_sorcery_cards` — creatures in the graveyard are not\n  counted; only the single instant contributes.\n- `test_ignores_opponent_graveyard` — \"in *your* graveyard\": the opponent's\n  instants/sorceries do not reduce the cost.\n- `test_reduction_never_negative` — reduction is a non-negative integer.\n- `test_large_graveyard_can_exceed_printed_generic` — with 12 instants the raw\n  per-card reduction is at least the printed generic of 10 (clamping is the\n  engine's job, tested separately).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReductionPayment — engine clamping at payment time\nExercises `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`, the public API the cast pipeline\nuses, so the contract covers the end-to-end payable reduction.\n- `test_engine_clamps_reduction_to_generic` — 15 instants ⇒ clamped to 10.\n- `test_engine_reduction_matches_count_when_below_generic` — 1 instant + 1\n  sorcery ⇒ 2 (below the cap, so unclamped).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackTrigger — \"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks…\"\nModelled via `register_triggers` wiring an `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger keyed\nto this creature (same pattern as FDN attack-trigger cards, e.g. fdn_8).\n- `test_registers_attack_trigger` — registering adds exactly one trigger for this\n  source.\n- `test_trigger_watches_attacks_event` — the registered trigger's `event_type`\n  is `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_trigger_controller_is_card_controller` — trigger controller is the card's\n  controller (\"*you* may cast\").\n- `test_trigger_condition_fires_for_self` — condition accepts an attack event that\n  names this creature (or is unconditioned).\n- `test_trigger_condition_ignores_other_attacker` — condition rejects an attack\n  event for a different creature; a condition-less trigger is treated as a\n  failure since the ability is keyed to *this* creature attacking.\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackTriggerEffect — event firing reaches the stack\n- `test_attack_event_pushes_trigger_onto_stack` — firing an `AttacksTriggeredEvent`\n  for this creature pushes the triggered ability onto the stack.\n- `test_unrelated_attack_event_does_not_push_trigger` — firing the event for a\n  different attacker leaves the stack empty.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **Full resolution of \"cast target instant or sorcery from graveyard without\n  paying its mana cost\"** — exercising the on-stack effect that lets the player\n  choose a graveyard spell and cast it free would require driving the\n  `DeterministicPlayer` \"you may\" / target-choice pipeline through the trigger\n  effect, which depends on implementation-internal details (how the card surfaces\n  the target choice and invokes `cast_spell_free`). Testing it here would couple\n  the contract to a specific implementation shape. The trigger registration,\n  conditioning, and stack-push are covered instead, which pin the observable\n  contract. See `untestable.json` for the residual requirements escalated to the\n  Coordinator/Implementer.\n\n- **\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"** — this is\n  a replacement effect that only applies to the *cast* spell after it resolves;\n  asserting it requires the free-cast pipeline above to run first, so it is\n  escalated rather than tested with a brittle setup.\n\n- **Legend rule / state-based actions** — handled by the engine's SBA layer\n  (covered by `engine_tests/`), not card-specific behaviour. Out of scope.\n\n- **Reach combat interaction** (blocking fliers) — Reach's combat semantics are\n  engine behaviour; the card contract here is only that the keyword is present.\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}}}
