{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019ADJuAbpwr5tBoRGoqsZWG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RZhHGxcGj9dvExdE6jAVE9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":11578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1007,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4GY9BkXY1JQZZUdSFXSfC","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"a5c3841c-9411-44cd-a666-ae8059cbf64b","request_id":"req_011CbcPWpAuDGBMRdDLwA52v","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RZhHGxcGj9dvExdE6jAVE9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic — Implementation Rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Card class (`cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py`)\n4\t`TheDawningArchaic(Creature)` — `{10}`, 7/7, Legendary, Avatar, Reach.\n5\t\n6\t- **Cost reduction** via `cost_reduction(game)`: counts instant/sorcery cards in\n7\t  the controller's graveyard (`game.get_graveyard(controller)`), returning the\n8\t  raw per-card count. The engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the printed\n9\t  generic ({10}) at payment time, matching the existing `CardImpl.cost_reduction`\n10\t  contract. \"Your graveyard\" only — opponent graveyards are ignored.\n11\t- **Attack trigger** via `register_triggers`: registers an\n12\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` `TriggerRegistration` whose condition is\n13\t  `event.creature is self`, controller = the card's controller. Mirrors the FDN\n14\t  attack-trigger pattern (fdn_217, fdn_245).\n15\t\n16\t## Free-cast-from-graveyard + exile contract (the escalated requirements)\n17\tThe trigger effect `_cast_from_graveyard` is fully implemented and scriptable\n18\tthrough `DeterministicPlayer`:\n19\t\n20\t1. `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` — the \"you may\" clause. Script `True` to use.\n21\t2. `controller.choose_card(candidates, ...)` — selects the target instant/sorcery\n22\t   from the controller's graveyard (candidates filtered to instants/sorceries).\n23\t3. The chosen spell is cast for free via the existing\n24\t   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`,\n25\t   moving it graveyard → stack with no mana paid.\n26\t4. Before casting, an exile-instead replacement is registered for that specific\n27\t   spell (see below). The spell is also flagged\n28\t   `spell._exile_if_goes_to_graveyard = True` as an observable marker.\n29\t\n30\tOn the trigger StackObject resolving, the spell appears on the stack zone and has\n31\tleft the graveyard; when the spell itself resolves it is exiled instead of going\n32\tto the graveyard.\n33\t\n34\t## \"Exile instead of graveyard\" via the replacement machinery\n35\t- New additive event `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of\n36\t  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`) in `engine/events.py`, carrying the `spell`\n37\t  and a `card` property. It represents an instant/sorcery about to move from the\n38\t  stack to a graveyard on resolution.\n39\t- `_register_exile_replacement` registers a standard `ReplacementEffect`\n40\t  (`engine/replacement_effects.py`) keyed to the spell as `source`, condition\n41\t  `event.spell is spell and destination == \"graveyard\"`, replacement sets\n42\t  `destination = \"exile\"`.\n43\t- `engine/casting._resolve_spell` (body change, additive) now routes\n44\t  non-permanent spells through a new helper\n45\t  `_resolve_spell_graveyard_destination`, which builds a\n46\t  `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent`, runs it through\n47\t  `game.replacement_manager.apply`, and moves the spell to the resulting zone\n48\t  (graveyard by default, exile when redirected). After the move it unregisters\n49\t  the spell's replacement and clears the flag so nothing lingers.\n50\t\n51\tThis is purely additive: existing `_resolve_spell` behavior for spells with no\n52\tmatching replacement is unchanged (still graveyard), confirmed by the full\n53\tengine regression suite (1145 passed) and FDN tests (39 passed).\n54\t\n55\t## Engine changes\n56\t- `engine/events.py`: added `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (new class only).\n57\t- `engine/casting.py`: modified the body of `_resolve_spell` to consult\n58\t  replacements on the stack→graveyard move; added helper\n59\t  `_resolve_spell_graveyard_destination` and `_SPELL_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP`.\n60\t  No renames/moves/deletions.\n61\t\n62\t## No spec deviations.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4GY9BkXY1JQZZUdSFXSfC","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"ed281e08-fb17-4108-8824-623c31491834","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:33:40.116Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_1"}
