{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a7be7a2504a2f2749","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MG2KMCFQQq7c1hNb1wPg3e","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":72792,"tool_uses":35,"duration_ms":155708},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"1be71f44-7faf-4592-a128-44468b88109b","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SpbKVWQuH7EJXLxCikPzKq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LhYUeW6zBFSuucc9jct6CP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n\nCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery.\nOracle: *Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage\nto any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\nspent to cast this spell.*\n\n## File\n\n`cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n\nThe converge precedent is FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle): the engine writes the\ncolors of mana spent during payment onto the card as `colors_spent`\n(`engine/casting.py` ~line 229 sets it to `list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`,\na list of `engine.mana.Color`). X is the number of *distinct* colors in that\nlist. Because the printed cost is a pure `{6}` generic cost, X depends entirely\non which mana the player actually used, ranging 0–5. Tests set `colors_spent`\ndirectly (the FDN 205 pattern) to drive the converge logic in isolation, and set\n`chosen_targets` directly (the FDN 13 pattern) to supply the targets.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneProperties — static card data\n- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery` with `CardType.SORCERY`.\n- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n- `test_mana_cost_is_six_generic` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n- `test_not_a_creature` / `test_no_power_toughness` — guards against an\n  over-broad type set (it is a noncreature spell).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting — target requirements\n- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — the spell advertises two targets:\n  the target player (draw) and the \"any target\" (damage).\n- `test_player_target_accepts_a_player` — a requirement accepts a player object\n  (the \"target player draws\" clause).\n- `test_any_target_accepts_player_and_creature` — a requirement accepts a\n  creature (the damage \"any target\").\n- `test_any_target_rejects_non_creature_permanent` — \"any target\" must not\n  accept a plain land (only players, creatures, planeswalkers, battles).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeResolution — X-driven effects\n- `test_two_colors_draws_two_deals_two_gains_two` — X=2 drives all three\n  clauses simultaneously.\n- `test_x_counts_distinct_colors_not_pips` — three red pips still yield X=1\n  (distinct colors, not pip count).\n- `test_five_colors_draws_five_deals_five_gains_five` — X=5 (WUBRG) upper bound.\n- `test_zero_colors_is_full_noop` — X=0 (only generic mana): draw/damage/gain\n  are all zero.\n- `test_damage_to_creature_target` — the damage clause marks damage on a\n  creature target (not just a player).\n- `test_life_gain_credited_to_controller_not_target_player` — \"you gain X life\"\n  credits the controller, even when the draw target is the opponent.\n- `test_target_player_draws_not_controller` — the draw goes to the chosen\n  target player, which may be the opponent rather than the controller.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneResolutionRobustness — defensive resolution\n- `test_resolve_with_no_colors_spent_attr_is_noop` — missing `colors_spent`\n  defaults X to 0; resolution does not raise and changes nothing.\n- `test_resolve_with_no_targets_does_not_raise` — with colors spent but no\n  chosen targets, resolution does not raise; the untargeted \"you gain X life\"\n  clause still applies.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- X spanning the full 0–5 range, including the 0 no-op and the 5 maximum.\n- Distinct-color counting (duplicate pips do not inflate X).\n- Damage routed to a creature vs. a player (\"any target\").\n- Life gain credited to the controller, decoupled from the draw target player.\n- Defensive resolution with absent `colors_spent` / `chosen_targets`.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (out of scope)\n- Full cast pipeline color-of-mana tracking through `cast_spell` with a real\n  mixed mana pool — that is engine behavior (`last_payment_colors`) already\n  covered by `engine_tests/test_mana.py` / `test_hybrid_mana.py`. These tests\n  exercise the *card's* use of `colors_spent`, set directly per the FDN 205\n  convention, rather than re-testing the engine's payment-color recording.\n- \"any target\" acceptance of planeswalkers/battles — the convenience harness\n  has no planeswalker/battle fixture readily available; player + creature +\n  land rejection sufficiently pin the target filter's contract.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":71922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MG2KMCFQQq7c1hNb1wPg3e","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"312fcaec-07b1-4484-b558-cafae59131c2","request_id":"req_011CbcQ1VkBraZbFWu42SRAK","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_4"}
