{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkhUGdxcsyJRLco2r2zJdU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery.\n4\tOracle: *Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage\n5\tto any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\n6\tspent to cast this spell.*\n7\t\n8\t## File\n9\t\n10\t`cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n11\t\n12\tThe converge precedent is FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle): the engine writes the\n13\tcolors of mana spent during payment onto the card as `colors_spent`\n14\t(`engine/casting.py` ~line 229 sets it to `list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`,\n15\ta list of `engine.mana.Color`). X is the number of *distinct* colors in that\n16\tlist. Because the printed cost is a pure `{6}` generic cost, X depends entirely\n17\ton which mana the player actually used, ranging 0–5. Tests set `colors_spent`\n18\tdirectly (the FDN 205 pattern) to drive the converge logic in isolation, and set\n19\t`chosen_targets` directly (the FDN 13 pattern) to supply the targets.\n20\t\n21\t### TestTogetherAsOneProperties — static card data\n22\t- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery` with `CardType.SORCERY`.\n23\t- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n24\t- `test_mana_cost_is_six_generic` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n25\t- `test_not_a_creature` / `test_no_power_toughness` — guards against an\n26\t  over-broad type set (it is a noncreature spell).\n27\t\n28\t### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting — target requirements\n29\t- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — the spell advertises two targets:\n30\t  the target player (draw) and the \"any target\" (damage).\n31\t- `test_player_target_accepts_a_player` — a requirement accepts a player object\n32\t  (the \"target player draws\" clause).\n33\t- `test_any_target_accepts_player_and_creature` — a requirement accepts a\n34\t  creature (the damage \"any target\").\n35\t- `test_any_target_rejects_non_creature_permanent` — \"any target\" must not\n36\t  accept a plain land (only players, creatures, planeswalkers, battles).\n37\t\n38\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeResolution — X-driven effects\n39\t- `test_two_colors_draws_two_deals_two_gains_two` — X=2 drives all three\n40\t  clauses simultaneously.\n41\t- `test_x_counts_distinct_colors_not_pips` — three red pips still yield X=1\n42\t  (distinct colors, not pip count).\n43\t- `test_five_colors_draws_five_deals_five_gains_five` — X=5 (WUBRG) upper bound.\n44\t- `test_zero_colors_is_full_noop` — X=0 (only generic mana): draw/damage/gain\n45\t  are all zero.\n46\t- `test_damage_to_creature_target` — the damage clause marks damage on a\n47\t  creature target (not just a player).\n48\t- `test_life_gain_credited_to_controller_not_target_player` — \"you gain X life\"\n49\t  credits the controller, even when the draw target is the opponent.\n50\t- `test_target_player_draws_not_controller` — the draw goes to the chosen\n51\t  target player, which may be the opponent rather than the controller.\n52\t\n53\t### TestTogetherAsOneResolutionRobustness — defensive resolution\n54\t- `test_resolve_with_no_colors_spent_attr_is_noop` — missing `colors_spent`\n55\t  defaults X to 0; resolution does not raise and changes nothing.\n56\t- `test_resolve_with_no_targets_does_not_raise` — with colors spent but no\n57\t  chosen targets, resolution does not raise; the untargeted \"you gain X life\"\n58\t  clause still applies.\n59\t\n60\t## Edge cases covered\n61\t- X spanning the full 0–5 range, including the 0 no-op and the 5 maximum.\n62\t- Distinct-color counting (duplicate pips do not inflate X).\n63\t- Damage routed to a creature vs. a player (\"any target\").\n64\t- Life gain credited to the controller, decoupled from the draw target player.\n65\t- Defensive resolution with absent `colors_spent` / `chosen_targets`.\n66\t\n67\t## Edge cases NOT covered (out of scope)\n68\t- Full cast pipeline color-of-mana tracking through `cast_spell` with a real\n69\t  mixed mana pool — that is engine behavior (`last_payment_colors`) already\n70\t  covered by `engine_tests/test_mana.py` / `test_hybrid_mana.py`. These tests\n71\t  exercise the *card's* use of `colors_spent`, set directly per the FDN 205\n72\t  convention, rather than re-testing the engine's payment-color recording.\n73\t- \"any target\" acceptance of planeswalkers/battles — the convenience harness\n74\t  has no planeswalker/battle fixture readily available; player + creature +\n75\t  land rejection sufficiently pin the target filter's contract.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013PFpPuM4TrJuL5iPtrQwzQ","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"dce34871-b99e-442f-9ad2-0272dac4c83b","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:40:47.216Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_4"}
