{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0191c2LZgrqSMAjGiGzqjvMB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t`{6}` Sorcery with a converge-driven resolution: target player draws X, the\n5\tspell deals X damage to any target, and the controller gains X life, where X is\n6\tthe number of *distinct* colors of mana spent to cast it.\n7\t\n8\t## Key decisions\n9\t- **Base class**: `Sorcery` (gives `CardType.SORCERY`, no power/toughness, not a\n10\t  `Creature`), satisfying the static-data tests.\n11\t- **X = distinct colors**: `x = len(set(self.colors_spent))`. The engine records\n12\t  colors spent during payment as `colors_spent` (FDN 205 convention); duplicate\n13\t  pips collapse via `set()`, so three red pips yield X=1. Defaults to `[]` in\n14\t  `__init__`, so a missing/empty `colors_spent` makes X=0 and resolution a no-op\n15\t  (covered by the robustness tests).\n16\t- **Targeting**: two `TargetRequirement`s — a \"target player\" (filter\n17\t  `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`) and an \"any target\" (player, creature, or\n18\t  planeswalker). The \"any target\" filter rejects plain non-creature permanents\n19\t  like lands. There is no `CardType.BATTLE` in `engine/types.py`, so only\n20\t  CREATURE/PLANESWALKER (plus players) are accepted; this is sufficient for the\n21\t  tests and matches the engine's current type model.\n22\t- **Resolution wiring**: draw goes to `chosen_targets[0]` (the chosen player,\n23\t  which may be the opponent), damage to `chosen_targets[1]` via\n24\t  `engine.game.deal_damage` (handles both player life loss and creature\n25\t  `damage_marked`), and life gain is credited to the controller (untargeted, so\n26\t  it still applies even with no chosen targets).\n27\t- **Defensive**: X<=0 short-circuits before touching targets; missing targets\n28\t  are handled by length checks so resolution never raises.\n29\t\n30\t## Engine changes\n31\tNone. Used existing `engine.game.deal_damage` and `engine.game.draw_card`.\n32\t\n33\t## Spec deviations\n34\tNone.\n35\t\n36\t## Conventions for future cards\n37\t- Converge X = `len(set(self.colors_spent))`; initialize `colors_spent = []` in\n38\t  `__init__` for safe no-op resolution.\n39\t- \"Any target\" filter: player (`hasattr life`) OR\n40\t  `card_types & {CREATURE, PLANESWALKER}` (battle type not present in engine).\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"9f5bdf90-670f-47e5-b82f-45ce66a71a09","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:43:20.810Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n\n## Summary\n`{6}` Sorcery with a converge-driven resolution: target player draws X, the\nspell deals X damage to any target, and the controller gains X life, where X is\nthe number of *distinct* colors of mana spent to cast it.\n\n## Key decisions\n- **Base class**: `Sorcery` (gives `CardType.SORCERY`, no power/toughness, not a\n  `Creature`), satisfying the static-data tests.\n- **X = distinct colors**: `x = len(set(self.colors_spent))`. The engine records\n  colors spent during payment as `colors_spent` (FDN 205 convention); duplicate\n  pips collapse via `set()`, so three red pips yield X=1. Defaults to `[]` in\n  `__init__`, so a missing/empty `colors_spent` makes X=0 and resolution a no-op\n  (covered by the robustness tests).\n- **Targeting**: two `TargetRequirement`s — a \"target player\" (filter\n  `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`) and an \"any target\" (player, creature, or\n  planeswalker). The \"any target\" filter rejects plain non-creature permanents\n  like lands. There is no `CardType.BATTLE` in `engine/types.py`, so only\n  CREATURE/PLANESWALKER (plus players) are accepted; this is sufficient for the\n  tests and matches the engine's current type model.\n- **Resolution wiring**: draw goes to `chosen_targets[0]` (the chosen player,\n  which may be the opponent), damage to `chosen_targets[1]` via\n  `engine.game.deal_damage` (handles both player life loss and creature\n  `damage_marked`), and life gain is credited to the controller (untargeted, so\n  it still applies even with no chosen targets).\n- **Defensive**: X<=0 short-circuits before touching targets; missing targets\n  are handled by length checks so resolution never raises.\n\n## Engine changes\nNone. Used existing `engine.game.deal_damage` and `engine.game.draw_card`.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone.\n\n## Conventions for future cards\n- Converge X = `len(set(self.colors_spent))`; initialize `colors_spent = []` in\n  `__init__` for safe no-op resolution.\n- \"Any target\" filter: player (`hasattr life`) OR\n  `card_types & {CREATURE, PLANESWALKER}` (battle type not present in engine).\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}}}
