{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017X3feNthCCQnxWpA4BvpwN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MbP6u1dRBCoZGCe6H4qj7c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_13 (initial implementation)\n\nCard: **Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares** (`{1}{W}{W}` 3/3 white\nCat Cleric with the new **Prepared** mechanic; prepare-spell face is Swords to\nPlowshares, `{W}` instant).\n\nThe Tester escalated three requirements as untestable because the engine lacks\nsupport. Engine changes are explicitly allowed and expected for new mechanics.\nImplement the FULL card and add the engine support so all three become testable.\n\n## Requirements to implement fully\n1. **ETB trigger**: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1\n   white and black Inkling creature token with flying.\" Use the engine ETB\n   trigger pattern (`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` via `register_triggers`),\n   target a player (default/self OK if no choice), create the token via\n   `engine.game.create_token`.\n2. **Token color**: the Inkling must be observably **white and black**. The\n   engine currently has no first-class color attribute on tokens/cards. Add an\n   observable color representation (additive — e.g. a `colors` set/attribute on\n   the card/token object, populated from mana cost for normal cards and from an\n   explicit color list for tokens). Make `create_token` accept/set the token's\n   colors. Tests must be able to assert the Inkling's colors are white+black.\n3. **Becomes prepared (conditional)**: \"Then if an opponent controls more\n   creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\" Strict `>` comparison;\n   the Emeritus itself counts toward the controller's total. Expose a queryable\n   boolean (e.g. `is_prepared` / a `prepared` flag) that starts False.\n4. **Prepared mechanic** (new keyword): \"While it's prepared, you may cast a\n   copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.\" Implement engine support: when a\n   permanent becomes prepared, the controller may cast a copy of its prepare\n   spell (Swords to Plowshares); casting that copy clears the prepared\n   designation. Expose a testable contract: a way to query that the prepared\n   spell copy exists / is castable while prepared, and that casting it puts the\n   Swords-to-Plowshares effect on the stack and removes the prepared marker.\n5. **Swords to Plowshares effect**: \"Exile target creature. Its controller\n   gains life equal to its power.\" Implement and make it resolvable/testable.\n\n## Make it testable\n- Expose the prepare-spell face (name \"Swords to Plowshares\", cost `{W}`) via a\n  queryable attribute (e.g. `prepare_spell` / `prepared_spell` / `other_face`).\n- Drive the prepared cast loop through the deterministic test pipeline so a test\n  can: become prepared → cast the copy → assert a creature is exiled, its\n  controller gains life = power, and the Emeritus is no longer prepared.\n- Add the `PREPARED` keyword to engine/types.py Keyword enum if appropriate\n  (additive). Do not rename/remove anything existing.\n\nDocument the exact contract you expose in your rationale so the Tester can assert\nagainst it. Do NOT stub these out — the grader's authoritative tests will\nexercise the full Prepared loop, token color, and Swords to Plowshares effect.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2892,"cache_read_input_tokens":46096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2892},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"8fce8f5b-2a71-4a52-b4f6-3c26ab9a7fcf","request_id":"req_011CbcQdWxNPxh