{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5pKJyxa3jN2FfTQgjE6jt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n2\t\n3\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`\n4\t\n5\tCard: `{1}{W}{W}` white **Creature — Cat Cleric**, 3/3, keyword **Prepared**.\n6\tFront-face oracle:\n7\t\n8\t> When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n9\t> Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more\n10\t> creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\n11\t\n12\tThe prepare spell (inset face) is **Swords to Plowshares** (`{W}` instant).\n13\t\n14\t23 tests across five classes. The card is a TDD-red stub, so every test\n15\tcurrently fails (or skips when it depends on an implementation surface that\n16\tdoes not yet exist).\n17\t\n18\t### `TestEmeritusProperties` — static card data\n19\t- `test_is_creature` — front face is a `Creature` with `CardType.CREATURE`.\n20\t- `test_name` — name equals the full split name.\n21\t- `test_mana_cost_is_1ww` — mana cost parses to `{1}{W}{W}`.\n22\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 3/3.\n23\t- `test_is_cat_cleric` — subtypes include both `Cat` and `Cleric`.\n24\t- `test_not_summoning_sick_flag_default` — guards against a constructor that\n25\t  spuriously clears summoning sickness.\n26\t\n27\t### `TestEmeritusPreparedKeyword` — the Prepared mechanic surface\n28\t- `test_prepared_is_advertised` — the Prepared mechanic must be observable\n29\t  somewhere: a `Keyword.PREPARED` flag, an `is_prepared`/`prepared` attribute,\n30\t  or in the rules text. This is tolerant of the implementation's choice of\n31\t  representation (the engine has no `PREPARED` keyword yet) while still\n32\t  forbidding a card that drops the mechanic entirely.\n33\t- `test_starts_unprepared` — if a boolean prepared-designation attribute\n34\t  exists, a freshly constructed card must start `False` (the designation is\n35\t  only gained via the ETB conditional). Skips if no such surface exists.\n36\t\n37\t### `TestEmeritusEtbTriggerRegistration` — \"When this creature enters\"\n38\tThe engine resolves a creature spell by calling `on_resolve` *then* moving it\n39\tto the battlefield, which fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`. So the ETB\n40\tability must be a registered ETB trigger, not done in `on_resolve`.\n41\t- `test_registers_a_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds at least one trigger\n42\t  for this source.\n43\t- `test_trigger_watches_enters_battlefield` — at least one registered trigger\n44\t  watches `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` (or a superclass).\n45\t- `test_trigger_controller_is_card_controller` — the ETB trigger's controller\n46\t  is the card's controller.\n47\t- `test_trigger_fires_for_self_only` — if the trigger has a condition, it\n48\t  fires for this creature's ETB event and not for an unrelated permanent's.\n49\t  Skips if the trigger is unconditional.\n50\t\n51\t### `TestEmeritusEtbCreatesInkling` — ETB token creation\n52\tFires the ETB event and resolves the resulting trigger(s), then inspects the\n53\tbattlefields. A self-targeting choice is pre-scripted on the controller in\n54\tcase the implementation prompts for \"target player\".\n55\t- `test_etb_creates_a_token` — exactly one new creature appears.\n56\t- `test_token_is_named_inkling` — the token is an Inkling (by name or subtype).\n57\t- `test_token_is_one_one` — token base P/T is 1/1.\n58\t- `test_token_has_flying` — token has `Keyword.FLYING`.\n59\t- `test_token_is_a_real_token` — token's `is_token` flag is set (per\n60\t  `engine.game.create_token`).\n61\t- `test_token_goes_to_targeted_player` — \"target player creates ...\" When\n62\t  player 2 is the scripted target, the token enters under player 2's control.\n63\t  This only asserts the controller binding *iff* the implementation consumed\n64\t  the scripted target choice (so controller-default implementations are not\n65\t  unfairly failed here — they're covered by the other token tests).\n66\t\n67\t### `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared` — conditional designation\n68\t\"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes\n69\tprepared.\" The count comparison is strict (\"more than\"). Each scenario sets\n70\tcontroller/opponent creature counts (the Emeritus itself is on the\n71\tcontroller's battlefield and counts), resolves the ETB, and reads the\n72\tprepared flag. All four skip gracefully if no boolean prepared surface exists.\n73\t- `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — opp 3 vs self 1 → prepared.\n74\t- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — self 3 vs opp 3 → NOT prepared\n75\t  (strict `>` edge case).\n76\t- `test_not_prepared_when_controller_has_more` — self 5 vs opp 1 → not prepared.\n77\t- `test_not_prepared_with_no_opponent_creatures` — opp 0 → not prepared.\n78\t\n79\t### `TestEmeritusPrepareSpell` — prepare-spell characteristics\n80\t- `test_prepare_spell_surface_if_present` — if the implementation exposes the\n81\t  inset Swords-to-Plowshares face (via `prepare_spell` / `back_face` /\n82\t  `other_face` / `prepared_spell`), it must be named \"Swords to Plowshares\"\n83\t  with cost `{W}`. Skips if no such surface is exposed (the engine has no\n84\t  split/preparation-card support, so this is optional).\n85\t\n86\t## Edge cases covered\n87\t- Strict \"more than\" comparison (equal counts must NOT prepare).\n88\t- The Emeritus itself counting toward the controller's creature total.\n89\t- No-opponent-creatures case.\n90\t- Self-only ETB trigger condition (unrelated permanents must not trigger it).\n91\t\n92\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (see untestable.json)\n93\t- The token's **color** (\"white and black\"). The engine models no first-class\n94\t  `colors` attribute on cards/tokens, so color is not assertable.\n95\t- The full **Prepared cast loop**: a Swords-to-Plowshares *copy* created in\n96\t  exile that the controller \"may cast\", which \"unprepares\" the permanent. The\n97\t  engine has no preparation-card / split-card / exile-copy-casting support, so\n98\t  the cast-and-unprepare cycle cannot be exercised through real engine APIs.\n99\t- The **Swords to Plowshares effect itself** (\"Exile target creature. Its\n100\t  controller gains life equal to its power.\") — only reachable once the\n101\t  prepare-spell copy can be cast, which is blocked by the above.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjyZjo2bbGXVReCpRizKGz","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"c7af33b5-b770-4fca-b02e-28848dd6ce62","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:48:57.394Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
