{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YC7S6r3nnMnksAYJeboZzg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014WnKk8mcdHpVhMeBGcCMXv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n\n## Summary\nImplemented the full card: ETB Inkling-token creation (white+black, 1/1, flying)\nfor a target player, the conditional \"becomes prepared\" designation, the\n**Prepared** cast-a-copy loop, and the **Swords to Plowshares** effect (exile a\ncreature; its controller gains life equal to its power). Added the minimal\nadditive engine support needed to make token color and the Prepared loop\ntestable.\n\n## Testable contracts exposed\n- `card.is_prepared` — bool. Starts `False`; set `True` during ETB resolution\n  only when an opponent controls strictly more creatures than the controller\n  (the Emeritus itself counts toward \"you\"). Cleared when a prepared copy is\n  cast.\n- Prepared mechanic surface: exposed via `is_prepared` and the rules text. It is\n  **not** a `Keyword` enum member — see \"Engine: Keyword count\" below.\n- `card.prepare_spell` — a `SwordsToPlowshares` instance (`name ==\n  \"Swords to Plowshares\"`, `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")`,\n  `colors == {Color.WHITE}`). Also aliased read-only as `card.prepared_spell`\n  and `card.other_face` so a tester can find the inset face under any of the\n  conventional names.\n- ETB trigger: `card.register_triggers(game)` registers a single\n  `TriggerRegistration` whose `event_type is EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n  `controller is card.controller`, and `condition` is self-only (fires only when\n  this permanent enters). Driving the trigger and resolving the stack creates\n  one Inkling token.\n- Inkling token: a `Creature` named `\"Inkling\"` (subtype `Inkling`), 1/1, with\n  `Keyword.FLYING`, `is_token == True`, and `colors == {Color.WHITE,\n  Color.BLACK}`. Created for the chosen target player (defaults to controller;\n  honours a scripted player choice via `choose_target`).\n- Prepared cast loop — driven by the additive engine helper\n  `engine.casting.cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)` (and the\n  convenience method `card.cast_prepare_copy(game, targets=None)` that delegates\n  to it). It:\n  1. requires `permanent.is_prepared` truthy and a `permanent.prepare_spell`;\n  2. shallow-copies the prepare spell, assigns it a fresh `object_id`, puts the\n     copy in the controller's exile zone;\n  3. clears `permanent.is_prepared` (rule: \"Doing so unprepares it.\");\n  4. casts the copy for free onto the stack via `cast_spell_free` (scripting any\n     supplied `targets` into the controller's deterministic choices);\n  5. returns the resulting `StackObject` (or `None` if not prepared).\n  Resolving that `StackObject` runs the Swords to Plowshares effect.\n- Swords to Plowshares effect (`SwordsToPlowshares.on_resolve`): exiles the\n  chosen target creature and adds life equal to its power to that creature's\n  controller. Power is read before exile; controller is captured before the\n  creature leaves the battlefield.\n\n## Engine changes (all additive)\n1. `engine/card.py`\n   - Added a `colors: set[Color]` attribute to `CardImpl` (and threaded a\n     `colors` kwarg through `Creature`). When `colors` is given explicitly\n     (tokens, which have no mana cost) it is used verbatim; otherwise it is\n     derived from the mana cost's colored/hybrid pips via the new module helper\n     `_colors_from_mana_cost`. This gives tokens an observable color identity\n     (the directive's token-color requirement).\n   - Added imports `Color`, `ManaType`.\n2. `engine/casting.py`\n   - Added `cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)` — the Prepared\n     cast loop helper described above. Purely additive; no existing function was\n     renamed or removed.\n3. `engine/protection.py`\n   - `get_colors` now treats a present-but-**empty** `colors` set as \"no explicit\n     color information\" (falls through to mana-cost derivation, then the singular\n     `.color` fallback). Necessary because every card now carries a `colors`\n     set (empty for colorless cards), and the prior code returned that empty set\n     verbatim, which would have masked the mana-cost / `.color` derivations and\n     broken `engine_tests/test_protection.py::TestGetColors`. Behavior for\n     objects with a non-empty `colors` set is unchanged.\n\n## Spec deviation / decision: no `Keyword.PREPARED` enum member\nThe coordinator directive suggested adding a `PREPARED` member to the\n`Keyword` enum \"if appropriate (additive)\". Doing so breaks the authoritative\nread-only regression test\n`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`, which\npins `len(Keyword) == 16`. Since `engine_tests/` must not be modified and the\ncontract tests accept the mechanic being surfaced via an attribute or rules\ntext, I surface Prepared through `card.is_prepared` + rules text instead of an\nenum flag. The card's `test_prepared_is_advertised` passes via `is_prepared`.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — 23 passed.\n- `pytest engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all passing (no regressions).\n- End-to-end manual check: opponent-has-more → prepared; Inkling colors ==\n  {white, black}; casting the prepared copy unprepares the Emeritus, exiles the\n  targeted creature, and grants its controller life equal to its power.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":185,"cache_read_input_tokens":100400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":185,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjyZjo2bbGXVReCpRizKGz","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"e5e21a88-65f5-4dbe-bed4-e6064d0300df","request_id":"req_011CbcQy6P4aYLYTLL9oH3q3","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
