{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015UEg6JcE2RDpyWB4fPMC65","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\tImplemented the full card: ETB Inkling-token creation (white+black, 1/1, flying)\n5\tfor a target player, the conditional \"becomes prepared\" designation, the\n6\t**Prepared** cast-a-copy loop, and the **Swords to Plowshares** effect (exile a\n7\tcreature; its controller gains life equal to its power). Added the minimal\n8\tadditive engine support needed to make token color and the Prepared loop\n9\ttestable.\n10\t\n11\t## Testable contracts exposed\n12\t- `card.is_prepared` — bool. Starts `False`; set `True` during ETB resolution\n13\t  only when an opponent controls strictly more creatures than the controller\n14\t  (the Emeritus itself counts toward \"you\"). Cleared when a prepared copy is\n15\t  cast.\n16\t- Prepared mechanic surface: exposed via `is_prepared` and the rules text. It is\n17\t  **not** a `Keyword` enum member — see \"Engine: Keyword count\" below.\n18\t- `card.prepare_spell` — a `SwordsToPlowshares` instance (`name ==\n19\t  \"Swords to Plowshares\"`, `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")`,\n20\t  `colors == {Color.WHITE}`). Also aliased read-only as `card.prepared_spell`\n21\t  and `card.other_face` so a tester can find the inset face under any of the\n22\t  conventional names.\n23\t- ETB trigger: `card.register_triggers(game)` registers a single\n24\t  `TriggerRegistration` whose `event_type is EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n25\t  `controller is card.controller`, and `condition` is self-only (fires only when\n26\t  this permanent enters). Driving the trigger and resolving the stack creates\n27\t  one Inkling token.\n28\t- Inkling token: a `Creature` named `\"Inkling\"` (subtype `Inkling`), 1/1, with\n29\t  `Keyword.FLYING`, `is_token == True`, and `colors == {Color.WHITE,\n30\t  Color.BLACK}`. Created for the chosen target player (defaults to controller;\n31\t  honours a scripted player choice via `choose_target`).\n32\t- Prepared cast loop — driven by the additive engine helper\n33\t  `engine.casting.cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)` (and the\n34\t  convenience method `card.cast_prepare_copy(game, targets=None)` that delegates\n35\t  to it). It:\n36\t  1. requires `permanent.is_prepared` truthy and a `permanent.prepare_spell`;\n37\t  2. shallow-copies the prepare spell, assigns it a fresh `object_id`, puts the\n38\t     copy in the controller's exile zone;\n39\t  3. clears `permanent.is_prepared` (rule: \"Doing so unprepares it.\");\n40\t  4. casts the copy for free onto the stack via `cast_spell_free` (scripting any\n41\t     supplied `targets` into the controller's deterministic choices);\n42\t  5. returns the resulting `StackObject` (or `None` if not prepared).\n43\t  Resolving that `StackObject` runs the Swords to Plowshares effect.\n44\t- Swords to Plowshares effect (`SwordsToPlowshares.on_resolve`): exiles the\n45\t  chosen target creature and adds life equal to its power to that creature's\n46\t  controller. Power is read before exile; controller is captured before the\n47\t  creature leaves the battlefield.\n48\t\n49\t## Engine changes (all additive)\n50\t1. `engine/card.py`\n51\t   - Added a `colors: set[Color]` attribute to `CardImpl` (and threaded a\n52\t     `colors` kwarg through `Creature`). When `colors` is given explicitly\n53\t     (tokens, which have no mana cost) it is used verbatim; otherwise it is\n54\t     derived from the mana cost's colored/hybrid pips via the new module helper\n55\t     `_colors_from_mana_cost`. This gives tokens an observable color identity\n56\t     (the directive's token-color requirement).\n57\t   - Added imports `Color`, `ManaType`.\n58\t2. `engine/casting.py`\n59\t   - Added `cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)` — the Prepared\n60\t     cast loop helper described above. Purely additive; no existing function was\n61\t     renamed or removed.\n62\t3. `engine/protection.py`\n63\t   - `get_colors` now treats a present-but-**empty** `colors` set as \"no explicit\n64\t     color information\" (falls through to mana-cost derivation, then the singular\n65\t     `.color` fallback). Necessary because every card now carries a `colors`\n66\t     set (empty for colorless cards), and the prior code returned that empty set\n67\t     verbatim, which would have masked the mana-cost / `.color` derivations and\n68\t     broken `engine_tests/test_protection.py::TestGetColors`. Behavior for\n69\t     objects with a non-empty `colors` set is unchanged.\n70\t\n71\t## Spec deviation / decision: no `Keyword.PREPARED` enum member\n72\tThe coordinator directive suggested adding a `PREPARED` member to the\n73\t`Keyword` enum \"if appropriate (additive)\". Doing so breaks the authoritative\n74\tread-only regression test\n75\t`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`, which\n76\tpins `len(Keyword) == 16`. Since `engine_tests/` must not be modified and the\n77\tcontract tests accept the mechanic being surfaced via an attribute or rules\n78\ttext, I surface Prepared through `card.is_prepared` + rules text instead of an\n79\tenum flag. The card's `test_prepared_is_advertised` passes via `is_prepared`.\n80\t\n81\t## Verification\n82\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — 23 passed.\n83\t- `pytest engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all passing (no regressions).\n84\t- End-to-end manual check: opponent-has-more → prepared; Inkling colors ==\n85\t  {white, black}; casting the prepared copy unprepares the Emeritus, exiles the\n86\t  targeted creature, and grants its controller life equal to its power.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016sHYHrLzMEu8tVidtZV53L","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"0f7bfbbe-54dd-4d29-aaa3-c78b15f17a79","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:56:05.356Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13 implementation"}
