{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014zpsCQYfgC8aGU6mjr6gci","type":"tool_result","content":"38\t\n39\tdef get_colors(obj: Any) -> set[Color]:\n40\t    \"\"\"Return the set of colours of *obj*.\n41\t\n42\t    Colour is determined by:\n43\t    1. An explicit ``colors`` attribute (set or list of :class:`Color`).\n44\t    2. The coloured pips in the object's ``mana_cost``.\n45\t    3. An explicit ``color`` attribute (single :class:`Color`).\n46\t\n47\t    Colourless objects return an empty set.\n48\t    \"\"\"\n49\t    # Explicit colors attribute (takes precedence). A present-but-empty set is\n50\t    # treated as \"no explicit color information\" so that derivation from the\n51\t    # mana cost or a singular ``color`` attribute can still apply (cards now\n52\t    # always carry a ``colors`` set, defaulting to empty for colorless cards).\n53\t    if hasattr(obj, \"colors\") and obj.colors:\n54\t        return set(obj.colors)\n55\t\n56\t    # Derive from mana cost pips\n57\t    mana_cost = getattr(obj, \"mana_cost\", None)\n58\t    if mana_cost is not None:\n59\t        pips = getattr(mana_cost, \"pips\", None)\n60\t        if pips:\n61\t            result: set[Color] = set()\n62\t            for mt in pips:\n63\t                if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n64\t                    result.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n65\t            return result\n66\t\n67\t    # Single color attribute fallback\n68\t    if hasattr(obj, \"color\") and obj.color is not None:\n69\t        return {obj.color}\n70\t\n71\t    return set()\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n75\t# ProtectionAbility\n76\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n77\t\n78\t@dataclass\n79\tclass ProtectionAbility:\n80\t    \"\"\"Represents a 'protection from [quality]' ability.\n81\t\n82\t    The *quality* is typically a :class:`Color`, but the framework supports\n83\t    arbitrary predicates via *predicate*.\n84\t\n85\t    Usage::\n86\t\n87\t        # Colour-based protection"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016sHYHrLzMEu8tVidtZV53L","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"4a7df075-2597-4fe4-ae9d-aaa396104d63","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:56:40.991Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13 implementation"}
