{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Hijj5kaVVfgwZxUHohy1JF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019J9oYPsCRhVhygNudsLPye","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json","content":"[\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"engine/casting.py\", \"line\": 430, \"comment\": \"cast_prepared_spell casts the copy as a real Instant via cast_spell_free; on resolution _resolve_spell moves a non-permanent STACK->GRAVEYARD (engine/casting.py:408-414). A spell copy should cease to exist rather than land in the controller's graveyard (CR 707.10/111.7). This leaves a phantom 'Swords to Plowshares' card in the controller's graveyard which the player never owned, and could be re-cast/found by graveyard effects. Not exercised by current tests and the engine has no 'copy ceases to exist' hook, so accepted as a limitation, but worth a TODO. Consider exiling/discarding the copy after resolution, or skipping the graveyard move for objects flagged as copies.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"engine/protection.py\", \"line\": 53, \"comment\": \"Changing the guard from 'obj.colors is not None' to a truthiness check ('if obj.colors') means a deliberately colorless object that still carries a colored mana_cost (e.g. a devoid-style card) would now derive color from its pips instead of being treated as colorless. For an explicitly-colorless card the empty set used to be authoritative; now it falls through. This is benign for the cards in this run (and is needed to keep engine_tests/test_protection.py green), but the precedence semantics changed: an explicit empty colors set no longer asserts 'colorless'. If a future card needs to be explicitly colorless despite a colored cost, get_colors will mis-report it.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 84, \"comment\": \"SwordsToPlowshares.get_targets returns a TargetRequirement that filters CardType.CREATURE in Zone.BATTLEFIELD but does not constrain controller/opponent (correct — StP targets any creature). However the filter_fn _is_creature does not guard against the chosen object being None or a non-card (e.g. a scripted player). cast_spell_free validates filter_fn only when target is not None, so a None scripted answer would pass through and on_resolve early-returns harmlessly; acceptable, but consider asserting the target is on the battlefield to fail fast on bad scripts.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 143, \"comment\": \"prepare_spell is constructed once in __init__ with owner/controller snapshotted at construction time. If the Emeritus changes controller before the prepared copy is cast, cast_prepared_spell re-derives controller from the permanent (good) and copies the face, so this is fine — but the original prepare_spell's stored controller/owner can go stale. Harmless since only the copy is ever cast, noting for clarity.\"}\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":38293,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016sHYHrLzMEu8tVidtZV53L","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"265a0805-ec16-419e-bedc-58d4e7c50a5e","request_id":"req_011CbcRLmvfdEwzJfJCBJ8h5","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13 implementation"}
