{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqavbJkpmSnKxeDm436RWr","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/types.py:239:class TargetRequirement:\nengine/types.py:240:    \"\"\"Describes a targeting requirement for a spell or ability.\nengine/casting.py:202:                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\nengine/casting.py:342:        # Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this spell\nengine/casting.py:348:                    f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\nengine/casting.py:580:    # Script the explicit targets so cast_spell_free's target choices resolve.\nengine/card.py:370:    def counters(self) -> dict[str, int]:\nengine/stack.py:15:class StackObject:\nengine/stack.py:21:        targets: The chosen targets for the spell/ability.\nengine/stack.py:33:class Stack:\nengine/stack.py:43:    def push(self, obj: StackObject) -> None:\nengine/stack.py:47:    def pop(self) -> StackObject:\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:11:| `types.py` | 250+ | **Foundation** — All enums (`Color`, `ManaType`, `Zone`, `Phase`, `Step`, `CardType`, `Supertype`, `Keyword`) and core dataclasses (`ManaCost` with `.parse()` and `.cmc`, `HybridManaSymbol`, `TargetRequirement` with lazy `filter_fn` convention). `ManaCost.parse()` handles `{X/Y}` hybrid mana tokens. Zero internal dependencies. |\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:18:[Omitted long matching line]\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:40:- **`TargetRequirement.filter_fn`** — Lazy filter evaluated at cast time (not snapshot-at-definition-time); enables dynamic target validation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015SHGWHNJVkcYKhc7mafbPZ","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"35698607-a051-4a4d-81fc-c91c609a385c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:58:52.490Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_57"}
