spent figure can be read at resolution and asserted by\n   tests.\n2. **Beginning-of-main-phase trigger.** Add a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n   (mirror the existing `BeginningOfUpkeep` event/firing pattern) and fire it at\n   the start of the controller's main phase during the turn loop /\n   `advance_phase()`. This is the firing site for the delayed {C} mana. Be careful\n   not to break existing engine tests — match the existing event/trigger\n   conventions and only ADD a firing site.\n\n## Make it testable\n- Implement the delayed effect as a registered trigger keyed to\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` for the controller, adding {C} mana = the\n  recorded mana spent on the countered spell.\n- Expose enough surface that a test can: counter a spell (incl. an X / cost-\n  reduced spell to prove it's actual mana spent, not CMC), advance to the\n  controller's next main phase, and assert the correct {C} appears in the pool.\n- Document the exact contracts (attribute names, event name) in your rationale.\n\nDo NOT stub these out — the grader's authoritative tests will exercise the full\nmana-spent tracking and the begin-of-main-phase delayed payoff.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QwnaH2XyCsCUYGR17oWvhg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T1i5yjUj1dNMiLhPHXtv3e","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement sos_57","subagent_type":"Implementer","prompt":"You are implementing a Magic: The Gathering card with new engine support (TDD green phase).\n\nCARD: sos_57 — Mana Sculpt ({1}{U}{U} Instant)\n- Spec: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_spec.json\n- Implementation file you complete: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\n- Test file (already written — you MUST NOT modify it): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\n- Test rationale: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md\n\nCOORDINATOR DIRECTIVES (read and follow): /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/coordinator-directives.md\nThe Tester escalated two requirements as untestable due to missing engine support: tracking the TOTAL mana spent to cast a spell, and a beginning-of-main-phase trigger. You must implement the FULL card plus the additive engine support and expose testable contracts. After you finish, the Tester will be re-invoked.\n\nREFERENCES (read for API discovery — rich docstrings):\n- engine/card.py, engine/events.py, engine/triggers.py, engine/zones.py, engine/casting.py, engine/turn.py (BeginningOfUpkeep firing pattern), engine/mana.py / ManaPool (last_payment_colors), engine/game.py\n- FDN reference implementations: cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py — find counterspells and delayed/trigger effects.\n- /workspace/AGENTS.md, /workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md, /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md, /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json\n- RULEBOOK.txt (grep, don't read whole) for counter / mana spent / phases.\n\nENGINE RULES (from AGENTS.md):\n- You MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files in engine/, modify bodies of existing engine functions, and add new event/trigger classes.\n- You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in engine/.\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file. Note engine_tests/test_types.py pins certain counts (e.g. Keyword count = 16) — do not change enums that would break pinned counts.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Read the spec, test file, rationale, and directives.\n2. Implement the card so ALL tests in tests.py pass, plus the full mana-spent tracking and begin-of-main-phase delayed payoff with testable contracts.\n3. Make additive engine changes. Be careful firing a new begin-of-main-phase event does not break existing engine tests.\n4. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, and `pytest cards/fdn/` to confirm nothing breaks.\n5. If a test is genuinely WRONG, do NOT modify it — return DISPUTE with details.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Implementation to /workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py (+ engine changes).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl.diff — `git diff` of all changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md — what you did, the exact testable contracts (mana-spent attribute name, event name, how to drive to next main phase), engine changes, any spec deviations.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-files.txt — modified files.\n- Upsert this card's entry into /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json (match by card: \"sos_57\"). Keep other entries intact.\n\nReturn either IMPL_DONE (files_changed, tests_passing, diff_path, rationale_path, notes) or DISPUTE (tests_failing, disputed_tests, dispute_path, notes) exactly as specified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1395,"cache_read_input_tokens":61576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1395},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"82da684b-6db7-4940-8822-096e176e853b","request_id":"req_011CbcRjQK3ocMee5vXMbUKc"}
