{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CmbBJoT9FRsM7DrsY3aEXw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant (blue).\n4\tOracle: *\"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\n5\tequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\n6\tnext main phase.\"*\n7\t\n8\tTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` (20 tests).\n9\t\n10\t## Engine surface findings\n11\t\n12\t- The engine ships **no built-in counter mechanism**, **no per-spell mana-spent\n13\t  tracking** (`ManaPool` only exposes `last_payment_colors`), and **no\n14\t  beginning-of-main-phase trigger event** (`advance_phase()` fires nothing;\n15\t  only `BeginningOfUpkeep` is fired in `turn.py`). The implementation must\n16\t  provide the counter and the delayed conditional mana itself.\n17\t- Tests therefore drive the observable contract: stack/zone movement for the\n18\t  counter, and the presence/absence + colorless amount of a delayed effect\n19\t  (a registered trigger) keyed on Wizard control. The precise \"mana spent vs\n20\t  mana value\" and \"fires at next main phase via natural progression\" pieces are\n21\t  recorded in `untestable.json`.\n22\t\n23\t## Test cases\n24\t\n25\t### TestManaSculptProperties — static card data\n26\t- `test_name` — name is \"Mana Sculpt\".\n27\t- `test_is_instant` — subclass of `Instant`, `INSTANT` in `card_types`.\n28\t- `test_mana_cost` — cost equals `{1}{U}{U}`.\n29\t- `test_is_blue` — `Color.BLUE` in `card.colors` (per KEY_DECISIONS colors attr).\n30\t- `test_not_a_creature` — `CREATURE` not in card_types. (Benign guardrail;\n31\t  passes against the stub but pins a real contract.)\n32\t\n33\t### TestManaSculptTargeting — \"Counter target spell\"\n34\t- `test_returns_one_target_requirement` — `get_targets` returns exactly one\n35\t  `TargetRequirement`.\n36\t- `test_target_requirement_uses_stack_zone` — the requirement's `zone` is\n37\t  `Zone.STACK` (spells live on the stack).\n38\t- `test_filter_accepts_an_instant_spell` / `test_filter_accepts_a_sorcery_spell`\n39\t  — the target filter accepts instant and sorcery spells.\n40\t- `test_filter_rejects_a_player` — \"target spell\" is not \"any target\"; players\n41\t  are illegal targets.\n42\t\n43\t### TestManaSculptCounter — counter resolution\n44\t- `test_targeted_spell_leaves_the_stack` — after `on_resolve`, the victim's\n45\t  StackObject is gone and its card has left the caster's STACK zone.\n46\t- `test_countered_spell_goes_to_owners_graveyard` — the countered spell is put\n47\t  into its **owner's** graveyard (the victim's owner, not Mana Sculpt's).\n48\t- `test_countered_spell_does_not_resolve` — the victim's StackObject is removed\n49\t  (so its resolve callback can never fire) and it never reached the\n50\t  battlefield.\n51\t- `test_no_target_resolution_is_safe_noop` — with no chosen target, resolution\n52\t  does not raise and leaves the stack untouched. (Defensive; passes against the\n53\t  stub but guards against crashes once implemented.)\n54\t\n55\t### TestManaSculptWizardConditional — \"If you control a Wizard\"\n56\t- `test_no_wizard_sets_up_no_delayed_mana_effect` — controlling only a\n57\t  non-Wizard creature: resolution registers **no** new trigger, but the counter\n58\t  still happens.\n59\t- `test_wizard_control_sets_up_a_delayed_mana_effect` — controlling a Wizard:\n60\t  resolution registers exactly one new trigger (the delayed mana payoff).\n61\t- `test_delayed_effect_controlled_by_mana_sculpt_caster` — the delayed effect is\n62\t  controlled by Mana Sculpt's controller (the player who gets the {C}).\n63\t\n64\t### TestManaSculptManaPayoff — colorless mana amount\n65\tDrive the delayed effect by running its registered trigger effect directly and\n66\tobserve the controller's mana pool:\n67\t- `test_payoff_adds_colorless_equal_to_mana_spent` — countering a 3-mana spell\n68\t  adds 3 `{C}`.\n69\t- `test_payoff_amount_scales_with_spell_cost` — countering a 1-mana spell adds\n70\t  only 1 `{C}`.\n71\t- `test_payoff_mana_is_colorless_not_colored` — the added mana is `{C}` only; no\n72\t  colored mana is produced.\n73\t\n74\t## Edge cases covered\n75\t- No-Wizard vs Wizard branch (the static conditional).\n76\t- Owner's (not caster's) graveyard destination for the countered spell.\n77\t- Colorless-only payoff; amount scales with the countered spell's cost.\n78\t- No-target safety (no crash, no stack mutation).\n79\t\n80\t## Edge cases NOT covered (see untestable.json)\n81\t- **Actual mana spent ≠ mana value** (X spells, additional costs, cost\n82\t  reduction): the engine does not track per-spell mana spent, so amount tests\n83\t  use fixed-cost spells where spent == CMC.\n84\t- **Natural firing at \"next main phase\"**: no begin-of-main-phase trigger event\n85\t  exists in the engine, so the payoff is exercised via the trigger's effect\n86\t  callback rather than through phase progression.\n87\t\n88\t## Out of scope\n89\t- The opponent's ability to respond to Mana Sculpt itself, full priority loops,\n90\t  and split second / can't-be-countered interactions — not implied by this\n91\t  card's text and not part of its local contract.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T1i5yjUj1dNMiLhPHXtv3e","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"abb2aed6-2f83-4b7a-b6a8-e07f91325d59","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:03:03.031Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57"}
