{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019m6uRds6cjMLev2fdr2KR8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you\n4\tcontrol a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to\n5\tcast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n6\t\n7\tAll 20 tests in `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` pass, plus `engine_tests/` (no\n8\tregressions) and `cards/fdn/` (no regressions).\n9\t\n10\t## Card behavior\n11\t\n12\t`ManaSculpt(Instant)` in `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`:\n13\t\n14\t- **Static data** — name, `{1}{U}{U}` cost, INSTANT type, blue (derived from\n15\t  cost pips by the existing `_colors_from_mana_cost`).\n16\t- **get_targets** — returns exactly one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK,\n17\t  description=\"target spell\")`. The `filter_fn` (`_is_spell`) accepts objects\n18\t  carrying spell `card_types` (instant/sorcery/permanent spells) and rejects\n19\t  players (anything with a `life` attribute) — \"target spell\" is not \"any\n20\t  target\".\n21\t- **on_resolve** — reads the first `chosen_targets` entry (set by the engine\n22\t  resolve pipeline or by tests). Empty/None target is a safe no-op. Otherwise:\n23\t  1. Captures the mana-spent amount BEFORE the spell leaves the stack.\n24\t  2. Counters: finds the `StackObject` on `game.stack` whose `source` is the\n25\t     target card, removes it from the stack, removes the card from its STACK\n26\t     zone, and places it in the **owner's** graveyard. Removing the\n27\t     StackObject means its `on_resolve` can never fire (the spell doesn't\n28\t     resolve).\n29\t  3. Wizard conditional: only if the controller controls a creature with\n30\t     `\"Wizard\"` in `subtypes` does it register the delayed payoff.\n31\t\n32\t## Testable contracts (for the re-invoked Tester)\n33\t\n34\t- **Mana-spent attribute:** `spell.mana_spent` (int). Set in\n35\t  `engine/casting.cast_spell` from the new `ManaPool.last_payment_total`\n36\t  immediately after payment. This is the TOTAL mana paid (colored +\n37\t  colorless), so it diverges from printed mana value for X / cost-reduced\n38\t  spells. `ManaSculpt` reads it via `_mana_spent_on(spell)`, falling back to\n39\t  `spell.mana_cost.cmc` when the spell was placed on the stack directly\n40\t  (tests do this), which is why the amount tests see CMC = mana spent.\n41\t- **Mana-pool accessor:** `ManaPool.last_payment_total` (read-only property).\n42\t- **Begin-of-main-phase event:** `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n43\t  with fields `player` (active player) and `phase` (the `Phase` value). Fired\n44\t  in `engine/turn.run_turn` at the start of `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` and\n45\t  `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (when `game.step is None`), mirroring the existing\n46\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` firing pattern.\n47\t- **Delayed effect surface:** registered as a `TriggerRegistration` with\n48\t  `source=<the ManaSculpt instance>`, `controller=<caster>`,\n49\t  `event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`. Discoverable via\n50\t  `game.trigger_manager.get_triggers_for_source(sculpt)` and\n51\t  `game.trigger_manager.get_triggers()`. Its `.effect(game)` adds\n52\t  `ManaType.COLORLESS` equal to the recorded mana spent to the caster's pool.\n53\t  The condition fires only for the controller's main phase; the effect is\n54\t  one-shot (sets an internal flag and unregisters itself after firing) so it\n55\t  pays out exactly once at the next main phase.\n56\t- **Driving to next main phase naturally:** advance the turn loop; at the\n57\t  controller's `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` the engine fires\n58\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller)`, the registered\n59\t  trigger's condition matches, and the effect runs.\n60\t\n61\t## Engine changes (additive only)\n62\t\n63\t- `engine/mana.py` — added `_last_payment_total` field, the\n64\t  `last_payment_total` property, and updated `pay()` to accumulate total mana\n65\t  deducted (alongside the existing `last_payment_colors` computation). No\n66\t  existing behavior changed.\n67\t- `engine/casting.py` — `cast_spell` now also records\n68\t  `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total` after payment\n69\t  (additive; sits next to the existing `colors_spent` assignment).\n70\t- `engine/events.py` — added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` dataclass.\n71\t- `engine/turn.py` — added a firing site in `run_turn` for the new event at\n72\t  the start of either main phase. Only an ADD; the existing upkeep/draw/combat\n73\t  branches are untouched, so existing engine tests still pass.\n74\t\n75\t## Spec deviations\n76\t\n77\tNone material. The \"amount of mana spent\" is faithfully implemented via\n78\t`last_payment_total`/`mana_spent`; tests that don't cast through the payment\n79\tpipeline fall back to CMC, which equals mana spent for their fixed-cost\n80\tspells.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"4ab11fd5-2008-445d-b242-850326e52249","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:06:02.688Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n\nCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you\ncontrol a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to\ncast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n\nAll 20 tests in `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` pass, plus `engine_tests/` (no\nregressions) and `cards/fdn/` (no regressions).\n\n## Card behavior\n\n`ManaSculpt(Instant)` in `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`:\n\n- **Static data** — name, `{1}{U}{U}` cost, INSTANT type, blue (derived from\n  cost pips by the existing `_colors_from_mana_cost`).\n- **get_targets** — returns exactly one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK,\n  description=\"target spell\")`. The `filter_fn` (`_is_spell`) accepts objects\n  carrying spell `card_types` (instant/sorcery/permanent spells) and rejects\n  players (anything with a `life` attribute) — \"target spell\" is not \"any\n  target\".\n- **on_resolve** — reads the first `chosen_targets` entry (set by the engine\n  resolve pipeline or by tests). Empty/None target is a safe no-op. Otherwise:\n  1. Captures the mana-spent amount BEFORE the spell leaves the stack.\n  2. Counters: finds the `StackObject` on `game.stack` whose `source` is the\n     target card, removes it from the stack, removes the card from its STACK\n     zone, and places it in the **owner's** graveyard. Removing the\n     StackObject means its `on_resolve` can never fire (the spell doesn't\n     resolve).\n  3. Wizard conditional: only if the controller controls a creature with\n     `\"Wizard\"` in `subtypes` does it register the delayed payoff.\n\n## Testable contracts (for the re-invoked Tester)\n\n- **Mana-spent attribute:** `spell.mana_spent` (int). Set in\n  `engine/casting.cast_spell` from the new `ManaPool.last_payment_total`\n  immediately after payment. This is the TOTAL mana paid (colored +\n  colorless), so it diverges from printed mana value for X / cost-reduced\n  spells. `ManaSculpt` reads it via `_mana_spent_on(spell)`, falling back to\n  `spell.mana_cost.cmc` when the spell was placed on the stack directly\n  (tests do this), which is why the amount tests see CMC = mana spent.\n- **Mana-pool accessor:** `ManaPool.last_payment_total` (read-only property).\n- **Begin-of-main-phase event:** `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n  with fields `player` (active player) and `phase` (the `Phase` value). Fired\n  in `engine/turn.run_turn` at the start of `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` and\n  `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (when `game.step is None`), mirroring the existing\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` firing pattern.\n- **Delayed effect surface:** registered as a `TriggerRegistration` with\n  `source=<the ManaSculpt instance>`, `controller=<caster>`,\n  `event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`. Discoverable via\n  `game.trigger_manager.get_triggers_for_source(sculpt)` and\n  `game.trigger_manager.get_triggers()`. Its `.effect(game)` adds\n  `ManaType.COLORLESS` equal to the recorded mana spent to the caster's pool.\n  The condition fires only for the controller's main phase; the effect is\n  one-shot (sets an internal flag and unregisters itself after firing) so it\n  pays out exactly once at the next main phase.\n- **Driving to next main phase naturally:** advance the turn loop; at the\n  controller's `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` the engine fires\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller)`, the registered\n  trigger's condition matches, and the effect runs.\n\n## Engine changes (additive only)\n\n- `engine/mana.py` — added `_last_payment_total` field, the\n  `last_payment_total` property, and updated `pay()` to accumulate total mana\n  deducted (alongside the existing `last_payment_colors` computation). No\n  existing behavior changed.\n- `engine/casting.py` — `cast_spell` now also records\n  `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total` after payment\n  (additive; sits next to the existing `colors_spent` assignment).\n- `engine/events.py` — added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` dataclass.\n- `engine/turn.py` — added a firing site in `run_turn` for the new event at\n  the start of either main phase. Only an ADD; the existing upkeep/draw/combat\n  branches are untouched, so existing engine tests still pass.\n\n## Spec deviations\n\nNone material. The \"amount of mana spent\" is faithfully implemented via\n`last_payment_total`/`mana_spent`; tests that don't cast through the payment\npipeline fall back to CMC, which equals mana spent for their fixed-cost\nspells.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
