{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MAdWP47KxuQj34FTm4SQfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Lo13eLBUbEdwg2J2hVdra","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Out of scope\n- The opponent's ability to respond to Mana Sculpt itself, full priority loops,\n  and split second / can't-be-countered interactions — not implied by this\n  card's text and not part of its local contract.","new_string":"## Out of scope\n- The opponent's ability to respond to Mana Sculpt itself, full priority loops,\n  and split second / can't-be-countered interactions — not implied by this\n  card's text and not part of its local contract.\n\n## Re-invocation coverage (engine support now exists)\n\nThe Implementer added `spell.mana_spent` (set in `engine/casting.cast_spell`\nfrom `ManaPool.last_payment_total`) and\n`engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fired in\n`engine/turn.run_turn` at each main phase). The two previously-untestable\nrequirements are now covered end-to-end (file grew from 20 → 27 tests).\n\n### TestManaSpentTrackingPipeline — \"amount of mana spent\" (rule 107.7)\nCasts a `_CostReducedSpell` ({4} that reduces generic by {2}) through the REAL\npayment pipeline (`engine.casting.cast_spell` with a stocked mana pool), so the\nactual mana paid (2) diverges from the printed mana value / CMC (4).\n- `test_cost_reduced_spell_records_actual_mana_spent` — after casting, the\n  spell's `mana_spent` is 2 while `mana_cost.cmc` is 4. Pins that the engine\n  records actual mana paid, not CMC.\n- `test_counter_payoff_equals_actual_mana_spent_not_cmc` — countering that\n  cost-reduced spell with Mana Sculpt (Wizard controlled) pays {C} equal to\n  the mana SPENT (2), not the printed mana value (4). This is the divergence\n  case the original `untestable.json` flagged.\n\n### TestManaSculptNaturalPayoff — \"at the beginning of your next main phase\"\nDrives the payoff through the real begin-of-main-phase firing path\n(`trigger_manager.fire_event(BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(...))`, mirroring\n`run_turn`'s firing site) rather than calling the effect directly.\n- `test_payoff_fires_at_controllers_next_main_phase` — with a Wizard, firing\n  the controller's begin-of-main-phase event adds 3 {C} to their pool (no {C}\n  before the event fires).\n- `test_payoff_does_not_fire_on_opponents_main_phase` — the trigger is keyed to\n  the controller; firing the OPPONENT's main phase event pays nothing.\n- `test_payoff_is_one_shot` — after firing once the delayed trigger unregisters\n  (`get_triggers_for_source` empty), and a second main phase adds no more mana.\n- `test_no_wizard_means_no_payoff_at_main_phase` — no Wizard ⇒ no trigger\n  registered ⇒ controller's next main phase produces no {C} (counter still\n  happens).\n- `test_payoff_via_full_turn_loop` — end-to-end: runs the real `engine.turn.run_turn`\n  (both players scripted to pass) so the ENGINE itself fires the begin-of-main-phase\n  event during the controller's precombat main phase; a spy on the controller's\n  `mana_pool.add` captures 3 {C} granted at the main phase, and the one-shot\n  trigger removes itself afterward. (Mana pools empty on phase transitions, so\n  the spy captures the value at the moment it is granted.)\n\nBoth items from `untestable.json` are now fully covered; that file is now empty."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":73489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":321,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0144yyhQJidrLDrPv1Gwwc7v","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"01cd595c-ebdf-4a5c-9293-1e12f5126b