{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YX96JwUDnYdbiNK5bRA6Ni","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 2\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json\n\nSummary of what I verified (all correct):\n- `engine/mana.py` `last_payment_total` accumulation is purely additive; the existing `last_payment_colors` computation is unchanged (the `if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR` branch still runs identically).\n- `engine/casting.py` sets `card.mana_spent` after payment alongside `colors_spent` — safe, additive.\n- `engine/turn.py` firing site only adds a new `elif` for `Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`/`POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` with `step is None`. Each main phase appears exactly once in `_TURN_SEQUENCE`, so no double-fire; existing upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup branches are untouched.\n- Delayed trigger is one-shot and player-scoped: `condition` requires `event.player is controller` and a `fired[\"done\"]` flag; `_effect` sets the flag and `unregister(self)`. The stack fully resolves before `advance_phase`, so it cannot fire on the opponent's main phase or pay out twice.\n- Counter logic removes the target's `StackObject` (still on the stack since ManaSculpt's own object was already popped) and routes the card to its owner's graveyard, so the spell never resolves.\n- Target filter `_is_spell` correctly rejects players and requires spell `card_types`; `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` kwargs and the `Instant` constructor kwargs all match the engine signatures.\n- Card lives at the required path `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`; no engine symbols renamed/removed; no test files touched.\n\nNo strict issues found. Two advisory notes recorded in the review JSON."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abce7c38e2dceb6e2 (use SendMessage with to: 'abce7c38e2dceb6e2' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 44544\ntool_uses: 23\nduration_ms: 121649</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i