{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WXVD7iq8nL36BCvNUCDT2P","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, cross-run conventions and decisions.\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t## Engine: spell resolution → graveyard is a replaceable move (sos_1)\n7\t`engine/casting._resolve_spell` now routes a resolving non-permanent spell's\n8\tstack→graveyard move through the replacement manager via the additive\n9\t`SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`,\n10\tin `engine/events.py`). Cards needing \"if this spell would go to the graveyard,\n11\texile/do X instead\" should register a `ReplacementEffect` keyed to the spell that\n12\tmatches `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` and rewrites `destination`. Default\n13\tbehavior (no matching replacement → graveyard) is unchanged.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: converge (sos_4)\n16\tConverge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast = `len(set(self.colors_spent))`.\n17\tThe engine records `colors_spent` during payment (FDN 205 convention). Initialize\n18\t`self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__` so an unpaid/empty cast yields X=0 and a\n19\tsafe no-op resolution. \"Any target\" filter: a player (`hasattr(obj,\"life\")`) OR a\n20\tpermanent whose `card_types` intersects {CREATURE, PLANESWALKER} (engine/types.py\n21\thas no BATTLE type).\n22\t\n23\t## Engine: card/token colors + Prepared mechanic (sos_13)\n24\t- `CardImpl`/`Creature` now carry a `colors: set[Color]` attribute. Pass `colors`\n25\t  explicitly for tokens (no mana cost); otherwise it derives from the mana cost's\n26\t  colored/hybrid pips (`_colors_from_mana_cost` in engine/card.py). `engine/game.create_token`\n27\t  accepts/sets token colors.\n28\t- `engine/protection.get_colors` treats a present-but-EMPTY `colors` set as \"no\n29\t  explicit color info\" and falls through to mana-cost / `.color` derivation\n30\t  (so colorless cards carrying an empty set don't mask derivation).\n31\t- **Prepared** mechanic is NOT a `Keyword` enum member (engine_tests/test_types.py\n32\t  pins `len(Keyword) == 16`). Surface it via a `card.is_prepared` bool + rules text.\n33\t  The prepared cast loop is driven by additive `engine.casting.cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)`:\n34\t  copies the `prepare_spell`, exiles the copy, clears `is_prepared`, free-casts it.\n35\t  Expose the inset face as `card.prepare_spell` (aliases `prepared_spell`/`other_face`).\n36\t\n37\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking + beginning-of-main-phase trigger (sos_57)\n38\t- `ManaPool.last_payment_total` (read-only property) records the TOTAL quantity of\n39\t  mana paid on the last payment (alongside the existing `last_payment_colors`).\n40\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell` persists it onto the spell as `card.mana_spent`\n41\t  (diverges from CMC for X / cost-reduced spells). Cards reading mana spent should\n42\t  use `spell.mana_spent`, falling back to `mana_cost.cmc` for stack-placed spells.\n43\t- `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fields: `player`, `phase`) is\n44\t  fired in `engine.turn.run_turn` at the start of each main phase\n45\t  (PRECOMBAT_MAIN / POSTCOMBAT_MAIN when `game.step is None`), mirroring the\n46\t  BeginningOfUpkeep firing pattern. Use it for begin-of-main-phase delayed effects;\n47\t  scope the trigger condition to `event.player is controller` and make one-shot\n48\t  delayed effects unregister themselves after firing.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q6xQr5h8dvwVA6KqJMtNcC","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"e3125eb3-e4dc-48b2-ab6e-fb3c0ab58804","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:11:55.989Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DC89b29e6WWZkfHNQ5QNhL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Utilities API Reference\n2\t\n3\tHelper functions for writing card tests. Import from `test_utils`.\n4\t\n5\t## Functions\n6\t\n7\t### `create_game`\n8\t\n9\t`create_game(deck1=None, deck2=None, *, player1_life=20, player2_life=20, scripts=None) -> GameState`\n10\t\n11\tCreate a two-player game with `DeterministicPlayer` instances. Decks default to empty lists.\n12\t\n13\t```python\n14\tfrom test_utils import create_game\n15\tgame = create_game(player1_life=25)\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\t### `set_board_state`\n19\t\n20\t`set_board_state(game, player_index, *, battlefield=None, hand=None, graveyard=None, life=None, mana=None) -> None`\n21\t\n22\tSet zone contents and player state. Only zones explicitly provided are modified.\n23\t\n24\t- **hand / battlefield / graveyard** — `list` of card objects.\n25\t- **mana** — `dict[ManaType, int]`.\n26\t\n27\t```python\n28\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n29\tfrom engine.types import ManaType\n30\tfrom cards.fdn.fdn_13.card_impl import FleetingFlight\n31\tfrom engine.card import Creature\n32\t\n33\tgame = create_game()\n34\tset_board_state(game, 0, hand=[FleetingFlight(owner=None)], mana={ManaType.WHITE: 2})\n35\tbear = Creature(name=\"Grizzly Bears\", base_power=2, base_toughness=2)\n36\tset_board_state(game, 1, battlefield=[bear], life=15)\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t### `cast_spell`\n40\t\n41\t`cast_spell(game, player_index, card_name, targets=None) -> None`\n42\t\n43\tFind a card in hand by name, cast it, and resolve. Sets sorcery-speed timing automatically.\n44\t\n45\t```python\n46\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell\n47\tfrom engine.types import ManaType\n48\tfrom cards.fdn.fdn_13.card_impl import FleetingFlight\n49\t\n50\tgame = create_game()\n51\tset_board_state(game, 0, hand=[FleetingFlight(owner=None)], mana={ManaType.WHITE: 2})\n52\tcast_spell(game, 0, \"Fleeting Flight\")\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t### `advance_to_phase`\n56\t\n57\t`advance_to_phase(game, phase, step=None) -> None`\n58\t\n59\tFast-forward to the specified phase/step without granting priority.\n60\t\n61\t```python\n62\tfrom test_utils import create_game, advance_to_phase\n63\tfrom engine.types import Phase, Step\n64\t\n65\tgame = create_game()\n66\tadvance_to_phase(game, Phase.COMBAT, Step.DECLARE_ATTACKERS)\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t### `declare_attackers`\n70\t\n71\t`declare_attackers(game, attacker_names) -> None`\n72\t\n73\tAdvance to combat and declare creatures as attackers by name from the active player's battlefield.\n74\t\n75\t```python\n76\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, declare_attackers\n77\tfrom engine.card import Creature\n78\t\n79\tgame = create_game()\n80\tbear = Creature(name=\"Grizzly Bears\", base_power=2, base_toughness=2)\n81\tset_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[bear])\n82\tdeclare_attackers(game, [\"Grizzly Bears\"])\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t### `declare_blockers`\n86\t\n87\t`declare_blockers(game, assignments) -> None`\n88\t\n89\tAssign blockers by name mapping: `{\"attacker_name\": [\"blocker_name\", ...]}`.\n90\t\n91\t```python\n92\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, declare_attackers, declare_blockers\n93\tfrom engine.card import Creature\n94\t\n95\tgame = create_game()\n96\tbear = Creature(name=\"Grizzly Bears\", base_power=2, base_toughness=2)\n97\twall = Creature(name=\"Wall of Wood\", base_power=0, base_toughness=3)\n98\tset_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[bear])\n99\tset_board_state(game, 1, battlefield=[wall])\n100\tdeclare_attackers(game, [\"Grizzly Bears\"])\n101\tdeclare_blockers(game, {\"Grizzly Bears\": [\"Wall of Wood\"]})\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t## Test Structure\n105\t\n106\t```python\n107\timport pytest\n108\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell\n109\tfrom cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic\n110\tfrom engine.types import ManaType\n111\t\n112\tclass TestTheDawningArchaic:\n113\t    def test_basic_cast(self):\n114\t        game = create_game()\n115\t        set_board_state(game, 0, hand=[TheDawningArchaic(owner=None)],\n116\t                        mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 10})\n117\t        cast_spell(game, 0, \"The Dawning Archaic\")\n118\t        assert game.players[0].life == 20\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\t## Constraints\n122\t\n123\t- **Max 30 tests per card.**\n124\t- Import helpers from `test_utils`.\n125\t- Import card implementations from `cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl` (SOS cards you\n126\t  are building) or `cards.fdn.fdn_<N>.card_impl` (FDN reference cards).\n127\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q6xQr5h8dvwVA6KqJMtNcC","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"82a311f1-d147-447d-ad53-0306e0987d8f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:11:55.990Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
