{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoUv7yXid43VRa3KT6QiqQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n2\t\n3\tCard: Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, `{1}{B}{B}`, starting loyalty 3.\n4\t\n5\t```\n6\t+1: Surveil 2.\n7\t-1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n8\t-2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n9\t-7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = heads.\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## File\n13\t`cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — 26 test cases.\n14\t\n15\tConventions followed: planeswalker reference `cards/fdn/fdn_134` — abilities are\n16\tobtained via `get_loyalty_abilities()` and resolved by calling\n17\t`ability.effect(game)`. The per-ability target is supplied on the planeswalker\n18\tbefore resolution. The reference reads `_resolve_target`; some SOS cards use\n19\t`chosen_targets`. The test helpers set both (`_resolve_target`,\n20\t`_resolve_targets`, `chosen_targets`) so the contract stays robust to whichever\n21\tattribute the Implementer reads.\n22\t\n23\t## Coverage\n24\t\n25\t### Static data (`TestRalZarekProperties`)\n26\t- Planeswalker subclass, name, mana cost `{1}{B}{B}`, `PLANESWALKER` card type,\n27\t  legendary (via supertypes or card_types), `Ral` subtype, starting loyalty / current loyalty == 3.\n28\t\n29\t### Ability declaration (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities`)\n30\t- Exactly four `LoyaltyAbility` instances with costs {+1, -1, -2, -7}.\n31\t\n32\t### +1 Surveil 2 (`TestRalZarekPlusOneSurveil`)\n33\t- Keep-on-top decisions leave the top two cards in the library, none milled.\n34\t- Put-to-graveyard decisions move both looked-at cards to the graveyard.\n35\t- Only the top two are looked at — a third library card is never touched.\n36\t  (Drives the controller's scripted yes/no surveil decisions via `_script`.)\n37\t\n38\t### -1 Discard (`TestRalZarekMinusOneDiscard`)\n39\t- A single targeted opponent discards a card (hand -> graveyard).\n40\t- Multiple targeted players each discard one card.\n41\t- Zero targets is a legal no-op (\"any number\" includes zero).\n42\t- Targeting a player with an empty hand does not crash.\n43\t\n44\t### -2 Reanimate (`TestRalZarekMinusTwoReanimate`)\n45\t- A mv<=3 creature in the controller's graveyard returns to the battlefield.\n46\t- mv exactly 3 is eligible (boundary).\n47\t- No chosen target is a no-op (creature stays in graveyard).\n48\t\n49\t  Eligibility upper-bound (mv 4+ ineligible) is enforced at target-selection\n50\t  time via `get_targets`/`TargetRequirement`; since the planeswalker target\n51\t  surface for loyalty abilities is not yet pinned by an engine convention, this\n52\t  test set asserts the resolution contract (low-mv returns; no-target no-op)\n53\t  rather than asserting the selection filter rejects a high-mv creature. That\n54\t  selection-filter check is intentionally left out to avoid coupling to an\n55\t  unestablished target-API shape.\n56\t\n57\t### -7 Ultimate (`TestRalZarekUltimate`)\n58\t- Five coin flips: 3 heads -> opponent skips 3 turns; 0 heads -> 0 skips;\n59\t  5 heads -> 5 skips. Coin outcomes are forced deterministically by patching\n60\t  `random.choice/randint/random` so the test is independent of which RNG call\n61\t  the Implementer uses. The skip count is read from `opponent.skipped_turns`\n62\t  with a fallback to `game.skipped_turns[seat]`.\n63\t- The skip count is applied to the targeted opponent, not the controller.\n64\t\n65\t### Loyalty payment pipeline (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyCosts`)\n66\t- Activating +1 through `engine.abilities.activate_ability` raises loyalty 3->4.\n67\t- The -7 ultimate cannot be activated at loyalty 3 (engine loyalty-cost guard\n68\t  raises `AbilityError`).\n69\t\n70\t## Engine gaps the Implementer will need to close (still tested observably)\n71\t- **Surveil** and **coin flips** have no dedicated engine helper today; the\n72\t  tests drive surveil decisions through the controller's `DeterministicPlayer`\n73\t  script and force coin outcomes by patching `random`. The observable contract\n74\t  (library/graveyard state, skip count) is asserted regardless of how the\n75\t  Implementer wires these.\n76\t- **Skipping turns**: the engine only has an `extra_turns` FIFO; there is no\n77\t  skip mechanism. The ultimate test asserts the *recorded* skip count\n78\t  (`skipped_turns` on the player or game), which the Implementer must surface.\n79\t  This keeps the test contract observable without depending on a full\n80\t  turn-skip execution path.\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases deliberately not covered\n83\t- Full turn-loop execution of skipped turns (would require an engine\n84\t  skip-turn subsystem that does not yet exist; the test asserts the recorded\n85\t  count instead).\n86\t- Legendary-rule uniqueness and planeswalker combat-damage redirection — engine\n87\t  behavior, out of scope for this card.\n88\t- High-mv-creature target rejection for -2 (target-selection API not pinned).\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"44f4f6ce-d832-45db-9426-a340ee681385","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:15:21.577Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\nCard: Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, `{1}{B}{B}`, starting loyalty 3.\n\n```\n+1: Surveil 2.\n-1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n-2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n-7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = heads.\n```\n\n## File\n`cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — 26 test cases.\n\nConventions followed: planeswalker reference `cards/fdn/fdn_134` — abilities are\nobtained via `get_loyalty_abilities()` and resolved by calling\n`ability.effect(game)`. The per-ability target is supplied on the planeswalker\nbefore resolution. The reference reads `_resolve_target`; some SOS cards use\n`chosen_targets`. The test helpers set both (`_resolve_target`,\n`_resolve_targets`, `chosen_targets`) so the contract stays robust to whichever\nattribute the Implementer reads.\n\n## Coverage\n\n### Static data (`TestRalZarekProperties`)\n- Planeswalker subclass, name, mana cost `{1}{B}{B}`, `PLANESWALKER` card type,\n  legendary (via supertypes or card_types), `Ral` subtype, starting loyalty / current loyalty == 3.\n\n### Ability declaration (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities`)\n- Exactly four `LoyaltyAbility` instances with costs {+1, -1, -2, -7}.\n\n### +1 Surveil 2 (`TestRalZarekPlusOneSurveil`)\n- Keep-on-top decisions leave the top two cards in the library, none milled.\n- Put-to-graveyard decisions move both looked-at cards to the graveyard.\n- Only the top two are looked at — a third library card is never touched.\n  (Drives the controller's scripted yes/no surveil decisions via `_script`.)\n\n### -1 Discard (`TestRalZarekMinusOneDiscard`)\n- A single targeted opponent discards a card (hand -> graveyard).\n- Multiple targeted players each discard one card.\n- Zero targets is a legal no-op (\"any number\" includes zero).\n- Targeting a player with an empty hand does not crash.\n\n### -2 Reanimate (`TestRalZarekMinusTwoReanimate`)\n- A mv<=3 creature in the controller's graveyard returns to the battlefield.\n- mv exactly 3 is eligible (boundary).\n- No chosen target is a no-op (creature stays in graveyard).\n\n  Eligibility upper-bound (mv 4+ ineligible) is enforced at target-selection\n  time via `get_targets`/`TargetRequirement`; since the planeswalker target\n  surface for loyalty abilities is not yet pinned by an engine convention, this\n  test set asserts the resolution contract (low-mv returns; no-target no-op)\n  rather than asserting the selection filter rejects a high-mv creature. That\n  selection-filter check is intentionally left out to avoid coupling to an\n  unestablished target-API shape.\n\n### -7 Ultimate (`TestRalZarekUltimate`)\n- Five coin flips: 3 heads -> opponent skips 3 turns; 0 heads -> 0 skips;\n  5 heads -> 5 skips. Coin outcomes are forced deterministically by patching\n  `random.choice/randint/random` so the test is independent of which RNG call\n  the Implementer uses. The skip count is read from `opponent.skipped_turns`\n  with a fallback to `game.skipped_turns[seat]`.\n- The skip count is applied to the targeted opponent, not the controller.\n\n### Loyalty payment pipeline (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyCosts`)\n- Activating +1 through `engine.abilities.activate_ability` raises loyalty 3->4.\n- The -7 ultimate cannot be activated at loyalty 3 (engine loyalty-cost guard\n  raises `AbilityError`).\n\n## Engine gaps the Implementer will need to close (still tested observably)\n- **Surveil** and **coin flips** have no dedicated engine helper today; the\n  tests drive surveil decisions through the controller's `DeterministicPlayer`\n  script and force coin outcomes by patching `random`. The observable contract\n  (library/graveyard state, skip count) is asserted regardless of how the\n  Implementer wires these.\n- **Skipping turns**: the engine only has an `extra_turns` FIFO; there is no\n  skip mechanism. The ultimate test asserts the *recorded* skip count\n  (`skipped_turns` on the player or game), which the Implementer must surface.\n  This keeps the test contract observable without depending on a full\n  turn-skip execution path.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately not covered\n- Full turn-loop execution of skipped turns (would require an engine\n  skip-turn subsystem that does not yet exist; the test asserts the recorded\n  count instead).\n- Legendary-rule uniqueness and planeswalker combat-damage redirection — engine\n  behavior, out of scope for this card.\n- High-mv-creature target rejection for -2 (target-selection API not pinned).\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
