{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01K38tR69u4Va3mdNrfrRQ6i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fpj3XF4bVrLFKGPYX2XFRj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/AGENTS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5447,"cache_read_input_tokens":8113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5447,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0131x3Q5CoF8oe17FvLyvBg1","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"97356d13-b343-4e01-bae2-e5a5a3418daf","request_id":"req_011CbcSjNYzeLp2YXiY3wqef","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015U68gjnxUSrzBxZMsu8uAp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n2\t\n3\tCard: Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, `{1}{B}{B}`, starting loyalty 3.\n4\t\n5\t```\n6\t+1: Surveil 2.\n7\t-1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n8\t-2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n9\t-7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = heads.\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## File\n13\t`cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — 26 test cases.\n14\t\n15\tConventions followed: planeswalker reference `cards/fdn/fdn_134` — abilities are\n16\tobtained via `get_loyalty_abilities()` and resolved by calling\n17\t`ability.effect(game)`. The per-ability target is supplied on the planeswalker\n18\tbefore resolution. The reference reads `_resolve_target`; some SOS cards use\n19\t`chosen_targets`. The test helpers set both (`_resolve_target`,\n20\t`_resolve_targets`, `chosen_targets`) so the contract stays robust to whichever\n21\tattribute the Implementer reads.\n22\t\n23\t## Coverage\n24\t\n25\t### Static data (`TestRalZarekProperties`)\n26\t- Planeswalker subclass, name, mana cost `{1}{B}{B}`, `PLANESWALKER` card type,\n27\t  legendary (via supertypes or card_types), `Ral` subtype, starting loyalty / current loyalty == 3.\n28\t\n29\t### Ability declaration (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities`)\n30\t- Exactly four `LoyaltyAbility` instances with costs {+1, -1, -2, -7}.\n31\t\n32\t### +1 Surveil 2 (`TestRalZarekPlusOneSurveil`)\n33\t- Keep-on-top decisions leave the top two cards in the library, none milled.\n34\t- Put-to-graveyard decisions move both looked-at cards to the graveyard.\n35\t- Only the top two are looked at — a third library card is never touched.\n36\t  (Drives the controller's scripted yes/no surveil decisions via `_script`.)\n37\t\n38\t### -1 Discard (`TestRalZarekMinusOneDiscard`)\n39\t- A single targeted opponent discards a card (hand -> graveyard).\n40\t- Multiple targeted players each discard one card.\n41\t- Zero targets is a legal no-op (\"any number\" includes zero).\n42\t- Targeting a player with an empty hand does not crash.\n43\t\n44\t### -2 Reanimate (`TestRalZarekMinusTwoReanimate`)\n45\t- A mv<=3 creature in the controller's graveyard returns to the battlefield.\n46\t- mv exactly 3 is eligible (boundary).\n47\t- No chosen target is a no-op (creature stays in graveyard).\n48\t\n49\t  Eligibility upper-bound (mv 4+ ineligible) is enforced at target-selection\n50\t  time via `get_targets`/`TargetRequirement`; since the planeswalker target\n51\t  surface for loyalty abilities is not yet pinned by an engine convention, this\n52\t  test set asserts the resolution contract (low-mv returns; no-target no-op)\n53\t  rather than asserting the selection filter rejects a high-mv creature. That\n54\t  selection-filter check is intentionally left out to avoid coupling to an\n55\t  unestablished target-API shape.\n56\t\n57\t### -7 Ultimate (`TestRalZarekUltimate`)\n58\t- Five coin flips: 3 heads -> opponent skips 3 turns; 0 heads -> 0 skips;\n59\t  5 heads -> 5 skips. Coin outcomes are forced deterministically by patching\n60\t  `random.choice/randint/random` so the test is independent of which RNG call\n61\t  the Implementer uses. The skip count is read from `opponent.skipped_turns`\n62\t  with a fallback to `game.skipped_turns[seat]`.\n63\t- The skip count is applied to the targeted opponent, not the controller.\n64\t\n65\t### Loyalty payment pipeline (`TestRalZarekLoyaltyCosts`)\n66\t- Activating +1 through `engine.abilities.activate_ability` raises loyalty 3->4.\n67\t- The -7 ultimate cannot be activated at loyalty 3 (engine loyalty-cost guard\n68\t  raises `AbilityError`).\n69\t\n70\t## Engine gaps the Implementer will need to close (still tested observably)\n71\t- **Surveil** and **coin flips** have no dedicated engine helper today; the\n72\t  tests drive surveil decisions through the controller's `DeterministicPlayer`\n73\t  script and force coin outcomes by patching `random`. The observable contract\n74\t  (library/graveyard state, skip count) is asserted regardless of how the\n75\t  Implementer wires these.\n76\t- **Skipping turns**: the engine only has an `extra_turns` FIFO; there is no\n77\t  skip mechanism. The ultimate test asserts the *recorded* skip count\n78\t  (`skipped_turns` on the player or game), which the Implementer must surface.\n79\t  This keeps the test contract observable without depending on a full\n80\t  turn-skip execution path.\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases deliberately not covered\n83\t- Full turn-loop execution of skipped turns (would require an engine\n84\t  skip-turn subsystem that does not yet exist; the test asserts the recorded\n85\t  count instead).\n86\t- Legendary-rule uniqueness and planeswalker combat-damage redirection — engine\n87\t  behavior, out of scope for this card.\n88\t- High-mv-creature target rejection for -2 (target-selection API not pinned).\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0131x3Q5CoF8oe17FvLyvBg1","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"adde076f-cb33-4bf5-8dbf-5af660d5256f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:15:51.420Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fpj3XF4bVrLFKGPYX2XFRj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md — Workspace Orientation\n2\t\n3\t## Task\n4\t\n5\tYou are implementing SOS card implementations. Each card's implementation class\n6\tmust be placed in its assigned file:\n7\t\n8\t```\n9\tcards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## Hard Rules\n13\t\n14\t1. **Card location invariant** — Each card's canonical implementation class must\n15\t   remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card\n16\t   directories.\n17\t\n18\t2. **Staged-test integrity** — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only: do not\n19\t   modify, add to, or delete files in it. Likewise do not modify or delete any\n20\t   existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (you may read\n21\t   them as examples, but never edit them). These tests are for your local\n22\t   verification and learning only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies\n23\t   for grading. Editing them — including adding new files — will not change\n24\t   your score, it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are\n25\t   correct. Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n26\t\n27\t3. **Additive-only engine modifications** — You may add new methods, classes,\n28\t   helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing\n29\t   functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete\n30\t   anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\n31\t   Restructuring the engine will break the grader's imports and zero your score.\n32\t\n33\tThese rules are derived from the project's Workspace Contract decisions\n34\t(maintained outside this workspace). They ensure deterministic grading.\n35\t\n36\t## Test Commands\n37\t\n38\tRun from the workspace root:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\tpytest\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tThis discovers:\n45\t- Engine regression tests at `engine_tests/test_*.py`.\n46\t- Per-card FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n47\t  Only a handful of FDN cards ship with a `tests.py` — see `PROJECT_MAP.md`\n48\t  for the canonical list, and use them as illustrative per-card test examples.\n49\t- Per-card SOS tests you write at `cards/sos/sos_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n50\t\n51\tThe workspace `pytest.ini` configures `python_files = test_*.py tests.py` for\n52\tdiscovery of all three patterns and sets a per-test timeout (5 minutes).\n53\t\n54\tStandard imports inside per-card tests:\n55\t\n56\t```python\n57\tfrom cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <ClassName>\n58\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant                  # or whichever base\n59\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n60\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Engine Extension Scope\n64\t\n65\t- **May**: Add files, methods, classes, and helpers inside `engine/`.\n66\t- **May**: Modify the bodies of existing functions in `engine/`.\n67\t- **Must NOT**: Rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/`.\n68\t\n69\t## Rules questions → grep RULEBOOK.txt\n70\t\n71\t`RULEBOOK.txt` (workspace root) is the Magic: The Gathering Comprehensive Rules — the authoritative source for any rules question. **Whenever you're unsure how a mechanic works (keyword behavior, timing, replacement vs trigger ordering, state-based actions, etc.), check the rulebook before guessing in a `card_impl.py` or an `engine/` change.**\n72\t\n73\tThe file is large — don't `cat` or `Read` it whole. See the workspace skill at [`skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`](skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md) for grep recipes, the file's structure (numbered rules + glossary), and best practices.\n74\t\n75\t## Tools\n76\t\n77\tGit is available. The workspace is initialized as a git repository at stage time.\n78\t\n79\t## Navigation\n80\t\n81\tSee `PROJECT_MAP.md` for the directory layout.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0131x3Q5CoF8oe17FvLyvBg1","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"6b5c7fc3-73df-4e10-b9aa-39e79863a0da","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:15:51.420Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
