ility.effect(game)`. Per-ability target is set on the planeswalker before resolution — read whichever of `_resolve_target` / `_resolve_targets` / `chosen_targets` the tests set (they set all to stay robust; support these).\n- Surveil 2 driven by the controller's DeterministicPlayer scripted yes/no decisions (keep-on-top vs to-graveyard). Look at exactly the top 2 library cards.\n- Coin flips: the tests FORCE outcomes by patching `random.choice` / `random.randint` / `random.random`. Use the `random` module (one of those calls) so patched RNG controls heads/tails.\n- Turn-skip: surface the recorded skip count on the TARGETED OPPONENT as `opponent.skipped_turns` (and/or `game.skipped_turns[seat]`). Implement a real skip mechanism if feasible; at minimum record the count there. Skip applies to the targeted opponent, not the controller.\n- Loyalty cost activation via `engine.abilities.activate_ability` adjusts loyalty; the -7 must be guarded so it can't activate at loyalty 3 (engine loyalty-cost guard raises AbilityError).\n\nREFERENCES (read for API discovery — rich docstrings):\n- engine/card.py (Planeswalker, LoyaltyAbility), engine/abilities.py (activate_ability, loyalty cost guard), engine/events.py, engine/triggers.py, engine/zones.py, engine/game.py, engine/turn.py (extra_turns FIFO — model skip similarly)\n- Planeswalker reference: cards/fdn/fdn_134/card_impl.py (loyalty abilities pattern). Also look for surveil/scry, discard, and reanimation examples among cards/fdn/fdn_*.\n- /workspace/AGENTS.md, /workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md, /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md, /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json\n- RULEBOOK.txt (grep, don't read whole) for Surveil, coin flips, \"skips their next turn\".\n\nENGINE RULES (from AGENTS.md):\n- You MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files in engine/, modify bodies of existing engine functions, and add new event/trigger classes.\n- You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in engine/.\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file. engine_tests/test_types.py pins certain enum counts (e.g. Keyword count = 16) — do not break pinned counts.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Read spec, test file, rationale.\n2. Implement the planeswalker so ALL 26 tests pass, adding additive engine support (surveil helper, coin-flip, skip-turn recording, reanimation) as needed.\n3. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, `pytest cards/fdn/` to confirm nothing breaks.\n4. If a test is genuinely WRONG, do NOT modify it — return DISPUTE with details.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Implementation to /workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py (+ engine changes).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff — `git diff` of all changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md — what you did, the exact contracts (surveil decision flow, coin-flip RNG call, skip-turn recording attribute, reanimation), engine changes, any spec deviations.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-files.txt — modified files.\n- Upsert this card's entry into /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json (match by card: \"sos_97\"). Keep other entries intact.\n\nReturn either IMPL_DONE (files_changed, tests_passing, diff_path, rationale_path, notes) or DISPUTE (tests_failing, disputed_tests, dispute_path, notes) exactly as specified.","agentId":"a7311c677a0424777","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All output files written and FILES_MODIFIED.json updated.\n\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: 2\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: Implemented Ral Zarek planeswalker (surveil/discard/reanimate/coin-flip turn-skip) with additive engine helpers `surveil`, `flip_coin`, `skip_turns` in engine/game.py; all 26 card tests plus 1184 engine+FDN tests pass."}],"totalDurationMs":155075,"totalTokens":76567,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":75744,"output_tokens":212,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_reque