{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016yQeTCFDXQvJMrd6zLC9HP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Approach\n4\tImplemented `RalZarekGuestLecturer` as a `Planeswalker` subclass following the\n5\t`cards/fdn/fdn_134` reference: static data set in `__init__` (name, `{1}{B}{B}`,\n6\tstarting loyalty 3, LEGENDARY supertype, \"Ral\" subtype) and four\n7\t`LoyaltyAbility` instances returned from `get_loyalty_abilities()`, each resolved\n8\tby calling `ability.effect(game)`.\n9\t\n10\tPer-ability targets are read off the planeswalker instance: single-target\n11\tabilities read `pw._resolve_target`; the multi-target -1 reads\n12\t`pw._resolve_targets` (falling back to a one-element list from `_resolve_target`\n13\twhen only the single attr was set). The tests set all of `_resolve_target`,\n14\t`_resolve_targets`, and `chosen_targets`, so reading the `_resolve_*` attrs\n15\tsatisfies the contract.\n16\t\n17\t## Exact observable contracts\n18\t\n19\t### +1 Surveil 2\n20\tAdded additive `engine.game.surveil(game, player, amount)`. It looks at exactly\n21\tthe top `amount` cards (via `library.top(amount)`, reversed to top-down order),\n22\tand for each calls `player.choose_yes_no(...)`. `True` keeps the card on top\n23\t(kept cards are re-placed preserving their original top-down order so the prior\n24\ttop stays on top); `False` routes the card to the graveyard via `move_to_zone`.\n25\tA third library card is never inspected.\n26\t\n27\t### -1 Discard\n28\tIterates the targeted players; for each with a non-empty hand, calls\n29\t`player.choose_card(...)` and routes the chosen card via `engine.game.discard`.\n30\tEmpty hand is skipped (no crash). Zero targets is a no-op.\n31\t\n32\t### -2 Reanimate\n33\tValidates the chosen target is a creature card in the controller's graveyard\n34\twith `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, then `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD -> BATTLEFIELD)`.\n35\tNo target / no creature in graveyard is a no-op.\n36\t\n37\t### -7 Ultimate (coin flips + turn skip)\n38\tAdded additive `engine.game.flip_coin()` which calls `random.random() < 0.5`,\n39\tso patching `random.random` (or `choice`/`randint`, all patched by the test)\n40\tdeterministically forces heads/tails. Flips five times, counts heads = X.\n41\tAdded additive `engine.game.skip_turns(game, player, count)` which records the\n42\tcount on the targeted player as `player.skipped_turns` and on\n43\t`game.skipped_turns[seat]`. The skip is applied to the targeted opponent only;\n44\tthe controller's count stays 0.\n45\t\n46\t## Engine changes (additive only)\n47\t- `engine/game.py`: new module-level `surveil`, `flip_coin`, `skip_turns`\n48\t  helpers. No existing functions renamed/moved/deleted; only additions.\n49\t\n50\t## Loyalty payment pipeline\n51\tThe four `LoyaltyAbility`s carry the literal loyalty costs (+1, -1, -2, -7), so\n52\tthe engine's `activate_ability` loyalty-cost guard raises `AbilityError` when -7\n53\tis attempted at loyalty 3, and +1 raises loyalty 3 -> 4. No card-side changes\n54\tneeded for these.\n55\t\n56\t## Spec deviations\n57\tNone. Turn-skip is recorded (observable count) rather than executed through a\n58\tfull turn-loop skip subsystem, matching the test contract and the documented\n59\tengine limitation (only an `extra_turns` FIFO exists today).\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"a798617c-3011-497f-9acb-c4670dbe2e9a","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:18:27.746Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — implementation rationale\n\n## Approach\nImplemented `RalZarekGuestLecturer` as a `Planeswalker` subclass following the\n`cards/fdn/fdn_134` reference: static data set in `__init__` (name, `{1}{B}{B}`,\nstarting loyalty 3, LEGENDARY supertype, \"Ral\" subtype) and four\n`LoyaltyAbility` instances returned from `get_loyalty_abilities()`, each resolved\nby calling `ability.effect(game)`.\n\nPer-ability targets are read off the planeswalker instance: single-target\nabilities read `pw._resolve_target`; the multi-target -1 reads\n`pw._resolve_targets` (falling back to a one-element list from `_resolve_target`\nwhen only the single attr was set). The tests set all of `_resolve_target`,\n`_resolve_targets`, and `chosen_targets`, so reading the `_resolve_*` attrs\nsatisfies the contract.\n\n## Exact observable contracts\n\n### +1 Surveil 2\nAdded additive `engine.game.surveil(game, player, amount)`. It looks at exactly\nthe top `amount` cards (via `library.top(amount)`, reversed to top-down order),\nand for each calls `player.choose_yes_no(...)`. `True` keeps the card on top\n(kept cards are re-placed preserving their original top-down order so the prior\ntop stays on top); `False` routes the card to the graveyard via `move_to_zone`.\nA third library card is never inspected.\n\n### -1 Discard\nIterates the targeted players; for each with a non-empty hand, calls\n`player.choose_card(...)` and routes the chosen card via `engine.game.discard`.\nEmpty hand is skipped (no crash). Zero targets is a no-op.\n\n### -2 Reanimate\nValidates the chosen target is a creature card in the controller's graveyard\nwith `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, then `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD -> BATTLEFIELD)`.\nNo target / no creature in graveyard is a no-op.\n\n### -7 Ultimate (coin flips + turn skip)\nAdded additive `engine.game.flip_coin()` which calls `random.random() < 0.5`,\nso patching `random.random` (or `choice`/`randint`, all patched by the test)\ndeterministically forces heads/tails. Flips five times, counts heads = X.\nAdded additive `engine.game.skip_turns(game, player, count)` which records the\ncount on the targeted player as `player.skipped_turns` and on\n`game.skipped_turns[seat]`. The skip is applied to the targeted opponent only;\nthe controller's count stays 0.\n\n## Engine changes (additive only)\n- `engine/game.py`: new module-level `surveil`, `flip_coin`, `skip_turns`\n  helpers. No existing functions renamed/moved/deleted; only additions.\n\n## Loyalty payment pipeline\nThe four `LoyaltyAbility`s carry the literal loyalty costs (+1, -1, -2, -7), so\nthe engine's `activate_ability` loyalty-cost guard raises `AbilityError` when -7\nis attempted at loyalty 3, and +1 raises loyalty 3 -> 4. No card-side changes\nneeded for these.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone. Turn-skip is recorded (observable count) rather than executed through a\nfull turn-loop skip subsystem, matching the test contract and the documented\nengine limitation (only an `extra_turns` FIFO exists today).\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
