{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HAHjYcCggkwrsHee8ds86U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"name\": \"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\",\n3\t  \"mana_cost\": \"{1}{B}{B}\",\n4\t  \"type_line\": \"Legendary Planeswalker — Ral\",\n5\t  \"oracle_text\": \"+1: Surveil 2.\\n−1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\\n−2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n−7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\",\n6\t  \"power\": null,\n7\t  \"toughness\": null,\n8\t  \"loyalty\": \"3\",\n9\t  \"colors\": [\n10\t    \"B\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"keywords\": [\n13\t    \"Surveil\"\n14\t  ],\n15\t  \"rarity\": \"mythic\",\n16\t  \"set_code\": \"sos\",\n17\t  \"collector_number\": \"97\",\n18\t  \"complexity_tier\": \"expert\"\n19\t}\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014cHGGqFoHmHis5WwMogErK","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"210f22f9-e87c-41a2-9488-96d535f682d6","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:18:56.004Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Spi8uAKx76h7eXaUwJzZyx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Approach\n4\tImplemented `RalZarekGuestLecturer` as a `Planeswalker` subclass following the\n5\t`cards/fdn/fdn_134` reference: static data set in `__init__` (name, `{1}{B}{B}`,\n6\tstarting loyalty 3, LEGENDARY supertype, \"Ral\" subtype) and four\n7\t`LoyaltyAbility` instances returned from `get_loyalty_abilities()`, each resolved\n8\tby calling `ability.effect(game)`.\n9\t\n10\tPer-ability targets are read off the planeswalker instance: single-target\n11\tabilities read `pw._resolve_target`; the multi-target -1 reads\n12\t`pw._resolve_targets` (falling back to a one-element list from `_resolve_target`\n13\twhen only the single attr was set). The tests set all of `_resolve_target`,\n14\t`_resolve_targets`, and `chosen_targets`, so reading the `_resolve_*` attrs\n15\tsatisfies the contract.\n16\t\n17\t## Exact observable contracts\n18\t\n19\t### +1 Surveil 2\n20\tAdded additive `engine.game.surveil(game, player, amount)`. It looks at exactly\n21\tthe top `amount` cards (via `library.top(amount)`, reversed to top-down order),\n22\tand for each calls `player.choose_yes_no(...)`. `True` keeps the card on top\n23\t(kept cards are re-placed preserving their original top-down order so the prior\n24\ttop stays on top); `False` routes the card to the graveyard via `move_to_zone`.\n25\tA third library card is never inspected.\n26\t\n27\t### -1 Discard\n28\tIterates the targeted players; for each with a non-empty hand, calls\n29\t`player.choose_card(...)` and routes the chosen card via `engine.game.discard`.\n30\tEmpty hand is skipped (no crash). Zero targets is a no-op.\n31\t\n32\t### -2 Reanimate\n33\tValidates the chosen target is a creature card in the controller's graveyard\n34\twith `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, then `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD -> BATTLEFIELD)`.\n35\tNo target / no creature in graveyard is a no-op.\n36\t\n37\t### -7 Ultimate (coin flips + turn skip)\n38\tAdded additive `engine.game.flip_coin()` which calls `random.random() < 0.5`,\n39\tso patching `random.random` (or `choice`/`randint`, all patched by the test)\n40\tdeterministically forces heads/tails. Flips five times, counts heads = X.\n41\tAdded additive `engine.game.skip_turns(game, player, count)` which records the\n42\tcount on the targeted player as `player.skipped_turns` and on\n43\t`game.skipped_turns[seat]`. The skip is applied to the targeted opponent only;\n44\tthe controller's count stays 0.\n45\t\n46\t## Engine changes (additive only)\n47\t- `engine/game.py`: new module-level `surveil`, `flip_coin`, `skip_turns`\n48\t  helpers. No existing functions renamed/moved/deleted; only additions.\n49\t\n50\t## Loyalty payment pipeline\n51\tThe four `LoyaltyAbility`s carry the literal loyalty costs (+1, -1, -2, -7), so\n52\tthe engine's `activate_ability` loyalty-cost guard raises `AbilityError` when -7\n53\tis attempted at loyalty 3, and +1 raises loyalty 3 -> 4. No card-side changes\n54\tneeded for these.\n55\t\n56\t## Spec deviations\n57\tNone. Turn-skip is recorded (observable count) rather than executed through a\n58\tfull turn-loop skip subsystem, matching the test contract and the documented\n59\tengine limitation (only an `extra_turns` FIFO exists today).\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014cHGGqFoHmHis5WwMogErK","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"170af40d-f0a5-4a6e-9c47-24928a4278b3","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:18:56.007Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
