{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0167RCsswBFjJPkri2HJbZsW","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/game.py:407:def skip_turns(game: GameState, player: Player, count: int) -> None:\nengine/game.py:411:    recorded count both on the player (``player.skipped_turns``) and on the\nengine/game.py:412:    game keyed by seat index (``game.skipped_turns[seat]``) so it is\nengine/game.py:421:    player.skipped_turns = getattr(player, \"skipped_turns\", 0) + count\nengine/game.py:423:    if not hasattr(game, \"skipped_turns\") or game.skipped_turns is None:\nengine/game.py:424:        game.skipped_turns = {}\nengine/game.py:430:        game.skipped_turns[seat] = game.skipped_turns.get(seat, 0) + count\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:16:| `game_state.py` | 180+ | `GameState` — central state container holding players, stack, trigger/effect/replacement managers, combat state, phase/step tracking, turn number, priority index. `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO queue for extra turn management. `_normal_next_index` for tracking normal rotation independently. `_TURN_SEQUENCE` constant. `advance_phase()` for turn progression (pops extra turns without advancing normal rotation). |\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:31:- **`GameState`** — The central authority; passed to nearly every function. Now includes `extra_turns` queue.\nengine/game_state.py:78:        self.extra_turns: list[int] = []\nengine/game_state.py:150:            if self.extra_turns:\nengine/game_state.py:155:                self.active_player_index = self.extra_turns.pop(0)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014cHGGqFoHmHis5WwMogErK","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"d4b6cb3f-f0d9-4cb7-b24b-00645a9e8d18","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:19:12.136Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
