{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RQUM9zqkWurLsaCyyVGn9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\"severity\": \"strict\", \"file\": \"engine/game.py\", \"line\": 407, \"comment\": \"skip_turns only records a count on player.skipped_turns and game.skipped_turns[seat]; nothing in engine/turn.py or GameState.advance_phase ever consumes it, so the targeted opponent never actually loses a turn. The card's -7 is therefore mechanically inert beyond the bookkeeping value. The engine already has a working precedent for this kind of turn manipulation: GameState.advance_phase (engine/game_state.py:150-159) pops from the extra_turns FIFO to grant additional turns. The skip should be wired symmetrically: when advance_phase is about to set active_player_index to a seat whose skipped_turns > 0, decrement that counter and advance rotation again (skip that player's turn) instead of running it. Without this the ultimate does not implement 'skips their next X turns' as printed. (Tests only assert the recorded count, so they pass regardless — this is still a real correctness gap a PR reviewer would block on.)\"},\n3\t  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 92, \"comment\": \"_minus2 does getattr(target.mana_cost, 'cmc', 0) > 3. If a targeted creature card ever has mana_cost == None this raises AttributeError (None has no attribute access guarded by getattr only on the attribute name, not the base). Real card objects always carry a ManaCost so this is unlikely in practice, but a defensive `mc = getattr(target, 'mana_cost', None)` + None check would harden the no-op path.\"},\n4\t  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"engine/game.py\", \"line\": 196, \"comment\": \"flip_coin accepts an unused `game` parameter (kept for signature symmetry) and imports `random` inside the function. Harmless, but the unused parameter may read as dead code to future maintainers; a brief note or removal would be cleaner.\"},\n5\t  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 84, \"comment\": \"_minus1 wraps player.choose_card in a bare `except Exception:` that silently falls back to cards[0]. This can mask genuine bugs in a player controller's choose_card. Catching a narrower exception (or letting it propagate in non-AI test contexts) would be safer; advisory since the fallback keeps the discard from crashing.\"}\n6\t]\n7\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BjxkzZ6oUYxDmJcFLGTGw8","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"25dad950-696d-412b-bffd-7ad030ffe08f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:20:08.739Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_97 implementation"}
