{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y3JVDNoL3tNkCACUXcPRVw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, cross-run conventions and decisions.\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t## Engine: spell resolution → graveyard is a replaceable move (sos_1)\n7\t`engine/casting._resolve_spell` now routes a resolving non-permanent spell's\n8\tstack→graveyard move through the replacement manager via the additive\n9\t`SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`,\n10\tin `engine/events.py`). Cards needing \"if this spell would go to the graveyard,\n11\texile/do X instead\" should register a `ReplacementEffect` keyed to the spell that\n12\tmatches `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` and rewrites `destination`. Default\n13\tbehavior (no matching replacement → graveyard) is unchanged.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: converge (sos_4)\n16\tConverge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast = `len(set(self.colors_spent))`.\n17\tThe engine records `colors_spent` during payment (FDN 205 convention). Initialize\n18\t`self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__` so an unpaid/empty cast yields X=0 and a\n19\tsafe no-op resolution. \"Any target\" filter: a player (`hasattr(obj,\"life\")`) OR a\n20\tpermanent whose `card_types` intersects {CREATURE, PLANESWALKER} (engine/types.py\n21\thas no BATTLE type).\n22\t\n23\t## Engine: card/token colors + Prepared mechanic (sos_13)\n24\t- `CardImpl`/`Creature` now carry a `colors: set[Color]` attribute. Pass `colors`\n25\t  explicitly for tokens (no mana cost); otherwise it derives from the mana cost's\n26\t  colored/hybrid pips (`_colors_from_mana_cost` in engine/card.py). `engine/game.create_token`\n27\t  accepts/sets token colors.\n28\t- `engine/protection.get_colors` treats a present-but-EMPTY `colors` set as \"no\n29\t  explicit color info\" and falls through to mana-cost / `.color` derivation\n30\t  (so colorless cards carrying an empty set don't mask derivation).\n31\t- **Prepared** mechanic is NOT a `Keyword` enum member (engine_tests/test_types.py\n32\t  pins `len(Keyword) == 16`). Surface it via a `card.is_prepared` bool + rules text.\n33\t  The prepared cast loop is driven by additive `engine.casting.cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)`:\n34\t  copies the `prepare_spell`, exiles the copy, clears `is_prepared`, free-casts it.\n35\t  Expose the inset face as `card.prepare_spell` (aliases `prepared_spell`/`other_face`).\n36\t\n37\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking + beginning-of-main-phase trigger (sos_57)\n38\t- `ManaPool.last_payment_total` (read-only property) records the TOTAL quantity of\n39\t  mana paid on the last payment (alongside the existing `last_payment_colors`).\n40\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell` persists it onto the spell as `card.mana_spent`\n41\t  (diverges from CMC for X / cost-reduced spells). Cards reading mana spent should\n42\t  use `spell.mana_spent`, falling back to `mana_cost.cmc` for stack-placed spells.\n43\t- `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fields: `player`, `phase`) is\n44\t  fired in `engine.turn.run_turn` at the start of each main phase\n45\t  (PRECOMBAT_MAIN / POSTCOMBAT_MAIN when `game.step is None`), mirroring the\n46\t  BeginningOfUpkeep firing pattern. Use it for begin-of-main-phase delayed effects;\n47\t  scope the trigger condition to `event.player is controller` and make one-shot\n48\t  delayed effects unregister themselves after firing.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BjxkzZ6oUYxDmJcFLGTGw8","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"b88a0dff-74a1-4b6f-b265-100cab5c63c0","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:20:15.709Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_97 implementation"}
