{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Bk4mMRF8wea6457cLeMqPp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X1MVdxyD8egbHF9h7QVS51","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_97 revision rationale\n\n## STRICT: wire the -7 turn-skip into the turn loop\n\nPreviously `engine.game.skip_turns` only *recorded* the skip count on\n`player.skipped_turns` and `game.skipped_turns[seat]`; nothing consumed it, so\nthe targeted opponent never actually lost a turn.\n\nI wired consumption symmetrically to the existing `extra_turns` FIFO, in the\nsingle place turn rotation happens — `GameState.advance_phase` (engine/game_state.py).\nAt end-of-turn, after the active player is chosen (from `extra_turns` if any,\nelse normal rotation), I now call a new helper `GameState._consume_skipped_turns()`:\n\n- If `game.skipped_turns` is empty/absent (the default for all existing games,\n  including every engine_test), it returns immediately — zero behavior change.\n- Otherwise, while the seat about to become active has `skipped_turns > 0`, it\n  decrements that seat's counter (both `game.skipped_turns[seat]` and the\n  player's `player.skipped_turns`, keeping the recorded-count contract intact)\n  and advances the normal rotation again, handing the turn to the next seat.\n- The loop is bounded by `len(self.players)` so an all-skipped board cannot spin\n  forever (it just proceeds with whatever seat is reached).\n\n`extra_turns` still takes precedence (it is popped first, before the skip check),\nso a granted extra turn is honored; skips only apply to seats reached via the\nnormal rotation. This keeps interaction with `extra_turns` sensible.\n\n`skip_turns` itself is unchanged: setting the count is still observable on both\n`player.skipped_turns` and `game.skipped_turns[seat]` (the existing sos_97 tests\nread these), and the count is now actually consumed by the turn loop.\n\n### Verified end-to-end\nA manual run (skip seat 1 twice, then `advance_phase` through three end-of-turns)\nconfirms seat 1 is skipped on its first two scheduled turns and resumes on the\nthird, with `game.skipped_turns[1]` decrementing 2 -> 1 -> 0.\n\n## Advisory hardening (applied)\n\n- **`_minus2` mana_cost None guard**: now `mc = getattr(target, \"mana_cost\", None)`\n  and only compares CMC when `mc is not None`, so a target lacking a ManaCost is\n  treated as eligible rather than raising AttributeError.\n- **`_minus1` narrower exception**: `except (AttributeError, NotImplementedError)`\n  instead of bare `except Exception`, so genuine controller bugs propagate while\n  the missing-`choose_card` fallback path is preserved.\n- **`flip_coin` unused `game` param**: documented in the docstring that the\n  parameter is accepted only for signature symmetry.\n\n## Tests\n`pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` -> 1210 passed.\nNo engine symbols renamed/moved/deleted; changes are additive (one new helper\nmethod + a body change in `advance_phase`). No test files modified.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":42815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":56,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BjxkzZ6oUYxDmJcFLGTGw8","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"47d046d9-1776-4882-bfee-46e5a1d3cd89","request_id":"req_011CbcTBbzrHXAU18qdSjy71","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_97 implementation"}
