{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BjxkzZ6oUYxDmJcFLGTGw8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All changes complete and verified. Final test run already confirmed 1210 passed across the three suites.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/disagreements.json\n\nSummary of changes:\n- STRICT fix: `GameState.advance_phase` (`/workspace/engine/game_state.py`) now calls a new additive helper `_consume_skipped_turns()` at end-of-turn. It reads `game.skipped_turns[seat]` (set by `engine.game.skip_turns`), and when the rotation is about to make a skipped seat active it decrements that seat's counter (on both `game.skipped_turns[seat]` and `player.skipped_turns`) and advances the normal rotation again — symmetric to the `extra_turns` FIFO. The loop is bounded by player count to avoid infinite spinning. When `game.skipped_turns` is absent/empty (every existing engine_test), it's a no-op, so pinned behavior is unchanged. Verified end-to-end that a targeted seat actually loses its scheduled turns and resumes once exhausted.\n- Advisory hardening (all applied): `_minus2` now guards `mana_cost is None` before reading `cmc`; `_minus1` narrows `except Exception` to `(AttributeError, NotImplementedError)`; `flip_coin`'s unused `game` param documented.\n- All changes additive (one new helper method + body change in `advance_phase`); no engine symbols renamed/moved/deleted; no test files modified.\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` -> 1210 passed.\n- `FILES_MODIFIED.json` updated to add `engine/game_state.py` to the sos_97 implementation set."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a005d127dad444be3 (use SendMessage with to: 'a005d127dad444be3' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 49290\ntool_uses: 33\nduration_ms: 157261</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"b19c0d1b-177c-4fee-a19d-cdb9cad3a8cd","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:22:42.973Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are revising your implementation of card sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer) to address review feedback.\n\n- Implementation file: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\n- Test file (you MUST NOT modify): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py\n- Your prior diff: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff\n- Review comments: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json\n- /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json, /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md\n- Engine references: engine/game_state.py (advance_phase, ~lines 150-159 where extra_turns FIFO is consumed), engine/turn.py, engine/game.py.\n\nREQUIRED CHANGES:\n- STRICT (must apply): The -7 ultimate's turn-skip is currently only RECORDED (player.skipped_turns / game.skipped_turns[seat]) and never consumed, so the targeted opponent never actually loses a turn. Wire it into the turn loop so the opponent ACTUALLY skips their next X turns. Follow the existing precedent: GameState.advance_phase consumes the extra_turns FIFO to grant extra turns — symmetrically, when the turn rotation is about to make a seat with skipped_turns > 0 the active player, decrement that seat's skipped_turns and skip that turn (advance rotation again) instead of running it. Keep the recorded count contract intact (the existing tests read player.skipped_turns / game.skipped_turns[seat]) — i.e. setting the count must still be observable, AND the count must now actually be consumed by the turn loop.\n- Make sure interaction with extra_turns is sensible and you do not break existing engine tests.\n\nYou MAY also apply the advisory hardening (defensive mana_cost None check in _minus2; narrower exception in _minus1; flip_coin unused-param note) at your discretion. If you DISAGREE with the strict comment, do NOT silently skip it — record your reasoning in disagreements.json.\n\nENGINE RULES: additive only — may modify function BODIES (e.g. advance_phase body), may add helpers; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; MUST NOT break engine_tests/ pinned counts; MUST NOT modify test files.\n\nVERIFY: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, and `pytest cards/fdn/` — all must pass.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Updated /workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py and engine changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised.diff — `git diff` of ALL current changes (cumulative).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised-rationale.md — what you changed and how the turn-skip now executes; confirm tests pass.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/disagreements.json — JSON array of {review_comment_index, reviewer_comment, implementer_justification}. Empty array [] if you applied everything.\n- Update this card's entry in /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json if the set of modified files changed.\n\nReturn:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/disagreements.json","agentId":"a005d127dad444be3","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All changes complete and verified. Final test run already confirmed 1210 passed across the three suites.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/disagreements.json\n\nSummary of changes:\n- STRICT fix: `GameState.advance_phase` (`/workspace/engine/game_state.py`) now calls a new additive helper `_consume_skipped_turns()` at end-of-turn. It reads `game.skipped_turns[seat]` (set by `engine.game.skip_turns`), and when the rotation is about to make a skipped seat active it decrements that seat's counter (on both `game.skipped_turns[seat]` and `player.skipped_turns`) and advances the normal rotation again — symmetric to the `extra_turns` FIFO. The loop is bounded by player count to avoid infinite spinning. When `game.skipped_turns`