{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JJShwucLnQCYYAQmmsWGxn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0166qnSWZmYYc9acAxtht7Fi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone\n\nCard: `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson (mythic, red).\n\nOracle text:\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total\n> mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them\n> without paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n> name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n> the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n\nTests are written against the established SOS conventions seen in\n`cards/sos/sos_1` (free-casting + exile-instead-of-graveyard replacement) and\n`cards/sos/sos_57` (begin-of-main-phase delayed trigger). They drive the card's\npublic hooks (`on_resolve`, `register_replacement_effects`, trigger\nregistration) through the real engine zone/casting APIs.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties (8 tests)\nStatic card data — the printed contract:\n- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`, `test_mana_value_is_seven` — name and cost\n  `{5}{R}{R}` (MV 7).\n- `test_is_sorcery` — is a `Sorcery` and carries `CardType.SORCERY`.\n- `test_is_lesson` — has the `Lesson` subtype.\n- `test_is_red` — `Color.RED` in colors (the `colors` attribute convention).\n- `test_not_a_creature` — guard against an over-broad type set.\n- `test_rules_text_mentions_paradigm` — Paradigm reminder text present.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneExileUntilFour (7 tests)\nThe \"exile from the top until total mana value ≥ 4\" loop:\n- `test_exiles_until_total_mana_value_at_least_four` — three `{2}` cards: stops\n  after the first two (2+2=4), leaving the third.\n- `test_stops_as_soon_as_threshold_reached_single_big_card` — a single `{4}`\n  meets the threshold alone.\n- `test_exact_threshold_of_four_stops` — exactly 4 (a `{3}{R}` card) is enough.\n- `test_zero_mana_value_cards_do_not_satisfy_threshold` — zero-MV lands do not\n  count toward the threshold; the effect keeps exiling until a real `{4}` is\n  reached (validates \"total mana value\", not \"card count\").\n- `test_exiled_cards_leave_the_library` — exiled cards leave the library and\n  untouched cards remain.\n- `test_empty_library_is_safe_noop` — empty library: no crash, no prompt\n  consumed (empty script proves no choice was requested).\n- `test_library_smaller_than_threshold_exiles_all` — fewer cards than needed to\n  hit 4: exile what's there and stop (no infinite loop / no crash).\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneFreeCast (5 tests)\n\"You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana\ncosts.\" Modeled as a per-spell `choose_yes_no` on the controller (the\nDeterministicPlayer script), with free-casting through the engine pipeline:\n- `test_yes_casts_an_exiled_spell_onto_the_stack` — yes → the spell leaves\n  exile and lands on the stack.\n- `test_free_cast_pays_no_mana` — the spell is cast (on the stack, out of\n  exile) while the mana pool stays empty.\n- `test_no_casts_leaves_spell_in_exile` — no → the exiled card stays in exile,\n  stack empty.\n- `test_can_cast_multiple_exiled_spells` — \"any number\": two yes answers cast\n  both exiled spells (both leave the library and exile; at least one is\n  observable on the stack).\n- `test_lands_among_exiled_cards_are_not_offered_as_spells` — lands are not\n  spells: a land among the exiled cards is not offered for casting (does not\n  consume a prompt) and remains in exile while the spell is cast.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmSelfExile (1 test)\n\"Then exile this spell.\" — `test_resolved_capstone_is_exiled_not_in_graveyard`\ncasts the Capstone for free from hand and resolves it through the engine's\nstack→zone pipeline (which consults `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent`,\nthe sos_1 convention). The Capstone must end up in exile, not the graveyard.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmRecast (3 tests)\n\"After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from\nexile … at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\" Following the\nsos_57 begin-of-main-phase trigger convention:\n- `test_resolution_registers_a_begin_of_main_phase_trigger` — resolving the\n  Capstone registers a trigger keyed to `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_paradigm_trigger_controller_is_the_capstone_controller` — the trigger's\n  controller is the Capstone's controller (\"your\" main phase).\n- `test_paradigm_trigger_only_fires_for_controllers_main_phase` — the trigger\n  condition rejects an opponent's main-phase event.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Mana-value threshold boundary (exact 4, single big card, accumulation past\n  zero-MV cards).\n- Empty / too-small library (no crash, no infinite loop, no spurious prompt).\n- Optional cast declined (cards stay in exile).\n- Lands among exiled cards excluded from the \"cast spells\" clause.\n- Self-exile via the replacement pipeline rather than graveyard.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- The precise number of recast copies allowed and \"first main phase\" vs second\n  main phase distinction in the recurring Paradigm loop: the recast cadence\n  (\"first main phases\", one-shot per turn) is novel and not pinned by any prior\n  KEY_DECISIONS convention. The tests pin that the recurring ability is wired as\n  a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger scoped to the controller, which\n  is the strongest contract shared with the established sos_57 pattern; the\n  exact per-turn-phase gating is left to the implementer to choose without\n  over-constraining a behavior the engine has no canonical surface for.\n- Stacking/copy identity of the recast (the copy is a distinct object): the\n  engine's copy semantics for free-cast-from-exile are exercised generically by\n  `cast_spell_free`; testing copy-object identity would test the engine, not\n  this card.\n- The interaction of \"any number of spells\" with targeting/legality of the\n  individual exiled spells (those belong to each cast spell's own contract).\n\nAll requirements have at least partial coverage; no `untestable.json` is\nproduced.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":95558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":406,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012rXFMpMiUxgBU3maGZJedn","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"9116fbf2-7b14-4c93-baed-5ffd8a2f0571","request_id":"req_011CbcTVe48L3pUdtvosQxDt","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
