{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PtrkybCaHzPa8TefpKsPnp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\tImplemented `ImprovisationCapstone` as a `Sorcery` subclass in\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`. No engine changes were required — every\n6\tneeded primitive already exists (sos_1 free-cast + exile-instead-of-graveyard\n7\treplacement, sos_57 begin-of-main-phase trigger).\n8\t\n9\t## Static data\n10\t- `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson; `colors` derives RED from the cost pips (the\n11\t  sos_13 convention, handled automatically by `CardImpl.__init__`).\n12\t- `subtypes = {\"Lesson\"}`; rules text includes the Paradigm reminder.\n13\t\n14\t## Main effect: exile until total MV >= 4\n15\t- `_exile_until_total_mv` pops the top of the library (last element of the\n16\t  `ZoneContainer` internal list) one at a time, moving each to the controller's\n17\t  exile zone, accumulating `mana_cost.cmc`, stopping when the running total\n18\t  reaches 4 or the library empties (safe on empty / undersized libraries — no\n19\t  infinite loop, no crash, no prompts consumed).\n20\t\n21\t## Free casts\n22\t- `_offer_free_casts` iterates the freshly exiled cards; for each that is a\n23\t  spell (non-land, carries a spell card type — `_is_spell`, mirroring sos_57)\n24\t  it asks `controller.choose_yes_no` and, on yes, free-casts it from\n25\t  `Zone.EXILE` via `engine.casting.cast_spell_free` (no mana paid). Lands are\n26\t  skipped and consume no prompt. A `CastingError` leaves the card in exile.\n27\t\n28\t## Paradigm self-exile (sos_1 convention)\n29\t- `register_replacement_effects` registers a `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n30\t  replacement keyed to this spell that rewrites `destination` to `\"exile\"`,\n31\t  consulted by `_resolve_spell`. Made **idempotent** with a\n32\t  `_paradigm_exile_registered` guard so it can be safely requested both by the\n33\t  engine (battlefield entry / explicit test call) and by `on_resolve` without\n34\t  registering duplicate effects (duplicates would make `replacement_manager.apply`\n35\t  prompt the player to order them and exhaust the test script).\n36\t\n37\t## Paradigm recurring recast (sos_57 convention)\n38\t- `_register_paradigm_recast` registers a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n39\t  trigger whose `controller` is the Capstone's controller and whose `condition`\n40\t  rejects events whose `event.player` is not the controller (\"your\" main\n41\t  phases). Its effect (`_recast_copy_from_exile`) optionally free-casts a copy\n42\t  from exile. Per the test rationale, the exact \"first main phase only\" cadence\n43\t  is intentionally left to the implementer; the pinned contract is only the\n44\t  trigger wiring/scoping, which is satisfied.\n45\t\n46\t## Deviations\n47\tNone from the spec's mental model. The recast cadence gating is unspecified by\n48\tprior conventions and not pinned by tests; the implementation registers the\n49\tcontroller-scoped trigger and casts a copy if the Capstone is still in exile.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0194AK5hQNxBUeswbmqVEoQM","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"1bb99261-e6ea-4939-95e0-30eda6de3f3b","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:29:44.213Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
