{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CLfw8SQQycGzz1Pxia8XHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019DSdxbAqMmgcSCARMFCkLc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","content":"[\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 235, \"comment\": \"Paradigm recast casts the original spell object (`source`/`self`) from exile via cast_spell_free, not a *copy* as the oracle requires (\\\"cast a copy of it from exile\\\"). Casting the original permanently removes it from exile, so after the first recast the Capstone is no longer in exile and every subsequent first-main-phase trigger finds nothing to cast. To match the oracle this should cast a copy and leave the original in exile (e.g. clone the card and free-cast the clone). Not pinned by tests (which only assert trigger wiring/scoping), so advisory.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 204, \"comment\": \"The recast effect (_recast_copy_from_exile) resolves by casting the Capstone again; when that recast resolves, on_resolve runs again and calls _register_paradigm_recast a second time without any idempotency guard (unlike register_replacement_effects, which has _paradigm_exile_registered). This stacks duplicate BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent registrations on the same source, which would compound over turns and prompt the player to order duplicate triggers. Consider guarding recast-trigger registration the same way the replacement effect is guarded. Currently benign only because casting the original (not a copy) empties exile, masking the duplicate.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 201, \"comment\": \"Oracle text is \\\"the beginning of each of your first main phases\\\" but the condition only checks event.player is controller; it does not restrict to the precombat/first main phase, so it would also fire on the postcombat (second) main phase since BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fires for both. Consider gating on event.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN. Rationale notes this cadence is intentionally unpinned, so advisory.\"}\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":39848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1592,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0194AK5hQNxBUeswbmqVEoQM","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"6afd4e41-fc84-44e9-b3cb-0a194993827d","request_id":"req_011CbcTrktEQ5Sy67PjWukFN","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
