{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bgv2UrfG4jS3XdbjfxhrKw","type":"tool_result","content":"4668:702.94. Miracle\n4669-\n4670:702.94a Miracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability. (See rule 603.11.) “Miracle [cost]” means “You may reveal this card from your hand as you draw it if it’s the first card you’ve drawn this turn. When you reveal this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.”\n4671-\n4672:702.94b If a player chooses to reveal a card using its miracle ability, they play with that card revealed until that card leaves their hand, that ability resolves, or that ability otherwise leaves the stack. (See rule 701.20a.)\n4673-\n4674-702.95. Soulbond\n4675-\n4676-702.95a Soulbond is a keyword that represents two triggered abilities. “Soulbond” means “When this creature enters, if you control both this creature and another creature and both are unpaired, you may pair this creature with another unpaired creature you control for as long as both remain creatures on the battlefield under your control” and “Whenever another creature you control enters, if you control both that creature and this one and both are unpaired, you may pair that creature with this creature for as long as both remain creatures on the battlefield under your control.”\n4677-\n4678-702.95b A creature becomes “paired” with another as the result of a soulbond ability. Abilities may refer to a paired creature, the creature another creature is paired with, or whether a creature is paired. An “unpaired” creature is one that is not paired.\n--\n8312:A keyword ability that lets you cast a spell for a reduced cost if it’s the first card you draw in a turn. See rule 702.94, “Miracle.”\n8313-\n8314-Mobilize\n8315-A keyword ability that creates a number of tapped and attacking red Warrior creature tokens that are sacrificed at the beginning of the next end step. See rule 702.181, “Mobilize.”\n8316-\n8317-Modal, Mode\n8318-A spell or ability is “modal” if it has two or more options in a bulleted list preceded by instructions for a player to choose a number of those options, such as “Choose one —.” See rule 700.2.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAkxZQxxK3TN7Tazw7TR79","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"f9f5252b-8d78-4008-8a04-3509eda58cc9","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:36:03.141Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a3fad967e7e1fd461","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAkxZQxxK3TN7Tazw7TR79","description":"Writing engine/miracle.py","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":100075,"tool_uses":27,"duration_ms":67261},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"94120f46-23a5-4a10-91a1-5a62cff89651","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YAYLzSGSzMRoGM71xZxUqm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KiLZyPL1oASiik2T9vGoy4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/miracle.py","content":"\"\"\"Miracle mechanic support (rule 702.94) — additive engine surface.\n\nMiracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability:\n\n    \"Miracle [cost]\" means \"You may reveal this card from your hand as you\n    draw it if it's the first card you've drawn this turn. When you reveal\n    this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its\n    mana cost.\"\n\nThe engine has no native ``miracle`` keyword (and the :class:`~engine.types.Keyword`\nenum is pinned at 16 members by ``engine_tests/test_types.py``), so miracle is\nsurfaced via a per-card ``miracle_cost`` attribute and a small set of helper\nfunctions here instead of a flag.\n\nContract exposed to cards / tests\n----------------------------------\n\n* :func:`set_miracle_cost` — stamp a :class:`~engine.types.ManaCost` (the\n  miracle/alternative cost) onto a card and mark it ``has_miracle = True``.\n* :func:`clear_miracle_cost` — remove the stamp (used when the granting\n  source leaves the battlefield / the card leaves the hand).\n* :func:`get_miracle_cost` — read the assigned miracle cost (``None`` if the\n  card has no miracle).\n* :func:`is_first_draw_this_turn` — first-card-drawn-this-turn gating, reading\n  the ``player.cards_drawn_this_turn`` counter the draw step maintains.\n* :func:`can_miracle_cast` — ``True`` iff the just-drawn card has a miracle\n  cost AND it is the first card drawn this turn.\n* :func:`offer_miracle` — the draw-time hook: if the card may be miracle-cast\n  and the controller says yes (``choose_yes_no``), cast it for the miracle\n  cost as an alternative cost via :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`.\n\nThe miracle cost is paid as a normal mana cost (just a *different* cost), so\nthe alternative-cost cast path pays from the player's mana pool.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n    from engine.player import Player\n    from engine.types import ManaCost\n\n\n# Attribute name used to stamp the miracle cost onto a card.\n_MIRACLE_COST_ATTR = \"miracle_cost\"\n\n\ndef set_miracle_cost(card: Any, cost: \"ManaCost\") -> None:\n    \"\"\"Assign *cost* as *card*'s miracle (alternative) cost.\n\n    Sets both ``card.miracle_cost`` and a ``card.has_miracle`` boolean flag\n    so callers can detect the grant without a ``None`` comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    setattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, cost)\n    card.has_miracle = True\n\n\ndef clear_miracle_cost(card: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Remove any miracle cost previously assigned to *card*.\"\"\"\n    if hasattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR):\n        try:\n            delattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR)\n        except AttributeError:\n            setattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, None)\n    card.has_miracle = False\n\n\ndef get_miracle_cost(card: Any) -> \"ManaCost | None\":\n    \"\"\"Return *card*'s assigned miracle cost, or ``None`` if it has none.\"\"\"\n    return getattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, None)\n\n\ndef is_first_draw_this_turn(player: \"Player\") -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if at most one card has been drawn by *player* this turn.\n\n    Miracle keys off \"the first card you've drawn this turn\".  The draw helper\n    (:func:`engine.game.draw_card`) increments ``player.cards_drawn_this_turn``\n    *before* firing the draw trigger, so when this is evaluated at draw time the\n    counter reads ``1`` for the first draw of the turn.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = getattr(player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0)\n    return count <= 1\n\n\ndef can_miracle_cast(player: \"Player\", card: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* may be miracle-cast as it is drawn.\n\n    Requires both that *card* carries an assigned miracle cost and that it is\n    the first card *player* has drawn this turn.\n    \"\"\"\n    if get_miracle_cost(card) is None:\n        return False\n    return is_first_draw_this_turn(player)\n\n\ndef offer_miracle(game: \"GameState\", player: \"Player\", card: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Draw-time miracle hook — offer to cast the just-drawn *card* for miracle.\n\n    Returns ``True`` if the card was miracle-cast (put on the stack), ``False``\n    otherwise.  No-op (returns ``False``) when the card has no miracle cost or\n    it is not the first card drawn this turn.\n\n    The optionality is driven by ``player.choose_yes_no`` (the \"you may\"\n    clause).  On a yes, the card is cast for its miracle cost via the\n    alternative-cost cast path.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not can_miracle_cast(player, card):\n        return False\n\n    cost = get_miracle_cost(card)\n    name = getattr(card, \"name\", \"card\")\n    if hasattr(player, \"choose_yes_no\"):\n        if not player.choose_yes_no(f\"Cast {name!r} for its miracle cost?\"):\n            return False\n\n    from engine.casting import cast_spell_alternative, CastingError\n\n    try:\n        cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, cost)\n    except CastingError:\n        return False\n    return True\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":901,"cache_read_input_tokens":98986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":901,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAkxZQxxK3TN7Tazw7TR79","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"68be2d6c-59eb-4b77-b31f-2b324d0543be","request_id":"req_011CbcUGygqW2oqsmeUDtnLi","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
