ert): /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md\n\nCOORDINATOR DIRECTIVES (read and follow): /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md\nThe Tester escalated the miracle mechanic as untestable (no engine surface). You must implement the FULL card plus an additive miracle engine surface and expose a testable contract. After you finish, the Tester will be re-invoked.\n\nKEY CONTRACTS THE TESTS ASSERT (must satisfy):\n- Miracle cost surface: tests accept EITHER a `miracle_cost(game, card)` method on Lorehold OR a per-card `miracle_cost` attribute reporting {2} for the controller's hand instants/sorceries (and NOT creatures / opponents' hands). Support that.\n- Upkeep trigger: BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent carries NO player field — the condition must read `game.active_player`; fire only on an OPPONENT's upkeep, controller = Lorehold's controller.\n- Loot effect resolution via choose_yes_no + choose_card; conditional draw only when a card was discarded; empty hand = no draw.\n\nREFERENCES (read for API discovery — rich docstrings):\n- engine/card.py, engine/events.py, engine/triggers.py, engine/zones.py, engine/casting.py, engine/game.py (draw_card, cards_drawn_this_turn tracking), engine/continuous_effects.py (for the in-hand miracle grant), engine/types.py\n- KEY_DECISIONS.md conventions: card colors (sos_13), free-cast pipeline (sos_1). FDN cards for Flying/Haste creatures, upkeep triggers, and any draw/loot effects.\n- RULEBOOK.txt (grep, don't read whole) for Miracle (702.94), \"first card you drew this turn\".\n\nENGINE RULES (from AGENTS.md):\n- Additive only: may add methods/classes/helpers/files, modify existing function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; MUST NOT break engine_tests pinned counts (engine_tests/test_types.py pins len(Keyword)==16 — do NOT add a Keyword member if it breaks that); MUST NOT modify test files.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Read spec, test file, rationale, directives.\n2. Implement the card so ALL tests in tests.py pass, plus the full miracle mechanic with a testable contract (first-card-drawn-this-turn alternative {2} cost).\n3. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, `pytest cards/fdn/` to confirm nothing breaks.\n4. If a test is genuinely WRONG, do NOT modify it — return DISPUTE with details.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Implementation to /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py (+ engine changes).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff — `git diff` of all changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md — what you did, the EXACT miracle contracts exposed (miracle cost accessor, draw-time cast API, first-draw gating), the in-hand grant mechanism, engine changes, any spec deviations.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-files.txt — modified files.\n- Upsert this card's entry into /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json (match by card: \"sos_201\"). Keep other entries intact.\n\nReturn either IMPL_DONE (files_changed, tests_passing, diff_path, rationale_path, notes) or DISPUTE (tests_failing, disputed_tests, dispute_path, notes) exactly as specified.","agentId":"a3fad967e7e1fd461","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All passing. Implementation complete.\n\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: 5\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: Implemented Lorehold (5/5 flying/haste, miracle_cost {2} grant scoped to controller-hand instants/sorceries, opponent-upkeep discard-then-draw loot trigger) plus an additive miracle engine surface — engine/miracle.py (set/get miracle cost, first-draw gating, offer_miracle), engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative (alternative-cost cast), draw_card miracle hook, and a per-turn cards_drawn_this_turn reset at untap. 25/25 card tests pass; 1184 engine+FDN and 192 SOS tests still green; Keyword pin (16) intact."}],"totalDurationMs":260759,"totalTokens":119152,"totalToolUseCount":48,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,