{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019c8Jk6WJ4qT2VctccwZ3XZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — sos_201, Lorehold, the Historian\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\t`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`.\n5\t\n6\t- Static: `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n7\t  keywords exactly `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, colors derived from the mana\n8\t  cost (`{R}{W}` → `{RED, WHITE}`).\n9\t- All 25 tests in `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` pass; engine_tests (incl. the\n10\t  pinned `len(Keyword)==16`) and all FDN/SOS tests pass (1184 + 192).\n11\t\n12\t## Miracle contract (the new mechanic)\n13\t\n14\tMiracle is NOT a Keyword enum member (the enum is pinned at 16). It is surfaced\n15\tvia a per-card attribute plus a small additive engine module.\n16\t\n17\t### Miracle cost accessor (what the tests probe)\n18\t`LoreholdTheHistorian.miracle_cost(game, card) -> ManaCost | None`:\n19\t- Returns `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` for an instant/sorcery card in the\n20\t  controller's hand while Lorehold is in play.\n21\t- Returns `None` for non-instant/sorcery cards and for cards in any other\n22\t  player's hand (\"in YOUR hand\" scoping). Scoping is by card type\n23\t  (`CardType.INSTANT`/`SORCERY`) and by `game.get_hand(controller).contains(card)`.\n24\t- As a side effect it stamps the engine-level `card.miracle_cost` attribute\n25\t  (and `card.has_miracle = True`) on qualifying cards via\n26\t  `engine.miracle.set_miracle_cost`, so the draw-time hook can fire. The test\n27\t  helper accepts either the method or the attribute; both report `{2}`.\n28\t- `apply_miracle_grant(game)` is a convenience that stamps the whole hand at once.\n29\t\n30\t### Engine miracle surface — `engine/miracle.py` (new, additive)\n31\t- `set_miracle_cost(card, cost)` / `clear_miracle_cost(card)` / `get_miracle_cost(card)`\n32\t  — stamp/read the alternative cost (`card.miracle_cost` + `card.has_miracle`).\n33\t- `is_first_draw_this_turn(player)` — first-card gating; reads\n34\t  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (the counter `engine.game.draw_card` already\n35\t  maintains). Returns `count <= 1` because `draw_card` increments the counter\n36\t  BEFORE the miracle is offered, so the first draw reads `1`.\n37\t- `can_miracle_cast(player, card)` — `True` iff the card has a miracle cost AND\n38\t  it is the first card drawn this turn.\n39\t- `offer_miracle(game, player, card)` — draw-time hook: if `can_miracle_cast`\n40\t  and the controller answers `choose_yes_no` yes, the card is cast for its\n41\t  miracle cost via `cast_spell_alternative`. Returns whether it was cast.\n42\t\n43\t### Draw-time cast API — `engine/casting.cast_spell_alternative` (new, additive)\n44\t`cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, alternative_cost, from_zone=HAND)`:\n45\t- Mirrors the normal cast pipeline (can_cast, target choice/validation +\n46\t  protection, mana payment with rollback, `on_cast`, push resolving StackObject)\n47\t  but pays `alternative_cost` from the mana pool instead of `card.mana_cost`, and\n48\t  skips the sorcery/instant timing check (miracle casts happen at draw time).\n49\t\n50\t### First-draw gating wiring\n51\t- `engine/game.draw_card`: after firing the draw trigger, if the drawn card has\n52\t  an assigned miracle cost, call `offer_miracle`. No-op for cards without a\n53\t  miracle cost, so existing behaviour is unchanged.\n54\t- `engine/turn._do_untap_step`: resets `player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for all\n55\t  players each untap so the \"first card this turn\" gate resets per turn. (The\n56\t  counter was previously incremented but never reset.)\n57\t\n58\tVerified manually: with a miracle-stamped instant on top of the library and {2}\n59\tavailable, drawing it as the FIRST draw of the turn puts it on the stack; drawing\n60\tit when it is NOT the first draw leaves the stack empty (no miracle cast).\n61\t\n62\t## Opponent-upkeep loot trigger\n63\t`register_triggers` registers exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\n64\ttrigger, controller = Lorehold's controller. The event carries no player field,\n65\tso the condition reads `game.active_player` and returns\n66\t`game.active_player is not controller` (fires only on an opponent's upkeep).\n67\t\n68\tEffect `_loot(game, controller)`:\n69\t- `choose_yes_no` drives the optional \"you may\"; on no, nothing happens.\n70\t- `choose_card` selects the discard; `engine.game.discard` moves it to the\n71\t  graveyard, then `engine.game.draw_card` draws (\"If you do\").\n72\t- Empty hand → returns before any prompt (no discard possible ⇒ no draw),\n73\t  matching `test_empty_hand_does_not_draw`.\n74\t\n75\t## Deviations / notes\n76\t- No spec deviations. Miracle reminder text matches the oracle text.\n77\t- Conventions established for future cards: alternative-cost casts go through\n78\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`; miracle is modelled via\n79\t  `engine/miracle.py` helpers + a `card.miracle_cost` attribute (no Keyword\n80\t  member); `cards_drawn_this_turn` now resets at untap.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"5417e5b0-f1e9-4193-a026-1a0c4a870d87","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:39:43.185Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_201, Lorehold, the Historian\n\n## Card\n`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`.\n\n- Static: `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n  keywords exactly `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, colors derived from the mana\n  cost (`{R}{W}` → `{RED, WHITE}`).\n- All 25 tests in `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` pass; engine_tests (incl. the\n  pinned `len(Keyword)==16`) and all FDN/SOS tests pass (1184 + 192).\n\n## Miracle contract (the new mechanic)\n\nMiracle is NOT a Keyword enum member (the enum is pinned at 16). It is surfaced\nvia a per-card attribute plus a small additive engine module.\n\n### Miracle cost accessor (what the tests probe)\n`LoreholdTheHistorian.miracle_cost(game, card) -> ManaCost | None`:\n- Returns `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` for an instant/sorcery card in the\n  controller's hand while Lorehold is in play.\n- Returns `None` for non-instant/sorcery cards and for cards in any other\n  player's hand (\"in YOUR hand\" scoping). Scoping is by card type\n  (`CardType.INSTANT`/`SORCERY`) and by `game.get_hand(controller).contains(card)`.\n- As a side effect it stamps the engine-level `card.miracle_cost` attribute\n  (and `card.has_miracle = True`) on qualifying cards via\n  `engine.miracle.set_miracle_cost`, so the draw-time hook can fire. The test\n  helper accepts either the method or the attribute; both report `{2}`.\n- `apply_miracle_grant(game)` is a convenience that stamps the whole hand at once.\n\n### Engine miracle surface — `engine/miracle.py` (new, additive)\n- `set_miracle_cost(card, cost)` / `clear_miracle_cost(card)` / `get_miracle_cost(card)`\n  — stamp/read the alternative cost (`card.miracle_cost` + `card.has_miracle`).\n- `is_first_draw_this_turn(player)` — first-card gating; reads\n  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (the counter `engine.game.draw_card` already\n  maintains). Returns `count <= 1` because `draw_card` increments the counter\n  BEFORE the miracle is offered, so the first draw reads `1`.\n- `can_miracle_cast(player, card)` — `True` iff the card has a miracle cost AND\n  it is the first card drawn this turn.\n- `offer_miracle(game, player, card)` — draw-time hook: if `can_miracle_cast`\n  and the controller answers `choose_yes_no` yes, the card is cast for its\n  miracle cost via `cast_spell_alternative`. Returns whether it was cast.\n\n### Draw-time cast API — `engine/casting.cast_spell_alternative` (new, additive)\n`cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, alternative_cost, from_zone=HAND)`:\n- Mirrors the normal cast pipeline (can_cast, target choice/validation +\n  protection, mana payment with rollback, `on_cast`, push resolving StackObject)\n  but pays `alternative_cost` from the mana pool instead of `card.mana_cost`, and\n  skips the sorcery/instant timing check (miracle casts happen at draw time).\n\n### First-draw gating wiring\n- `engine/game.draw_card`: after firing the draw trigger, if the drawn card has\n  an assigned miracle cost, call `offer_miracle`. No-op for cards without a\n  miracle cost, so existing behaviour is unchanged.\n- `engine/turn._do_untap_step`: resets `player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for all\n  players each untap so the \"first card this turn\" gate resets per turn. (The\n  counter was previously incremented but never reset.)\n\nVerified manually: with a miracle-stamped instant on top of the library and {2}\navailable, drawing it as the FIRST draw of the turn puts it on the stack; drawing\nit when it is NOT the first draw leaves the stack empty (no miracle cast).\n\n## Opponent-upkeep loot trigger\n`register_triggers` registers exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\ntrigger, controller = Lorehold's controller. The event carries no player field,\nso the condition reads `game.active_player` and returns\n`game.active_player is not controller` (fires only on an opponent's upkeep).\n\nEffect `_loot(game, controller)`:\n- `choose_yes_no` drives the optional \"you may\"; on no, nothing happens.\n- `choose_card` selects the discard; `engine.game.discard` moves it to the\n  graveyard, then `engine.game.draw_card` draws (\"If you do\").\n- Empty hand → returns before any prompt (no discard possible ⇒ no draw),\n  matching `test_empty_hand_does_not_draw`.\n\n## Deviations / notes\n- No spec deviations. Miracle reminder text matches the oracle text.\n- Conventions established for future cards: alternative-cost casts go through\n  `engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`; miracle is modelled via\n  `engine/miracle.py` helpers + a `card.miracle_cost` attribute (no Keyword\n  member); `cards_drawn_this_turn` now resets at untap.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
