{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7ZLuCRk4bSXtgtU6UPFCn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — SOS 201, Lorehold, the Historian\n2\t\n3\tCard: `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5.\n4\t\n5\tOracle text:\n6\t- Flying, haste\n7\t- Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\n8\t- At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\n9\t\n10\t## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n11\t\n12\t25 tests across five classes. TDD red phase: the stub is empty, so the\n13\tpositive-assertion tests fail until implemented. Three negative-scoping tests\n14\tpass against the empty stub (they guard against over-broad behaviour) but stay\n15\tmeaningful once the grant/trigger exists.\n16\t\n17\t### TestLoreholdProperties (static data)\n18\t- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` with `CardType.CREATURE`.\n19\t- `test_name` / `test_mana_cost` / `test_power_toughness` — name, `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5.\n20\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n21\t- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both `Elder` and `Dragon`.\n22\t- `test_colors_are_red_and_white` — `colors == {RED, WHITE}` (spec colors).\n23\t- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_haste` — both keywords present.\n24\t- `test_no_extraneous_keywords` — keyword set is exactly Flying|Haste (no over-grant).\n25\t\n26\t### TestLoreholdMiracleGrant (miracle {2} on hand instants/sorceries)\n27\tProbes the observable miracle-cost surface (a `miracle_cost(game, card)` method\n28\ton Lorehold, or a per-card `miracle_cost` attribute — helper accepts either):\n29\t- `test_hand_instant_has_miracle_two` — a hand instant reports miracle `{2}`.\n30\t- `test_hand_sorcery_has_miracle_two` — a hand sorcery reports miracle `{2}`.\n31\t- `test_hand_creature_does_not_get_miracle` — creatures are unaffected (scoping).\n32\t- `test_opponent_hand_instant_does_not_get_miracle` — \"in YOUR hand\": an\n33\t  opponent's instant is unaffected (scoping).\n34\t\n35\tThe deeper requirement — actually casting a drawn card for its {2} miracle cost\n36\tonly when it's the first card drawn this turn — is recorded in `untestable.json`\n37\tbecause the engine has no miracle/draw-step surface to exercise it.\n38\t\n39\t### TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerRegistration (trigger wiring)\n40\t- `test_registers_one_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds exactly one trigger.\n41\t- `test_trigger_watches_upkeep_event` — it watches `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n42\t- `test_trigger_controller_is_card_controller` — controller is Lorehold's controller.\n43\t- `test_trigger_fires_on_opponents_upkeep` — condition true when the active\n44\t  player (whose upkeep it is) is an opponent. `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\n45\t  carries no `player` field, so the condition must read `game.active_player`.\n46\t- `test_trigger_does_not_fire_on_own_upkeep` — condition false on the\n47\t  controller's own upkeep (\"each OPPONENT's upkeep\"). Both condition tests\n48\t  reject a condition-less (always-fire) trigger as incorrect.\n49\t\n50\t### TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerFires (trigger firing onto the stack)\n51\t- `test_opponent_upkeep_event_pushes_trigger` — firing on the opponent's upkeep\n52\t  pushes the trigger onto the stack.\n53\t- `test_own_upkeep_event_does_not_push_trigger` — firing on the controller's\n54\t  upkeep pushes nothing (scoping guard; passes against the empty stub).\n55\t\n56\t### TestLoreholdLootEffect (discard-then-draw resolution)\n57\tDrives optionality via `choose_yes_no` and the discarded card via `choose_card`\n58\t(DeterministicPlayer script), resolving the trigger StackObject directly:\n59\t- `test_yes_discards_chosen_card_and_draws` — \"yes\" discards the chosen card to\n60\t  the graveyard and then draws the top library card.\n61\t- `test_yes_is_net_neutral_hand_size` — discard one + draw one ⇒ hand size unchanged.\n62\t- `test_no_does_not_discard_or_draw` — \"you may\"/decline: hand and library untouched.\n63\t- `test_empty_hand_does_not_draw` — \"If you do\": with no card to discard, the\n64\t  conditional draw must not happen.\n65\t\n66\t## Edge cases covered\n67\t- Keyword scoping (exactly Flying|Haste, no extras).\n68\t- Miracle scoping by card type (only instant/sorcery) and zone owner (\"your hand\").\n69\t- Upkeep-trigger scoping (opponents only, not the controller's own upkeep) at\n70\t  both the condition level and the fire-onto-stack level.\n71\t- The conditional nature of the loot (\"you may\", \"if you do\"): yes-path,\n72\t  no-path, and empty-hand path.\n73\t\n74\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n75\t- Actual miracle casting at draw time (first-card-drawn-this-turn alternative\n76\t  cost): no engine surface — see `untestable.json`.\n77\t- Legend rule for a second Lorehold, summoning-sickness interaction with haste,\n78\t  and combat flying evasion: these are generic engine behaviours covered by\n79\t  `engine_tests/`, not card-specific to SOS 201.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019Mbmw3oikAhHtz8Xfv7wgN","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"eb933b8d-85f7-4c8a-b773-030ab695b83c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:41:14.906Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_201"}
