{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011satGpg1UdWh4Agqu5TV8D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The engine has no native 'miracle' mechanic: there is no draw-step hook that offers an alternative miracle cost for the first card drawn each turn, and no Keyword/ability surface that represents miracle. The tests can assert that Lorehold reports a {2} miracle cost for the controller's hand instants/sorceries (and not for creatures or opponents' hands), but the actual behaviour -- being able to cast such a card for {2} when it is the first card drawn this turn, and only then -- cannot be exercised through real engine APIs.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine 'miracle' surface: e.g. a draw-step interaction that, when a card has an assigned miracle cost and is the first card drawn this turn (player.cards_drawn_this_turn tracking already exists), offers a free/alternative-cost cast for the miracle cost. The Implementer would then expose how Lorehold assigns miracle {2} to the controller's hand instants/sorceries, and a test could draw a card on the controller's turn and assert it may be cast for {2}.\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019Mbmw3oikAhHtz8Xfv7wgN","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"34fa1008-8d78-487c-adfe-19b90a8ed5b2","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:41:15.094Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_201"}
