 trigger: BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent, controller-owned, fires only on an OPPONENT's upkeep (reads game.active_player); optional discard; conditional draw only if a card was discarded; empty hand = no draw.\n- ENGINE CHANGES — scrutinize for safety/regressions:\n  * engine/miracle.py (new module) — set/get miracle cost, first-draw gating logic (is_first_draw_this_turn returns count <= 1 because draw_card increments BEFORE offering — verify this is correct and not off-by-one), offer_miracle.\n  * engine/casting.py cast_spell_alternative — pays an alternative cost; mana rollback on failure; skips timing check. Any bugs (e.g. fails to clean up on payment failure, leaves card in wrong zone)?\n  * engine/game.py draw_card — new miracle hook; confirm it's a no-op for non-miracle cards (no regression).\n  * engine/turn.py untap step — now resets player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0 for all players. Is this safe? Does any existing engine behavior depend on the counter NOT being reset? (Tests pass, but reason about it.)\n- Do NOT flag earlier-card patterns or KEY_DECISIONS.md conventions. Do NOT demand test rewrites — advisory only for test quality.\n- Note: miracle is intentionally NOT a Keyword enum member (engine_tests pins count). Do not flag that.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Write /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json — JSON array of {\"severity\":\"strict\"|\"advisory\",\"file\",\"line\",\"comment\"}. Empty array [] if none.\n\nReturn:\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json","agentId":"aadcd7346726ae404","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 2\nadvisory_count: 2\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":90597,"totalTokens":52361,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1700,"cache_read_input_tokens":50606,"output_tokens":53,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servi