{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019w35wGueRp37ni9PnR69St","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both strict issues are valid: the draw-time miracle never fires on a naturally-drawn card (the grant only stamps cards already in hand), and the stamp is sticky/never cleared. These are real correctness bugs. Siding with the Reviewer — directing a revision to derive the miracle grant dynamically at draw time."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":110872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1329},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"e01bdf98-5517-44e4-9540-b16fd7205fd2","request_id":"req_011CbcUrsM35RBDAdmHGZzhX"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019w35wGueRp37ni9PnR69St","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QajJUa79G9Z52zNRAZM6nC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (revision round)\n\nTwo STRICT review findings must be fixed. The coordinator sides with the Reviewer.\n\n## STRICT 1 — draw-time miracle must fire on naturally-drawn cards\nCurrently the miracle grant only stamps cards ALREADY in the controller's hand,\nbut `engine.game.draw_card` reads the stamp off the card just drawn from the\nLIBRARY (never stamped), so miracle never fires in real gameplay — it only works\nbecause the tests pre-stamp the top library card.\n\nFix: make the draw-time miracle offer DYNAMICALLY derive the miracle cost for the\ncard being drawn, rather than relying solely on a pre-applied sticky stamp. At\ndraw time, determine whether any active \"miracle granter\" applies to the drawn\ncard — e.g. a Lorehold on the battlefield grants miracle {2} to instant/sorcery\ncards drawn by ITS controller. So when the controller naturally draws an\ninstant/sorcery as their first draw of the turn (with Lorehold in play), the\nmiracle cast is offered for {2} with NO manual pre-stamping required.\n\nSuggested approach: have the draw-time hook query active grants (e.g. iterate\nthe drawer's battlefield for permanents exposing a miracle-grant, like Lorehold's\n`miracle_cost`/grant API) and compute the cost for the just-drawn card, instead\nof only reading `get_miracle_cost(card)`. You may keep honoring an explicit stamp\nfor backward compatibility, but the natural-draw path MUST work without it.\n\n## STRICT 2 — miracle grant must not be permanent/sticky\nThe stamp set by `set_miracle_cost` is never cleared (`clear_miracle_cost` has no\ncall sites). After Lorehold leaves play, or after the card leaves the controller's\nhand, the grant should no longer apply. A previously-stamped card drawn later when\nLorehold is gone must NOT offer a miracle cast.\n\nFix: derive the grant dynamically (preferred — solving STRICT 1 this way also\nsolves this), OR clear the stamp when the grant no longer applies. The\ncorrectness contract: miracle {2} applies iff a granter (Lorehold) is currently\nin play and the drawn card is an instant/sorcery being drawn by the granter's\ncontroller.\n\n## Constraints\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file (including the existing pre-stamping test\n  helper). ALL existing 31 tests must still pass — the dynamic path must cover\n  the test scenarios (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand\n  instant/sorcery), and explicitly-stamped cards must continue to work.\n- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep Keyword count = 16.\n- Address the two advisories at your discretion (docstring note on cost reduction\n  not applying to the alternative cost; the untap reset semantics note).\n\nRun `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all must pass.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":110872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1329},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"46cb4602-3450-4553-9598-49a7e1583d00","request_id":"req_011CbcUrsM35RBDAdmHGZzhX"}
