w path MUST work without it.\n\n## STRICT 2 — miracle grant must not be permanent/sticky\nThe stamp set by `set_miracle_cost` is never cleared (`clear_miracle_cost` has no\ncall sites). After Lorehold leaves play, or after the card leaves the controller's\nhand, the grant should no longer apply. A previously-stamped card drawn later when\nLorehold is gone must NOT offer a miracle cast.\n\nFix: derive the grant dynamically (preferred — solving STRICT 1 this way also\nsolves this), OR clear the stamp when the grant no longer applies. The\ncorrectness contract: miracle {2} applies iff a granter (Lorehold) is currently\nin play and the drawn card is an instant/sorcery being drawn by the granter's\ncontroller.\n\n## Constraints\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file (including the existing pre-stamping test\n  helper). ALL existing 31 tests must still pass — the dynamic path must cover\n  the test scenarios (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand\n  instant/sorcery), and explicitly-stamped cards must continue to work.\n- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep Keyword count = 16.\n- Address the two advisories at your discretion (docstring note on cost reduction\n  not applying to the alternative cost; the untap reset semantics note).\n\nRun `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all must pass.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":46,"newStart":1,"newLines":46,"lines":["-# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (initial implementation)","+# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (revision round)"," ","-Card: **Lorehold, the Historian** — `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon,","-5/5, Flying, Haste.","-- \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"","-- \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do,","-  draw a card.\"","+Two STRICT review findings must be fixed. The coordinator sides with the Reviewer."," ","-The Tester escalated the **miracle** mechanic as untestable — the engine has no","-miracle surface. Engine changes are allowed and expected. Implement the FULL card","-plus an additive miracle engine surface, and expose a testable contract. After you","-finish, the Tester will be re-invoked.","+## STRICT 1 — draw-time miracle must fire on naturally-drawn cards","+Currently the miracle grant only stamps cards ALREADY in the controller's hand,","+but `engine.game.draw_card` reads the stamp off the card just drawn from the","+LIBRARY (never stamped), so miracle never fires in real gameplay — it only works","+because the tests pre-stamp the top library card."," ","-## Requirements to implement fully","-1. **Static**: 5/5, Flying, Haste, Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {RED, WHITE}.","-2. **Miracle grant**: while Lorehold is on the battlefield, each instant/sorcery","-   card in ITS CONTROLLER's hand has miracle {2}. Scope strictly to the","-   controller's hand and to instant/sorcery cards (not creatures, not opponents'","-   hands). Expose the miracle cost via a queryable surface — the tests accept","-   either a `miracle_cost(game, card)` method on Lorehold OR a per-card","-   `miracle_cost` attribute. Support that contract.","-3. **Each opponent's upkeep loot**: a trigger on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`","-   (which carries no player field — read `game.active_player` in the condition),","-   controller = Lorehold's controller, firing only when the upkeep belongs to an","-   opponent (not the controller's own). Effect: \"you may discard a card; if you","-   do, draw a card\" — optional via `choose_yes_no`, discard via `choose_card`,","-   conditional draw only when a card was actually discarded; empty hand = no draw.","+Fix: make the draw-time miracle offer DYNAMICALLY derive the miracle cost for the","+card being drawn, rather than relying solely on a pre-applied sticky stamp. At","+draw time, determine whether any active \"miracle granter\" applies to the drawn","+card — e.g. a Lorehold on the battlefield grants miracle {2} to instant/sorcery","+cards drawn by ITS controller. So when the controller naturally draws an","+instant/sorcery as their first draw of the turn (with Lorehold in play), the","+miracle cast is offered for {2} with NO manual pre-stamping required."," ","-## Engine support to add for miracle (additive only)","-- Add a **miracle** surface to the engine: when a player draws a card and it is","-  the FIRST card drawn this turn, if that card has an assigned miracle cost, the","-  player may cast it for its miracle cost (an alternative cost). Reuse the","-  existing `cards_drawn_this_turn` tracking the Tester noted already exists","-  (verify the exact attribute in engine source). Model it consistent with the","-  engine's draw / casting conventions (e.g. a draw hook + an alternative-cost","-  cast path). Do NOT add a Keyword enum member if it breaks the pinned","-  `len(Keyword)==16` test in engine_tests/test_types.py — surface miracle via an","-  attribute/method + rules text instead.","-- Expose enough contract that a test can: with Lorehold in play, draw an","-  instant/sorcery on the controller's turn as the FIRST draw, and assert it may","-  be cast for {2}; and that it may NOT be cast for {2} when it's not the first","-  draw of the turn.","+Suggested approach: have the draw-time hook query active grants (e.g. iterate","+the drawer's battlefield for permanents exposing a miracle-grant, like Lorehold's","+`miracle_cost`/grant API) and compute the cost for the just-drawn card, instead","+of only reading `get_miracle_cost(card)`. You may keep honoring an explicit stamp","+for backward compatibility, but the natural-draw path MUST work without it."," ","-Document the exact contracts (miracle cost accessor, draw-time cast API, the","-first-draw gating) in your rationale so the Tester can assert against it.","-Do NOT stub miracle out — the grader's authoritative tests will exercise it.","+## STRICT 2 — miracle grant must not be permanent/sticky","+The stamp set by `set_miracle_cost` is never cleared (`clear_miracle_cost` has no","+call sites). After Lorehold leaves play, or after the card leaves the controller's","+hand, the grant should no longer apply. A previously-stamped card drawn later when","+Lorehold is gone must NOT offer a miracle cast.","+","+Fix: derive the grant dynamically (preferred — solving STRICT 1 this way also","+solves this), OR clear the stamp when the grant no longer applies. The","+correctness contract: miracle {2} applies iff a granter (Lorehold) is currently","+in play and the drawn card is an instant/sorcery being drawn by the granter's","+controller.","+","+## Constraints","+- You MUST NOT modify any test file (including the existing pre-stamping test","+  helper). ALL existing 31 tests must still pass — the dynamic path must cover","+  the test scenarios (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand","+  instant/sorcery), and explicitly-stamped cards must continue to work.","+- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep Keyword count = 16.","+- Address the two advisories at your discretion (docstring note on cost reduction","+  not applying to the alternative cost; the untap reset semantics note).","+","+Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all must pass."]}],"originalFile":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (initial implementation)\n\nCard: **Lorehold, the Historian** — `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon,\n5/5, Flying, Haste.\n- \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n- \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do,\n  draw a card.\"\n\nThe Tester escalated the **miracle** mechanic as untestable — the engine has no\nmiracle surface. Engine changes are allowed and expected. Implement the FULL card\nplus an additive miracle engine surface, and expose a testable contract. After you\nfinish, the Tester will be re-invoked.\n\n## Requirements to implement fully\n1. **Static**: 5/5, Flying, Haste, Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {RED, WHITE}.\n2. **Miracle grant**: while Lorehold is on the battlefield, each instant/sorcery\n   card in ITS CONTROLLER's hand has miracle {2}. Scope strictly to the\n   controller's hand and to instant/sorcery cards (not creatures, not opponents'\n   hands). Expose the miracle cost via a queryable surface — the tests accept\n   either a `miracle_cost(game, card)` method on Lorehold OR a per-card\n   `miracle_cost` attribute. Support that contract.\n3. **Each opponent's upkeep loot**: a trigger on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\n   (which carries no player field — read `game.active_player` in the condition),\n   controller = Lorehold's controller, firing only when the upkeep belongs to an\n   opponent (not the controller's own). Effect: \"you may discard a card; if you\n   do, draw a card\" — optional via `choose_yes_no`, discard via `choose_card`,\n   conditional draw only when a card was actually discarded; empty hand = no draw.\n\n## Engine support to add for miracle (additive only)\n- Add a **miracle** surface to the engine: when a player draws a card and it is\n  the FIRST card drawn this turn, if that card has an assigned miracle cost, the\n  player may cast it for its miracle cost (an alternative cost). Reuse the\n  existing `cards_drawn_this_turn` tracking the Tester noted already exists\n  (verify the exact attribute in engine source). Model it consistent with the\n  engine's draw / casting conventions (e.g. a draw hook + an alternative-cost\n  cast path). Do NOT add a Keyword enum member if it breaks the pinned\n  `len(Keyword)==16` test in engine_tests/test_types.py — surface miracle via an\n  attribute/method + rules text instead.\n- Expose enough contract that a test can: with Lorehold in play, draw an\n  instant/sorcery on the controller's turn as the FIRST draw, and assert it may\n  be cast for {2}; and that it may NOT be cast for {2} when it's not the first\n  draw of the turn.\n\nDocument the exact contracts (miracle cost accessor, draw-time cast API, the\nfirst-draw gating) in your rationale so the Tester can assert against it.\nDo NOT stub miracle out — the grader's authoritative tests will exercise it.\n","userModified":false}}
