ill pass (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand instant/sorcery; explicitly pre-stamped cards must continue to work too — keep honoring an explicit stamp for backward compat while adding the dynamic path).\n- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep len(Keyword)==16.\n- You MAY also apply the two advisories (docstring note that cost reduction is intentionally not applied to the alternative cost; the untap-reset semantics note).\n- If you DISAGREE with a strict comment, do NOT silently skip it — record reasoning in disagreements.json.\n\nVERIFY: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, `pytest cards/fdn/` — all must pass. Also manually verify: with Lorehold in play and an UNSTAMPED instant on top of the controller's library, the controller's first draw of the turn offers the {2} miracle cast; and with Lorehold NOT in play, a previously-stamped card drawn later does NOT offer miracle.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Updated /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py and engine changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff — `git diff` of ALL current changes (cumulative).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised-rationale.md — what you changed, how the dynamic grant works, and confirm both manual checks + all tests pass.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json — JSON array of {review_comment_index, reviewer_comment, implementer_justification}. Empty array [] if you applied everything.\n- Update this card's entry in /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json if the modified-file set changed.\n\nReturn:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2198,"cache_read_input_tokens":112201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_