{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011QYEzsHmHCZJCCCt6jSJ4L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CdABVsoGwK6gfR3X4v3Rr5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1562,"cache_read_input_tokens":11605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1562,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015Db1w2LmRhkJgHeDaM9a5T","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"e5914258-11a5-4c43-8f87-37ef42eb39db","request_id":"req_011CbcUv6hHyTrQgZ8MhsfAJ","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_201 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CdABVsoGwK6gfR3X4v3Rr5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (revision round)\n2\t\n3\tTwo STRICT review findings must be fixed. The coordinator sides with the Reviewer.\n4\t\n5\t## STRICT 1 — draw-time miracle must fire on naturally-drawn cards\n6\tCurrently the miracle grant only stamps cards ALREADY in the controller's hand,\n7\tbut `engine.game.draw_card` reads the stamp off the card just drawn from the\n8\tLIBRARY (never stamped), so miracle never fires in real gameplay — it only works\n9\tbecause the tests pre-stamp the top library card.\n10\t\n11\tFix: make the draw-time miracle offer DYNAMICALLY derive the miracle cost for the\n12\tcard being drawn, rather than relying solely on a pre-applied sticky stamp. At\n13\tdraw time, determine whether any active \"miracle granter\" applies to the drawn\n14\tcard — e.g. a Lorehold on the battlefield grants miracle {2} to instant/sorcery\n15\tcards drawn by ITS controller. So when the controller naturally draws an\n16\tinstant/sorcery as their first draw of the turn (with Lorehold in play), the\n17\tmiracle cast is offered for {2} with NO manual pre-stamping required.\n18\t\n19\tSuggested approach: have the draw-time hook query active grants (e.g. iterate\n20\tthe drawer's battlefield for permanents exposing a miracle-grant, like Lorehold's\n21\t`miracle_cost`/grant API) and compute the cost for the just-drawn card, instead\n22\tof only reading `get_miracle_cost(card)`. You may keep honoring an explicit stamp\n23\tfor backward compatibility, but the natural-draw path MUST work without it.\n24\t\n25\t## STRICT 2 — miracle grant must not be permanent/sticky\n26\tThe stamp set by `set_miracle_cost` is never cleared (`clear_miracle_cost` has no\n27\tcall sites). After Lorehold leaves play, or after the card leaves the controller's\n28\thand, the grant should no longer apply. A previously-stamped card drawn later when\n29\tLorehold is gone must NOT offer a miracle cast.\n30\t\n31\tFix: derive the grant dynamically (preferred — solving STRICT 1 this way also\n32\tsolves this), OR clear the stamp when the grant no longer applies. The\n33\tcorrectness contract: miracle {2} applies iff a granter (Lorehold) is currently\n34\tin play and the drawn card is an instant/sorcery being drawn by the granter's\n35\tcontroller.\n36\t\n37\t## Constraints\n38\t- You MUST NOT modify any test file (including the existing pre-stamping test\n39\t  helper). ALL existing 31 tests must still pass — the dynamic path must cover\n40\t  the test scenarios (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand\n41\t  instant/sorcery), and explicitly-stamped cards must continue to work.\n42\t- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep Keyword count = 16.\n43\t- Address the two advisories at your discretion (docstring note on cost reduction\n44\t  not applying to the alternative cost; the untap reset semantics note).\n45\t\n46\tRun `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ cards/fdn/` — all must pass.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015Db1w2LmRhkJgHeDaM9a5T","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"75c68f85-7ea0-4d18-af74-14fea5d8f522","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:44:30.225Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_201 implementation"}
