{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Db1w2LmRhkJgHeDaM9a5T","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 1215 tests pass (31 sos_201 + engine_tests + fdn). Both manual verification checks confirmed.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json\n\nSummary of what changed:\n- STRICT 1: Added `engine.miracle.derive_miracle_cost(game, player, card)` which iterates the drawer's battlefield and asks each permanent exposing a callable `miracle_cost(game, card)` grant (e.g. Lorehold) for the just-drawn card's cost. `engine/game.py draw_card` now calls `offer_miracle` unconditionally, and `offer_miracle` derives the cost dynamically — so a naturally-drawn, unstamped instant/sorcery fires the `{2}` offer with no pre-stamping.\n- STRICT 2: The dynamic deriver is authoritative every draw — when no granter applies it clears any stale stamp via `clear_miracle_cost` (now has a real call site) and returns `None`. The grant ends when Lorehold leaves play.\n- Surfaced-and-fixed interaction: scoped the offer to the active player's own draw via `_is_active_player`, so the opponent-upkeep loot draw does not present a miracle offer (this is what kept the loot test's loot-only script from being exhausted).\n- Both advisories applied (docstring note on cost reduction in `cast_spell_alternative`; untap-reset semantics note in `engine/turn.py`).\n\nRelevant files (all absolute): `/workspace/engine/miracle.py`, `/workspace/engine/game.py`, `/workspace/engine/casting.py`, `/workspace/engine/turn.py`, `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`. The modified-file set is unchanged, so `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` needed no update."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a0ce44bc247c3b7b9 (use SendMessage with to: 'a0ce44bc247c3b7b9' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 65484\ntool_uses: 42\nduration_ms: 250215</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"1f7ee277-1586-4152-932d-b2e79d30f3d8","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:48:37.160Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are revising your implementation of card sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian) to address two STRICT review findings.\n\n- Implementation file: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\n- Test file (you MUST NOT modify): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py\n- Your prior diff: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff\n- Review comments: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json\n- COORDINATOR DIRECTIVES (read and follow — the coordinator sides with the Reviewer on both strict items): /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md\n- /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json, /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md\n- Engine: engine/miracle.py, engine/game.py (draw_card), engine/casting.py (cast_spell_alternative), engine/card.py.\n\nREQUIRED CHANGES (both STRICT — must apply):\n1. Draw-time miracle must fire on a NATURALLY-drawn card. Currently the grant only stamps cards already in hand, but draw_card reads the stamp off the card just drawn from the library (never stamped), so miracle never fires in real gameplay. Make the draw-time miracle offer DYNAMICALLY derive the miracle cost for the just-drawn card by consulting active grants (e.g. a Lorehold on the drawer's battlefield grants {2} to instant/sorcery cards it draws). The natural-draw path MUST work with no manual pre-stamping.\n2. The miracle grant must NOT be permanent/sticky. After Lorehold leaves play or the card leaves the controller's hand, the grant must no longer apply. Deriving the grant dynamically (per #1) is the preferred way to satisfy this; otherwise clear the stamp when the grant no longer applies.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file. ALL existing 31 tests in cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py must still pass (those tests have Lorehold in play and draw a controller-hand instant/sorcery; explicitly pre-stamped cards must continue to work too — keep honoring an explicit stamp for backward compat while adding the dynamic path).\n- Additive engine changes only; no renames/moves/deletes; keep len(Keyword)==16.\n- You MAY also apply the two advisories (docstring note that cost reduction is intentionally not applied to the alternative cost; the untap-reset semantics note).\n- If you DISAGREE with a strict comment, do NOT silently skip it — record reasoning in disagreements.json.\n\nVERIFY: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, `pytest cards/fdn/` — all must pass. Also manually verify: with Lorehold in play and an UNSTAMPED instant on top of the controller's library, the controller's first draw of the turn offers the {2} miracle cast; and with Lorehold NOT in play, a previously-stamped card drawn later does NOT offer miracle.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Updated /workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py and engine changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff — `git diff` of ALL current changes (cumulative).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised-rationale.md — what you changed, how the dynamic grant works, and confirm both manual checks + all tests pass.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json — JSON array of {review_comment_index, reviewer_comment, implementer_justification}. Empty array [] if you applied everything.\n- Update this card's entry in /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json if the modified-file set changed.\n\nReturn:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json","agentId":"a0ce44bc247c3b7b9","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 1215 tests pass (31 sos_201 + engine_tests + fdn). Both manual verification checks confirmed.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/disagreements.json\n\nSummary of what changed:\n- STRICT 1: Added `engine.miracle.derive_miracle_cost(game, player, card)` which iterates the drawer's battlefield and asks each permanent exposing a callable `miracle_cost(game, card)` grant (e.g. Lorehold) for the just-drawn card's cost. `engine/game.py draw_card` now calls `offer_miracle` unconditionally, and `offer_miracle` derives the cost dynamically — so a naturally-drawn, unstamped instant/sorcery fires the `{2}` offer with no pre-stamping.\n- STRICT 2: The dynamic deriver is authoritative every draw — when no granter applies it clears any stale stamp via `clear_miracle_cost` (now has a real call site) and returns `None`. The grant ends when Lorehold leaves play.\n- Surfaced-and-fixed interaction: scoped the offer to the active player's own draw via `_is_active_player`, so the opponent-upkeep loot draw does not present a miracle offer (this is what kept the loot test's loot-only script from being exhausted).\n- Both advisories applied (docstring note on cost reduction in `cast_spell_alternative`; untap-reset semantics note in `engine/turn.py`).\n\nRelevant files (all absolute): `/workspace/engine/miracle.py`, `/workspace/engine/game.py`, `/workspace/engine/casting.py`, `/workspace/engine/turn.py`, `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`. The modified-file set is unchanged, so `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` needed no update."}],"totalDurationMs":250215,"totalTokens":65484,"totalToolUseCount":42,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":64574,"output_tokens":679,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":229},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":64574,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens