{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QNwHCoT1UrWykJ1PiM4DPz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XGyLDbAuxDJkbkEbiFu4Ak","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt","offset":5108,"limit":15},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7793,"cache_read_input_tokens":70974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7793,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHujhzSrizXureD9tNErgr","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"80b06c0d-18e5-4b52-af47-c49f0d77b5fa","request_id":"req_011CbcVMb9X9Vx5papHMary6","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XGyLDbAuxDJkbkEbiFu4Ak","type":"tool_result","content":"5108\t702.153. Casualty\n5109\t\n5110\t702.153a Casualty is a keyword that represents two abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. The second is a triggered ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. Casualty N means “As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power N or greater,” and “When you cast this spell, if a casualty cost was paid for it, copy it. If the spell has any targets, you may choose new targets for the copy.” Paying a spell’s casualty cost follows the rules for paying additional costs in rules 601.2b and 601.2f–h.\n5111\t\n5112\t702.153b If a spell has multiple instances of casualty, each is paid separately and triggers based on the payments made for it, not any other instance of casualty.\n5113\t\n5114\t702.154. Enlist\n5115\t\n5116\t702.154a Enlist represents a static ability and a triggered ability. Enlist means “As this creature attacks, you may tap up to one untapped creature you control that you didn’t choose to attack with and that either has haste or has been under your control continuously since this turn began. When you do, this creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the tapped creature’s power.”\n5117\t\n5118\t702.154b Enlist’s static ability represents an optional cost to attack (see rule 508.1g). Its triggered ability is linked to that static ability (see rule 607.2h).\n5119\t\n5120\t702.154c A creature “enlists” another creature when you pay the cost of the creature’s enlist ability by tapping the other creature. Note that it isn’t possible for a creature to enlist itself.\n5121\t\n5122\t702.154d Multiple instances of enlist on a single creature function independently. The triggered ability represented by each instance of enlist triggers only once and only for the cost associated with that enlist ability."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHujhzSrizXureD9tNErgr","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"8a42856b-e005-4f14-af10-1a71e907466c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:50:15.819Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
