{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qyodw4Kpu68ovhARVYNJpT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. (casualty 1 paid as an additional cost during casting, rule 601.2b / 702.153a)\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The engine's cast_spell pipeline has no casualty / additional-cost hook, and SpellCastTriggeredEvent is defined but never fired by the casting code. Tests therefore fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent manually and assert the sacrifice/copy consequence, rather than exercising the true 'as you cast' additional-cost prompt inside cast_spell.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine surface for casualty as an additional cost (e.g. casting code that consults a card-provided casualty grant and offers the sacrifice mid-cast), and/or having engine.casting.cast_spell fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent so the grant can be observed through a real cast.\"\n6\t  },\n7\t  {\n8\t    \"requirement\": \"When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.\",\n9\t    \"reason\": \"Verifying that the copy can take NEW targets requires a fixed copy/re-target API and a targeted spell whose target choice is observable. engine.stack.copy_spell exists but the card's exact re-target prompt and how new targets are scripted is undefined, so only the existence of the copy (same name, distinct object) is asserted, not the new-target choice.\",\n10\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"A defined contract for how Silverquill's casualty copy chooses new targets (e.g. it calls controller.choose_target for each original target on the copy), plus a targetable test spell exposing its chosen targets after resolution.\"\n11\t  }\n12\t]\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"3541dac7-d544-405e-b0b6-ed969e1ba719","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:52:43.153Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. (casualty 1 paid as an additional cost during casting, rule 601.2b / 702.153a)\",\n    \"reason\": \"The engine's cast_spell pipeline has no casualty / additional-cost hook, and SpellCastTriggeredEvent is defined but never fired by the casting code. Tests therefore fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent manually and assert the sacrifice/copy consequence, rather than exercising the true 'as you cast' additional-cost prompt inside cast_spell.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine surface for casualty as an additional cost (e.g. casting code that consults a card-provided casualty grant and offers the sacrifice mid-cast), and/or having engine.casting.cast_spell fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent so the grant can be observed through a real cast.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.\",\n    \"reason\": \"Verifying that the copy can take NEW targets requires a fixed copy/re-target API and a targeted spell whose target choice is observable. engine.stack.copy_spell exists but the card's exact re-target prompt and how new targets are scripted is undefined, so only the existence of the copy (same name, distinct object) is asserted, not the new-target choice.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock\": \"A defined contract for how Silverquill's casualty copy chooses new targets (e.g. it calls controller.choose_target for each original target on the copy), plus a targetable test spell exposing its chosen targets after resolution.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}}}
