{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BMMrYV22uJf4rbjaZ3F1mT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — SOS 226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n2\t\n3\t## File: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n4\t\n5\tSilverquill is a {2}{W}{B} 4/4 Legendary Elder Dragon with Flying and Vigilance.\n6\tIts payoff line grants **casualty 1** to every instant and sorcery spell its\n7\tcontroller casts: as the controller casts such a spell, they may sacrifice a\n8\tcreature with power 1 or greater; if they do, the spell is copied (with optional\n9\tnew targets).\n10\t\n11\tCasualty (rule 702.153) is a brand-new mechanic with no existing engine surface,\n12\tso the tests pin the firmest observable contract and lean on the established\n13\t`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + `trigger_manager` pattern that FDN cast-trigger cards\n14\t(e.g. FDN 92 Rite of the Dragoncaller) use.\n15\t\n16\t### TestSilverquillProperties — static card data\n17\t- `test_is_creature` — instance is a `Creature`.\n18\t- `test_name` — name matches the spec.\n19\t- `test_mana_cost` — `{2}{W}{B}`.\n20\t- `test_power_toughness` — 4/4.\n21\t- `test_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n22\t- `test_elder_dragon_subtypes` — subtypes include `Dragon` and `Elder`\n23\t  (type line \"Elder Dragon\").\n24\t- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_vigilance` — the two printed keywords.\n25\t- `test_is_white_and_black` — colors include WHITE and BLACK (derived from cost).\n26\t- `test_not_other_colors` — colors exclude RED/BLUE/GREEN.\n27\t\n28\t### TestSilverquillTriggerRegistration — wiring\n29\t- `test_registers_a_spell_cast_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds at least one\n30\t  trigger to the manager.\n31\t- `test_trigger_watches_spell_cast_event` — at least one registered trigger uses\n32\t  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` as its event type. This is the natural hook for an\n33\t  \"as you cast\" / \"when you cast\" casualty grant.\n34\t\n35\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyScope — which/whose spells qualify\n36\t- `test_controller_instant_offers_casualty` — casting your own instant, with a\n37\t  power>=1 creature available and a \"yes\" choice, sacrifices that creature\n38\t  (it leaves the battlefield for the graveyard).\n39\t- `test_opponent_spell_does_not_trigger` — an opponent's instant must NOT fire\n40\t  the grant (\"each instant and sorcery spell *you* cast\"). Negative/scope guard.\n41\t- `test_creature_spell_does_not_trigger` — a creature spell does not get casualty\n42\t  (only instants/sorceries). Negative/scope guard.\n43\t- `test_sorcery_qualifies` — sorceries also get the grant (a trigger is pushed).\n44\t\n45\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyCopy — copy & optional cost\n46\t- `test_paying_casualty_creates_a_copy_on_the_stack` — resolving the casualty\n47\t  trigger after choosing \"yes\" puts a distinct copy (same name, different object)\n48\t  of the spell onto the stack.\n49\t- `test_declining_casualty_makes_no_copy_and_no_sacrifice` — casualty is optional\n50\t  (\"you may\"); a \"no\" choice sacrifices nothing and creates no copy.\n51\t- `test_no_eligible_creature_means_no_copy` — with only a 0-power creature, the\n52\t  casualty sacrifice (power 1 or greater) cannot be paid: no copy, no sacrifice.\n53\t- `test_zero_power_creature_not_a_legal_sacrifice` — a 0-power creature is never\n54\t  chosen as the casualty sacrifice.\n55\t\n56\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyBattlefieldDependency\n57\t- `test_no_trigger_when_silverquill_not_on_battlefield` — the grant is a static\n58\t  ability of the permanent; with Silverquill in hand it produces no copy.\n59\t\n60\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n61\t- **Exact \"as you cast\" interactive timing.** Casualty is an additional cost paid\n62\t  *during* casting (rule 601.2b), but the engine's `cast_spell` pipeline has no\n63\t  casualty hook today. The tests fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` directly (the\n64\t  \"when you cast this spell\" half of casualty, rule 702.153a) and assert on the\n65\t  resulting sacrifice/copy. The precise integration point (additional-cost prompt\n66\t  inside `cast_spell` vs. a post-cast trigger) is left to the Implementer; see\n67\t  `untestable.json`.\n68\t- **Choosing new targets for the copy.** Verifying that the copy can re-target is\n69\t  out of reach without a fixed copy API; `copy_spell` exists but the card's exact\n70\t  re-target prompt is undefined. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n71\t- **Stacking with native casualty / multiple instances** (rule 702.153b) — out of\n72\t  scope for this single card.\n73\t- **Layer/continuous-effect modelling of the grant** — not asserted; only the\n74\t  observable cast-time consequence is.\n75\t\n76\t## Note on currently-passing negative tests\n77\tSix tests pass against the empty stub because they assert the *absence* of a\n78\tbehaviour (opponent spell, creature spell, ineligible creature, off-battlefield,\n79\tnon-WBRG colors). These are scope guards that stay green only if the Implementer\n80\tdoes not over-trigger; the positive-path tests carry the red-phase signal.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"74d5020b-18ae-441a-8b84-5155fa1b1b40","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:52:52.663Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — SOS 226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n\n## File: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n\nSilverquill is a {2}{W}{B} 4/4 Legendary Elder Dragon with Flying and Vigilance.\nIts payoff line grants **casualty 1** to every instant and sorcery spell its\ncontroller casts: as the controller casts such a spell, they may sacrifice a\ncreature with power 1 or greater; if they do, the spell is copied (with optional\nnew targets).\n\nCasualty (rule 702.153) is a brand-new mechanic with no existing engine surface,\nso the tests pin the firmest observable contract and lean on the established\n`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + `trigger_manager` pattern that FDN cast-trigger cards\n(e.g. FDN 92 Rite of the Dragoncaller) use.\n\n### TestSilverquillProperties — static card data\n- `test_is_creature` — instance is a `Creature`.\n- `test_name` — name matches the spec.\n- `test_mana_cost` — `{2}{W}{B}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — 4/4.\n- `test_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n- `test_elder_dragon_subtypes` — subtypes include `Dragon` and `Elder`\n  (type line \"Elder Dragon\").\n- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_vigilance` — the two printed keywords.\n- `test_is_white_and_black` — colors include WHITE and BLACK (derived from cost).\n- `test_not_other_colors` — colors exclude RED/BLUE/GREEN.\n\n### TestSilverquillTriggerRegistration — wiring\n- `test_registers_a_spell_cast_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds at least one\n  trigger to the manager.\n- `test_trigger_watches_spell_cast_event` — at least one registered trigger uses\n  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` as its event type. This is the natural hook for an\n  \"as you cast\" / \"when you cast\" casualty grant.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyScope — which/whose spells qualify\n- `test_controller_instant_offers_casualty` — casting your own instant, with a\n  power>=1 creature available and a \"yes\" choice, sacrifices that creature\n  (it leaves the battlefield for the graveyard).\n- `test_opponent_spell_does_not_trigger` — an opponent's instant must NOT fire\n  the grant (\"each instant and sorcery spell *you* cast\"). Negative/scope guard.\n- `test_creature_spell_does_not_trigger` — a creature spell does not get casualty\n  (only instants/sorceries). Negative/scope guard.\n- `test_sorcery_qualifies` — sorceries also get the grant (a trigger is pushed).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyCopy — copy & optional cost\n- `test_paying_casualty_creates_a_copy_on_the_stack` — resolving the casualty\n  trigger after choosing \"yes\" puts a distinct copy (same name, different object)\n  of the spell onto the stack.\n- `test_declining_casualty_makes_no_copy_and_no_sacrifice` — casualty is optional\n  (\"you may\"); a \"no\" choice sacrifices nothing and creates no copy.\n- `test_no_eligible_creature_means_no_copy` — with only a 0-power creature, the\n  casualty sacrifice (power 1 or greater) cannot be paid: no copy, no sacrifice.\n- `test_zero_power_creature_not_a_legal_sacrifice` — a 0-power creature is never\n  chosen as the casualty sacrifice.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyBattlefieldDependency\n- `test_no_trigger_when_silverquill_not_on_battlefield` — the grant is a static\n  ability of the permanent; with Silverquill in hand it produces no copy.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- **Exact \"as you cast\" interactive timing.** Casualty is an additional cost paid\n  *during* casting (rule 601.2b), but the engine's `cast_spell` pipeline has no\n  casualty hook today. The tests fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` directly (the\n  \"when you cast this spell\" half of casualty, rule 702.153a) and assert on the\n  resulting sacrifice/copy. The precise integration point (additional-cost prompt\n  inside `cast_spell` vs. a post-cast trigger) is left to the Implementer; see\n  `untestable.json`.\n- **Choosing new targets for the copy.** Verifying that the copy can re-target is\n  out of reach without a fixed copy API; `copy_spell` exists but the card's exact\n  re-target prompt is undefined. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Stacking with native casualty / multiple instances** (rule 702.153b) — out of\n  scope for this single card.\n- **Layer/continuous-effect modelling of the grant** — not asserted; only the\n  observable cast-time consequence is.\n\n## Note on currently-passing negative tests\nSix tests pass against the empty stub because they assert the *absence* of a\nbehaviour (opponent spell, creature spell, ineligible creature, off-battlefield,\nnon-WBRG colors). These are scope guards that stay green only if the Implementer\ndoes not over-trigger; the positive-path tests carry the red-phase signal.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
