{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EzMbwh2NeUa1M3e4BxREye","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B7aKC3gyQv6QBVRSwBRoRj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_226 (initial implementation)\n\nCard: **Silverquill, the Disputant** — `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder\nDragon, 4/4, Flying, Vigilance.\n- \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that\n  spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy\n  the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n\nThe Tester escalated two requirements as untestable: the true \"as you cast\"\nadditional-cost timing (no casualty hook; SpellCastTriggeredEvent is defined but\nnever fired by cast_spell), and the new-target choice for the copy. Engine\nchanges are allowed and expected. Implement the FULL card plus additive engine\nsupport, and expose a testable contract. After you finish, the Tester will be\nre-invoked.\n\n## Requirements to implement fully\n1. **Static**: 4/4, Flying, Vigilance, Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {WHITE, BLACK}.\n2. **Casualty 1 grant**: while Silverquill is on the battlefield, each instant or\n   sorcery spell ITS CONTROLLER casts has casualty 1. Scope strictly: only the\n   controller's instant/sorcery spells (not opponents', not creatures, not while\n   Silverquill is off the battlefield).\n3. **Casualty resolution**: optionally (`choose_yes_no`) sacrifice a creature with\n   power >= 1 (`choose_card` among eligible; a 0-power creature is never eligible;\n   if no eligible creature, no sacrifice and no copy). Use `engine.game.sacrifice`.\n   When the sacrifice is made, COPY the spell (`engine.stack.copy_spell`) and the\n   controller MAY choose new targets for the copy.\n\n## Engine support to add (additive only)\n- **Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` from `engine.casting.cast_spell`** so cast-time\n  grants (casualty and future \"when you cast\" effects) can observe a real cast.\n  This is the natural hook the tests use (FDN-92 pattern). Be careful not to break\n  existing engine tests — only ADD the firing; match the existing event/trigger\n  conventions. Verify the event's fields/firing site against engine source.\n- **New-target choice for the copy**: provide/define how the casualty copy chooses\n  new targets — e.g. `copy_spell` (or a helper) that, for each original target,\n  calls `controller.choose_target` (or equivalent) on the copy so a test can\n  script new targets and observe them on the copy after resolution. Keep\n  backward compatibility with existing `copy_spell` callers.\n\n## Make it testable\n- Model casualty so the test contract holds: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n  trigger via `register_triggers` (scoped to the controller's instant/sorcery\n  spells, only while Silverquill is on the battlefield); on resolve, offer the\n  optional sacrifice and create the copy with optional new targets.\n- A test must be able to: cast a controller instant with an eligible creature in\n  play, answer yes, and observe the creature sacrificed and a distinct copy of the\n  spell on the stack — AND observe the copy taking newly-chosen targets.\n\nDocument the exact contracts (trigger event, sacrifice flow, copy/new-target API)\nin your rationale. Do NOT stub these out — the grader's authoritative tests will\nexercise the casualty sacrifice, the copy, and new-target selection.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2563,"cache_read_input_tokens":121155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2563},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"fdd98de1-9981-49ae-9eb2-7d5abe36f5b3","request_id":"req_011CbcVZQEGdKBStSXGJWNpW"}
