{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bXKcBe7fz8KpBs8ZekPVV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_226 (initial implementation)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Silverquill, the Disputant** — `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder\n4\tDragon, 4/4, Flying, Vigilance.\n5\t- \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that\n6\t  spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy\n7\t  the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n8\t\n9\tThe Tester escalated two requirements as untestable: the true \"as you cast\"\n10\tadditional-cost timing (no casualty hook; SpellCastTriggeredEvent is defined but\n11\tnever fired by cast_spell), and the new-target choice for the copy. Engine\n12\tchanges are allowed and expected. Implement the FULL card plus additive engine\n13\tsupport, and expose a testable contract. After you finish, the Tester will be\n14\tre-invoked.\n15\t\n16\t## Requirements to implement fully\n17\t1. **Static**: 4/4, Flying, Vigilance, Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {WHITE, BLACK}.\n18\t2. **Casualty 1 grant**: while Silverquill is on the battlefield, each instant or\n19\t   sorcery spell ITS CONTROLLER casts has casualty 1. Scope strictly: only the\n20\t   controller's instant/sorcery spells (not opponents', not creatures, not while\n21\t   Silverquill is off the battlefield).\n22\t3. **Casualty resolution**: optionally (`choose_yes_no`) sacrifice a creature with\n23\t   power >= 1 (`choose_card` among eligible; a 0-power creature is never eligible;\n24\t   if no eligible creature, no sacrifice and no copy). Use `engine.game.sacrifice`.\n25\t   When the sacrifice is made, COPY the spell (`engine.stack.copy_spell`) and the\n26\t   controller MAY choose new targets for the copy.\n27\t\n28\t## Engine support to add (additive only)\n29\t- **Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` from `engine.casting.cast_spell`** so cast-time\n30\t  grants (casualty and future \"when you cast\" effects) can observe a real cast.\n31\t  This is the natural hook the tests use (FDN-92 pattern). Be careful not to break\n32\t  existing engine tests — only ADD the firing; match the existing event/trigger\n33\t  conventions. Verify the event's fields/firing site against engine source.\n34\t- **New-target choice for the copy**: provide/define how the casualty copy chooses\n35\t  new targets — e.g. `copy_spell` (or a helper) that, for each original target,\n36\t  calls `controller.choose_target` (or equivalent) on the copy so a test can\n37\t  script new targets and observe them on the copy after resolution. Keep\n38\t  backward compatibility with existing `copy_spell` callers.\n39\t\n40\t## Make it testable\n41\t- Model casualty so the test contract holds: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n42\t  trigger via `register_triggers` (scoped to the controller's instant/sorcery\n43\t  spells, only while Silverquill is on the battlefield); on resolve, offer the\n44\t  optional sacrifice and create the copy with optional new targets.\n45\t- A test must be able to: cast a controller instant with an eligible creature in\n46\t  play, answer yes, and observe the creature sacrificed and a distinct copy of the\n47\t  spell on the stack — AND observe the copy taking newly-chosen targets.\n48\t\n49\tDocument the exact contracts (trigger event, sacrifice flow, copy/new-target API)\n50\tin your rationale. Do NOT stub these out — the grader's authoritative tests will\n51\texercise the casualty sacrifice, the copy, and new-target selection.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCYYisVY7Xuo39nNQTUeL3","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"0f8431d1-e6ef-40e2-986e-014adfa61087","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:53:34.496Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
