{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2g5XsDcCNNoVkVNDHX9wt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\t`SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` in `cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`:\n5\t{2}{W}{B} 4/4 Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying + Vigilance, colors {WHITE, BLACK}\n6\t(set explicitly because of the hybrid-free WB cost; matches the sos_13 colors\n7\tconvention). Subtypes `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`, supertype LEGENDARY.\n8\t\n9\t## Casualty 1 grant — exact contracts exposed\n10\t\n11\t### Trigger event\n12\t`register_triggers` registers a `TriggerRegistration` watching\n13\t`engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (FDN-92 / FDN-248 pattern), controller =\n14\t`self.controller or game.active_player`.\n15\t\n16\tCondition scope (all must hold):\n17\t- Silverquill is on a battlefield (`_is_on_battlefield`) — the grant is a static\n18\t  ability of the permanent, so it does nothing from hand.\n19\t- The spell's caster (`event.controller`/`event.player`) or the spell's\n20\t  `controller` is Silverquill's controller — only spells **you** cast.\n21\t- The spell's `card_types` intersect `{INSTANT, SORCERY}` — creature/permanent\n22\t  spells do not qualify.\n23\tThe matched spell is stashed on `self._casualty_spell` for the effect.\n24\t\n25\t### Sacrifice flow (`_resolve_casualty`)\n26\t1. Eligible sacrifices = creatures the controller controls with `power >= 1`,\n27\t   **excluding Silverquill itself**. (See deviation below.) A 0-power creature is\n28\t   never eligible; if the eligible list is empty there is no `choose_yes_no`\n29\t   prompt, no sacrifice, and no copy.\n30\t2. Optional via `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`. Declining => no sacrifice, no copy.\n31\t3. Selection: `controller.choose_card(eligible, ...)` when more than one creature\n32\t   is eligible; auto-selected when exactly one (matches the Tester scripts, which\n33\t   provide a single dedicated sacrifice creature and a trailing leftover entry).\n34\t4. Sacrifice via `engine.game.sacrifice(game, controller, chosen)`.\n35\t\n36\t### Copy + new-target API (`copy_spell` / `_choose_new_targets`)\n37\tAfter a sacrifice, the original spell's live `StackObject` is located on\n38\t`game.stack`; if none exists (e.g. the spell sits only in the player's STACK\n39\tzone, as in the tests) a transient `StackObject` is synthesised around the spell\n40\t(targets read from `spell.chosen_targets`). The copy is created with\n41\t`engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original_so, controller, new_targets)` and pushed\n42\tonto `game.stack` (distinct object, same `name`).\n43\t\n44\tNew targets: `_choose_new_targets` returns `None` (keep originals) when the spell\n45\thas no targets; otherwise it asks `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`, and on yes\n46\trebuilds the legal-target set per `get_targets()` requirement (battlefield\n47\tpermanents + players passing `filter_fn`) and calls `controller.choose_target`\n48\tper requirement — backward-compatible with the existing `copy_spell(new_targets=None)`\n49\tcontract (FDN-248 convention).\n50\t\n51\t## Engine change (additive)\n52\t`engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell` now fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after\n53\tpushing the spell's `StackObject`, via a new helper `_fire_spell_cast_event`\n54\t(spell=card, player/controller=casting player). Previously the event was defined\n55\tbut never fired by the cast pipeline. The helper is a safe no-op if the game has\n56\tno `trigger_manager`. This is the only existing-function body change; the full\n57\tengine suite, FDN, and SOS suites all pass (1403 passed), so no regressions.\n58\t`cast_spell_free` / `cast_spell_alternative` were intentionally left unchanged to\n59\tkeep the blast radius minimal (the directive scoped the firing to `cast_spell`).\n60\t\n61\t## Deviation from MTG rules\n62\tThe casualty candidate list excludes Silverquill itself. Strict rules (702.153)\n63\twould allow sacrificing any creature with power >= 1 (including Silverquill). The\n64\tauthoritative tests place Silverquill plus a single dedicated sacrifice creature\n65\tand assert that with one eligible creature no `choose_card` is consumed and that a\n66\t0-power \"wall\" alongside Silverquill yields no sacrifice/copy; counting Silverquill\n67\t(power 4) as eligible would contradict those assertions. Excluding the source\n68\tcreature is the minimal model that satisfies the pinned contract. Future cards\n69\tneeding a fully rules-accurate casualty should generalise this.\n70\t\n71\t## Convention for future cards\n72\t- `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is now fired by `engine.casting.cast_spell` — any\n73\t  \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery spell\" or cast-time grant can rely on it\n74\t  firing through the normal cast pipeline (not just when fired manually in tests).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"a0be8643-a6a8-47ba-ade2-0822851fb8ef","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:57:09.588Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n\n## Card\n`SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` in `cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`:\n{2}{W}{B} 4/4 Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying + Vigilance, colors {WHITE, BLACK}\n(set explicitly because of the hybrid-free WB cost; matches the sos_13 colors\nconvention). Subtypes `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`, supertype LEGENDARY.\n\n## Casualty 1 grant — exact contracts exposed\n\n### Trigger event\n`register_triggers` registers a `TriggerRegistration` watching\n`engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (FDN-92 / FDN-248 pattern), controller =\n`self.controller or game.active_player`.\n\nCondition scope (all must hold):\n- Silverquill is on a battlefield (`_is_on_battlefield`) — the grant is a static\n  ability of the permanent, so it does nothing from hand.\n- The spell's caster (`event.controller`/`event.player`) or the spell's\n  `controller` is Silverquill's controller — only spells **you** cast.\n- The spell's `card_types` intersect `{INSTANT, SORCERY}` — creature/permanent\n  spells do not qualify.\nThe matched spell is stashed on `self._casualty_spell` for the effect.\n\n### Sacrifice flow (`_resolve_casualty`)\n1. Eligible sacrifices = creatures the controller controls with `power >= 1`,\n   **excluding Silverquill itself**. (See deviation below.) A 0-power creature is\n   never eligible; if the eligible list is empty there is no `choose_yes_no`\n   prompt, no sacrifice, and no copy.\n2. Optional via `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`. Declining => no sacrifice, no copy.\n3. Selection: `controller.choose_card(eligible, ...)` when more than one creature\n   is eligible; auto-selected when exactly one (matches the Tester scripts, which\n   provide a single dedicated sacrifice creature and a trailing leftover entry).\n4. Sacrifice via `engine.game.sacrifice(game, controller, chosen)`.\n\n### Copy + new-target API (`copy_spell` / `_choose_new_targets`)\nAfter a sacrifice, the original spell's live `StackObject` is located on\n`game.stack`; if none exists (e.g. the spell sits only in the player's STACK\nzone, as in the tests) a transient `StackObject` is synthesised around the spell\n(targets read from `spell.chosen_targets`). The copy is created with\n`engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original_so, controller, new_targets)` and pushed\nonto `game.stack` (distinct object, same `name`).\n\nNew targets: `_choose_new_targets` returns `None` (keep originals) when the spell\nhas no targets; otherwise it asks `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`, and on yes\nrebuilds the legal-target set per `get_targets()` requirement (battlefield\npermanents + players passing `filter_fn`) and calls `controller.choose_target`\nper requirement — backward-compatible with the existing `copy_spell(new_targets=None)`\ncontract (FDN-248 convention).\n\n## Engine change (additive)\n`engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell` now fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after\npushing the spell's `StackObject`, via a new helper `_fire_spell_cast_event`\n(spell=card, player/controller=casting player). Previously the event was defined\nbut never fired by the cast pipeline. The helper is a safe no-op if the game has\nno `trigger_manager`. This is the only existing-function body change; the full\nengine suite, FDN, and SOS suites all pass (1403 passed), so no regressions.\n`cast_spell_free` / `cast_spell_alternative` were intentionally left unchanged to\nkeep the blast radius minimal (the directive scoped the firing to `cast_spell`).\n\n## Deviation from MTG rules\nThe casualty candidate list excludes Silverquill itself. Strict rules (702.153)\nwould allow sacrificing any creature with power >= 1 (including Silverquill). The\nauthoritative tests place Silverquill plus a single dedicated sacrifice creature\nand assert that with one eligible creature no `choose_card` is consumed and that a\n0-power \"wall\" alongside Silverquill yields no sacrifice/copy; counting Silverquill\n(power 4) as eligible would contradict those assertions. Excluding the source\ncreature is the minimal model that satisfies the pinned contract. Future cards\nneeding a fully rules-accurate casualty should generalise this.\n\n## Convention for future cards\n- `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is now fired by `engine.casting.cast_spell` — any\n  \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery spell\" or cast-time grant can rely on it\n  firing through the normal cast pipeline (not just when fired manually in tests).\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":75}}}
