{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015jLJQmZ2V3xLLpUegsEsMV","type":"tool_result","content":"FILES_MODIFIED.json:104:          \"summary\": \"tests for sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant: static data, SpellCastTriggeredEvent casualty trigger registration, controller-only instant/sorcery scope, optional power>=1 sacrifice, and distinct spell copy on the stack\"\nFILES_MODIFIED.json:110:          \"summary\": \"Silverquill, the Disputant: 4/4 flying vigilance WB Elder Dragon granting casualty 1 to controller instant/sorcery spells via a SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger that optionally sacrifices a power>=1 creature (excluding itself) and copies the spell with optional new targets\"\nFILES_MODIFIED.json:114:          \"summary\": \"cast_spell now fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent (via additive _fire_spell_cast_event) after pushing the spell so cast-time/casualty grants trigger through the normal pipeline\"\nengine/events.py:111:class SpellCastTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\nengine/casting.py:262:    \"\"\"Fire :class:`~engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` for a cast spell.\nengine/casting.py:271:    from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\nengine/casting.py:275:        SpellCastTriggeredEvent(\ncards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:13::class:`~engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger scoped to the\ncards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:22:``SpellCastTriggeredEvent`` is now fired by ``engine.casting.cast_spell``\ncards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:78:        from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\ncards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py:115:                event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent,\ncards/sos/sos_226/tests.py:23:The casualty-driven copy/sacrifice tests fire ``SpellCastTriggeredEvent``\ncards/sos/sos_226/tests.py:34:from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\ncards/sos/sos_226/tests.py:130:        assert any(r.event_type is SpellCastTriggeredEvent for r in regs)\ncards/sos/sos_226/tests.py:157:            SpellCastTrig