{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016botgDJ1X78ZG2b9xXKUaf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json\n\nSummary of assessment:\n- Static data (4/4, Flying+Vigilance only, Legendary, Elder Dragon, {WHITE,BLACK}) and casualty scope (controller-only instants/sorceries, on-battlefield gate, optional power>=1 sacrifice, 0-power never eligible, distinct copy with same name) all match the spec and the pinned tests.\n- Engine change is safe and additive: `_fire_spell_cast_event` is new; the single added call site in `engine/casting.py:258` fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after the StackObject is pushed, with correct spell/player. No production code fires this event manually (so no double-firing), the casualty copy is pushed via `game.stack.push` rather than `cast_spell` (so no re-firing/recursion), and `cast_spell_free`/`cast_spell_alternative` are untouched. Full suite: 1403 passed, no regressions.\n- Judgment call on excluding Silverquill from casualty candidates: I confirmed there is no rules-accurate approach that includes Silverquill and still passes `test_no_eligible_creature_means_no_copy` unchanged, so per the directive this is recorded as ADVISORY, not strict.\n- No strict findings. Three advisories: the documented rules-fidelity gap, a latent `_casualty_spell` stash-clobber bug for multi-spell turns, and the ad-hoc re-targeting target construction.\n\nRelevant files:\n- /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\n- /workspace/engine/casting.py\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae2aef7f18dd7bc10 (use SendMessage with to: 'ae2aef7f18dd7bc10' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 50496\ntool_uses: 27\nduration_ms: 115915</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"b239dd74-cfc8-45e0-b8d1-06832c0092c5","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:59:48.918Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are reviewing a Magic: The Gathering card implementation diff (with a NEW casualty mechanic and an engine change to cast_spell) for correctness.\n\nCARD: sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant ({2}{W}{B} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, Flying, Vigilance)\n- \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n\n- Spec: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_spec.json\n- Implementation diff: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl.diff\n- Implementer's rationale: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md\n- Implementation file: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\n- Test file (already arbitrated — do NOT demand test rewrites): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n- /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json, /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md (do NOT flag established conventions or earlier-card patterns).\n- RULEBOOK.txt for rules (grep, don't read whole): Casualty (702.153), copying spells (707.10), choosing new targets.\n\nREVIEW SCOPE (correctness vs spec + MTG rules):\n- Static: 4/4, Flying+Vigilance (exactly), Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {WHITE, BLACK}.\n- Casualty grant scope: only the CONTROLLER's instant/sorcery spells, only while Silverquill is on the battlefield.\n- Casualty resolution: optional; sacrifice a power>=1 creature; 0-power never eligible; no eligible => no sacrifice/copy; copy created (distinct object, same name) and may take new targets.\n- ENGINE CHANGE — scrutinize for safety/regressions: engine/casting.py cast_spell now fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent via _fire_spell_cast_event. Is the firing site correct (after the StackObject is pushed), does it pass the right spell/player, and could it cause double-firing, infinite recursion (e.g. copy_spell re-firing cast events), or break existing engine tests?\n\nSPECIFIC JUDGMENT CALL — the Implementer DEVIATED from strict rules by EXCLUDING Silverquill itself from the casualty sacrifice candidate list (strict rules would allow sacrificing any power>=1 creature including Silverquill). The Implementer says the pinned tests force this (they auto-select when exactly one eligible creature and assert a 0-power wall alongside Silverquill yields no sacrifice; including Silverquill would break those, and tests can't be modified). Please assess: is there ANY implementation approach that is rules-accurate (includes Silverquill as an eligible sacrifice) AND still passes the existing tests without modifying them? If yes, describe it concretely and flag the exclusion STRICT. If no such approach exists (the tests genuinely require the exclusion), treat the exclusion as ADVISORY (an accepted, documented rules-fidelity gap), not strict.\n\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — advisory only for test quality.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Write /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json — JSON array of {\"severity\":\"strict\"|\"advisory\",\"file\",\"line\",\"comment\"}. Empty array [] if none.\n\nReturn:\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json","agentId":"ae2aef7f18dd7bc10","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json\n\nSummary of assessment:\n- Static data (4/4, Flying+Vigilance only, Legendary, Elder Dragon, {WHITE,BLACK}) and casualty scope (controller-only instants/sorceries, on-battlefield gate, optional power>=1 sacrifice, 0-power never eligible, distinct copy with same name) all match the spec and the pinned tests.\n- Engine change is safe and additive: `_fire_spell_cast_event` is new; the single added call site in `engine/casting.py:258` fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after the StackObject is pushed, with correct spell/player. No production code fires this event manually (so no double-firing), the casualty copy is pushed via `game.stack.push` rather than `cast_spell` (so no re-firing/recursion), and `cast_spell_free`/`cast_spell_alternative` are untouched. Full suite: 1403 passed, no regressions.\n- Judgment call on excluding Silverquill from casualty candidates: I confirmed there is no rules-accurate approach that includes Silverquill and still passes `test_no_eligible_creature_means_no_copy` unchanged, so per the directive this is recorded as ADVISORY, not strict.\n- No strict findings. Three advisories: the documented rules-fidelity gap, a latent `_casualty_spell` stash-clobber bug for multi-spell turns, and the ad-hoc re-targeting target construction.\n\nRelevant files:\n- /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\n- /workspace/engine/casting.py\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":115915,"totalTokens":50496,"totalToolUseCount":27,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_read_input_tokens":48701,"output_tokens":602,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":48701,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":12,"searchCount":9,"bashCount":5,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":6,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
