{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CL7sRGqhS3j18Kf2D38MDX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016acQwUBv61AyKxkC2uPPM7","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- **Exact \"as you cast\" interactive timing.** Casualty is an additional cost paid\n  *during* casting (rule 601.2b), but the engine's `cast_spell` pipeline has no\n  casualty hook today. The tests fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` directly (the\n  \"when you cast this spell\" half of casualty, rule 702.153a) and assert on the\n  resulting sacrifice/copy. The precise integration point (additional-cost prompt\n  inside `cast_spell` vs. a post-cast trigger) is left to the Implementer; see\n  `untestable.json`.\n- **Choosing new targets for the copy.** Verifying that the copy can re-target is\n  out of reach without a fixed copy API; `copy_spell` exists but the card's exact\n  re-target prompt is undefined. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Stacking with native casualty / multiple instances** (rule 702.153b) — out of","new_string":"## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- **\"As you cast\" as a true additional cost paid mid-cast** (rule 601.2b). The\n  card models casualty via the \"when you cast this spell\" trigger fired by\n  `cast_spell` after the spell hits the stack (rule 702.153a), so the copy is put\n  on the stack above the still-unresolved original — which is what the new\n  real-cast tests assert. A mid-cast additional-cost prompt (sacrifice resolved\n  before the spell is on the stack) is not modelled; this is the Implementer's\n  documented integration choice and is now covered to the firmest observable\n  contract (no longer untestable).\n- **Stacking with native casualty / multiple instances** (rule 702.153b) — out of"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":nu