{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NGPgShq7ufcrA89j3njWbF","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TESTS_REWRITTEN\n\n- Total tests now: 26 (in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`)\n- New tests added: 6 (all existing 20 unchanged and still passing)\n- All passing: yes (26 passed)\n- Remaining untestable_count: 0 (`/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` is now `[]`)\n\nNew coverage (both previously-untestable requirements now exercised end-to-end through the real engine pipeline):\n\n`TestSilverquillCasualtyThroughRealCast` (real-cast \"as you cast\" path via `engine.casting.cast_spell`):\n- `test_real_cast_queues_casualty_trigger_above_the_spell` — real cast leaves the spell on the stack with the casualty trigger pushed above it (the `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired by `cast_spell` itself).\n- `test_real_cast_paying_casualty_sacrifices_and_copies` — resolving that trigger with \"yes\" sacrifices the creature and puts exactly one distinct copy on the stack.\n- `test_real_cast_declining_casualty_makes_no_copy` — declining leaves only the original spell, no sacrifice.\n\n`TestSilverquillCasualtyNewTargets` (copy may choose new targets):\n- `test_copy_can_retarget_a_different_creature` — uses a minimal targeted `_PingInstant`; cast at the original creature, pay casualty, choose new targets → copy's `targets` is the new creature and resolving marks damage on the NEW target while the original takes none.\n- `test_copy_keeps_original_target_when_retarget_declined` — declining the re-target prompt keeps the copy on the original target.\n\nNote on test design: in the new-target tests the two targetable creatures are 0-power so the dedicated power-1 \"Sacrifice\" creature is the sole eligible casualty (keeping the sacrifice auto-selected and the `DeterministicPlayer` scripts unambiguous, matching the implementation's `choose_card`-only-when->1-eligible contract). Updated rationale at `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae8d04658600cfb73 (use SendMessage with to: 'ae8d04658600cfb73' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 77969\ntool_uses: 37\nduration_ms: 176929</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"beef63cc-4faa-4886-9de0-a6ac13704ef9","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:03:02.607Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You previously wrote tests for card sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant) at /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py and escalated two requirements as untestable (the \"as you cast\" casualty timing through a real cast, and the new-target choice for the copy — see /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json). The Implementer has now implemented the full card AND added engine support, exposing testable contracts.\n\nCARD: sos_226\n- Spec: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_spec.json\n- Implementation (read it): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\n- Implementer's rationale with EXACT contracts: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md (READ THIS)\n- Engine: engine/casting.py now FIRES SpellCastTriggeredEvent from cast_spell (via _fire_spell_cast_event, after the StackObject is pushed). engine/stack.py copy_spell supports new_targets. engine/game.sacrifice.\n- Existing tests to extend (do NOT remove existing passing tests): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n\nContracts available (per rationale — verify against the code):\n- Casting a controller instant/sorcery via engine.casting.cast_spell now fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent, so the casualty trigger fires through a REAL cast (not just a manually-fired event).\n- The casualty copy can take NEW targets: _choose_new_targets asks the controller choose_yes_no and then choose_target per target requirement; copy_spell(new_targets=...) builds the copy with them.\n\nTASK: Add tests covering the two previously-untestable requirements end-to-end:\n1. Real-cast casualty: cast a controller's instant/sorcery through engine.casting.cast_spell (with Silverquill in play and an eligible creature), and verify the casualty trigger fires through the real cast pipeline (the SpellCastTriggeredEvent is fired by cast_spell, the trigger is pushed/resolvable), leading to the sacrifice + copy when accepted.\n2. New-target choice for the copy: cast/resolve a TARGETED spell with casualty, pay it, choose NEW targets for the copy, and assert the copy resolves against the newly-chosen target (different from the original).\n\nRead the implementation/engine source to use the REAL APIs and DeterministicPlayer scripts. Follow existing test conventions. Do NOT modify or break existing tests.\n\nAfter writing, run `pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` and confirm ALL tests pass.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Update /workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py with new tests.\n- Append new coverage to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md.\n- Empty /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json to [] (or note any genuinely-remaining items).\n\nReturn a short status: total tests now, how many new, all passing (yes/no), remaining untestable_count.","agentId":"ae8d04658600cfb73","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TESTS_REWRITTEN\n\n- Total tests now: 26 (in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`)\n- New tests added: 6 (all existing 20 unchanged and still passing)\n- All passing: yes (26 passed)\n- Remaining untestable_count: 0 (`/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` is now `[]`)\n\nNew coverage (both previously-untestable requirements now exercised end-to-end through the real engine pipeline):\n\n`TestSilverquillCasualtyThroughRealCast` (real-cast \"as you cast\" path via `engine.casting.cast_spell`):\n- `test_real_cast_queues_casualty_trigger_above_the_spell` — real cast leaves the spell on the stack with the casualty trigger pushed above it (the `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired by `cast_spell` itself).\n- `test_real_cast_paying_casualty_sacrifices_and_copies` — resolving that trigger with \"yes\" sacrifices the creature and puts exactly one distinct copy on the stack.\n- `test_real_cast_declining_casualty_makes_no_copy` — declining leaves only the original spell, no sacrifice.\n\n`TestSilverquillCasualtyNewTargets` (copy may choose new targets):\n- `test_copy_can_retarget_a_different_creature` — uses a minimal targeted `_PingInstant`; cast at the original creature, pay casualty, choose new targets → copy's `targets` is the new creature and resolving marks damage on the NEW target while the original takes none.\n- `test_copy_keeps_original_target_when_retarget_declined` — declining the re-target prompt keeps the copy on the original target.\n\nNote on test design: in the new-target tests the two targetable creatures are 0-power so the dedicated power-1 \"Sacrifice\" creature is the sole eligible casualty (keeping the sacrifice auto-selected and the `DeterministicPlayer` scripts unambiguous, matching the implementation's `choose_card`-only-when->1-eligible contract). Updated rationale at `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":176929,"totalTokens":77969,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":76887,"output_tokens":740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":340},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":76887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":340,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":16,"searchCount":9,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":8,"linesAdded":327,"linesRemoved":37,"otherToolCount":0}}}
