{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DmWX8jjsApZBJrJaiTJrGw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n2\t\n3\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n4\t\n5\tWitherbloom, the Balancer is a `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Elder Dragon (5/5) with:\n6\t1. **Affinity for creatures** — costs `{1}` less per creature you control (self cost reduction).\n7\t2. **Flying, deathtouch**.\n8\t3. \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" — a static grant of the same affinity to the controller's instant/sorcery spells while Witherbloom is on the battlefield.\n9\t\n10\tThe engine's cost-reduction surface is `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game) -> int` (the generic reduction for casting a card), consumed by `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` which clamps the reduction to the generic portion of the mana cost. FDN 6 (Claws Out) is the in-repo precedent for the affinity self-reduction pattern. Tests assert observable behavior through `cost_reduction`, `get_cost_reduction`, and the real `cast_spell` pipeline (`card.mana_spent`).\n11\t\n12\t### TestWitherbloomProperties (static data)\n13\t- `test_is_creature`, `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`, `test_power_toughness` — base identity (5/5, `{6}{B}{G}`).\n14\t- `test_is_legendary`, `test_elder_dragon_subtypes` — Legendary supertype + \"Dragon\"/\"Elder\" subtypes from the type line.\n15\t- `test_has_flying`, `test_has_deathtouch` — evergreen keyword grants (these ARE `Keyword` enum members; Affinity intentionally is not, per the pinned `len(Keyword)==16`).\n16\t- `test_is_black_and_green`, `test_not_other_colors` — color identity B+G only.\n17\t\n18\t### TestWitherbloomSelfAffinity (own Affinity for creatures)\n19\t- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction` — empty battlefield -> reduction 0.\n20\t- `test_reduction_counts_creatures_you_control` — two other creatures -> reduction 2.\n21\t- `test_reduction_counts_itself_when_on_battlefield` — on battlefield with one other creature -> counts both (2). Affinity counts every creature you control, including the source if it is on the battlefield.\n22\t- `test_opponent_creatures_excluded` — only creatures *you* control count.\n23\t- `test_noncreature_permanents_not_counted` — an artifact you control is not a creature; excluded.\n24\t- `test_get_cost_reduction_clamped_to_generic` — 9 creatures but generic is `{6}` -> clamped to 6 (validates the engine clamp applies to Witherbloom).\n25\t- `test_get_cost_reduction_matches_creature_count_under_generic` — 3 creatures, under the generic -> reduction 3.\n26\t\n27\t### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinity (ability #3)\n28\t- `test_instant_cost_reduced_through_real_cast` — casting your own `{6}{B}` instant with Witherbloom + 2 creatures (3 total) reduces generic by 3; `mana_spent == 4` (3 generic + 1 black pip).\n29\t- `test_sorcery_cost_reduced_through_real_cast` — same grant applies to sorceries; `{6}{G}` with 2 creatures -> `mana_spent == 5`.\n30\t- `test_granted_reduction_visible_via_get_cost_reduction` — the grant is visible through the canonical query for a controller instant.\n31\t- `test_no_reduction_without_witherbloom_on_battlefield` — the grant only functions while Witherbloom is on the battlefield (negative guard).\n32\t- `test_opponent_spell_not_granted_affinity` — only *your* spells are granted affinity; an opponent's instant gets 0 (negative guard).\n33\t- `test_creature_spell_not_granted_affinity` — the grant is limited to instant/sorcery; a creature spell you cast gets 0 (negative guard).\n34\t- `test_granted_reduction_clamped_to_generic` — granted affinity is also clamped to the spell's generic cost (`{2}{B}` with 6 creatures -> 2).\n35\t\n36\t## Edge cases covered\n37\t- Source counting itself when on the battlefield (vs. when queried off-battlefield).\n38\t- Opponent creatures / noncreature permanents excluded from the creature count.\n39\t- Generic clamp applied to both Witherbloom itself and the granted spells.\n40\t- Scope of the grant: whose spells (controller-only) and which types (instant/sorcery-only); only while Witherbloom is on the battlefield.\n41\t- Real-cast `mana_spent` assertions, independent of how the implementer wires the grant into the engine reduction query.\n42\t\n43\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n44\t- Legend rule / Elder Dragon legendary uniqueness — engine-level, out of scope for this card's contract.\n45\t- Flying/deathtouch combat interactions — those keywords are tested by `engine_tests/` (combat/abilities); here we only assert the grants are present.\n46\t- Multiple simultaneous cost reducers from different sources (engine notes a simplified single-card model) — out of scope.\n47\t- The exact engine mechanism by which ability #3 reaches `get_cost_reduction` (implementation detail); tests pin only the observable reduction.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"d1797472-5bb1-415a-9026-b6e41d71eb4f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:06:45.677Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n\nWitherbloom, the Balancer is a `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Elder Dragon (5/5) with:\n1. **Affinity for creatures** — costs `{1}` less per creature you control (self cost reduction).\n2. **Flying, deathtouch**.\n3. \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" — a static grant of the same affinity to the controller's instant/sorcery spells while Witherbloom is on the battlefield.\n\nThe engine's cost-reduction surface is `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game) -> int` (the generic reduction for casting a card), consumed by `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` which clamps the reduction to the generic portion of the mana cost. FDN 6 (Claws Out) is the in-repo precedent for the affinity self-reduction pattern. Tests assert observable behavior through `cost_reduction`, `get_cost_reduction`, and the real `cast_spell` pipeline (`card.mana_spent`).\n\n### TestWitherbloomProperties (static data)\n- `test_is_creature`, `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`, `test_power_toughness` — base identity (5/5, `{6}{B}{G}`).\n- `test_is_legendary`, `test_elder_dragon_subtypes` — Legendary supertype + \"Dragon\"/\"Elder\" subtypes from the type line.\n- `test_has_flying`, `test_has_deathtouch` — evergreen keyword grants (these ARE `Keyword` enum members; Affinity intentionally is not, per the pinned `len(Keyword)==16`).\n- `test_is_black_and_green`, `test_not_other_colors` — color identity B+G only.\n\n### TestWitherbloomSelfAffinity (own Affinity for creatures)\n- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction` — empty battlefield -> reduction 0.\n- `test_reduction_counts_creatures_you_control` — two other creatures -> reduction 2.\n- `test_reduction_counts_itself_when_on_battlefield` — on battlefield with one other creature -> counts both (2). Affinity counts every creature you control, including the source if it is on the battlefield.\n- `test_opponent_creatures_excluded` — only creatures *you* control count.\n- `test_noncreature_permanents_not_counted` — an artifact you control is not a creature; excluded.\n- `test_get_cost_reduction_clamped_to_generic` — 9 creatures but generic is `{6}` -> clamped to 6 (validates the engine clamp applies to Witherbloom).\n- `test_get_cost_reduction_matches_creature_count_under_generic` — 3 creatures, under the generic -> reduction 3.\n\n### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinity (ability #3)\n- `test_instant_cost_reduced_through_real_cast` — casting your own `{6}{B}` instant with Witherbloom + 2 creatures (3 total) reduces generic by 3; `mana_spent == 4` (3 generic + 1 black pip).\n- `test_sorcery_cost_reduced_through_real_cast` — same grant applies to sorceries; `{6}{G}` with 2 creatures -> `mana_spent == 5`.\n- `test_granted_reduction_visible_via_get_cost_reduction` — the grant is visible through the canonical query for a controller instant.\n- `test_no_reduction_without_witherbloom_on_battlefield` — the grant only functions while Witherbloom is on the battlefield (negative guard).\n- `test_opponent_spell_not_granted_affinity` — only *your* spells are granted affinity; an opponent's instant gets 0 (negative guard).\n- `test_creature_spell_not_granted_affinity` — the grant is limited to instant/sorcery; a creature spell you cast gets 0 (negative guard).\n- `test_granted_reduction_clamped_to_generic` — granted affinity is also clamped to the spell's generic cost (`{2}{B}` with 6 creatures -> 2).\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Source counting itself when on the battlefield (vs. when queried off-battlefield).\n- Opponent creatures / noncreature permanents excluded from the creature count.\n- Generic clamp applied to both Witherbloom itself and the granted spells.\n- Scope of the grant: whose spells (controller-only) and which types (instant/sorcery-only); only while Witherbloom is on the battlefield.\n- Real-cast `mana_spent` assertions, independent of how the implementer wires the grant into the engine reduction query.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- Legend rule / Elder Dragon legendary uniqueness — engine-level, out of scope for this card's contract.\n- Flying/deathtouch combat interactions — those keywords are tested by `engine_tests/` (combat/abilities); here we only assert the grants are present.\n- Multiple simultaneous cost reducers from different sources (engine notes a simplified single-card model) — out of scope.\n- The exact engine mechanism by which ability #3 reaches `get_cost_reduction` (implementation detail); tests pin only the observable reduction.\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}}}
