{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDsNAwn7r4Pmvwvweyoob4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Miracle mechanic support (rule 702.94) — additive engine surface.\n2\t\n3\tMiracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability:\n4\t\n5\t    \"Miracle [cost]\" means \"You may reveal this card from your hand as you\n6\t    draw it if it's the first card you've drawn this turn. When you reveal\n7\t    this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its\n8\t    mana cost.\"\n9\t\n10\tThe engine has no native ``miracle`` keyword (and the :class:`~engine.types.Keyword`\n11\tenum is pinned at 16 members by ``engine_tests/test_types.py``), so miracle is\n12\tsurfaced via a per-card ``miracle_cost`` attribute and a small set of helper\n13\tfunctions here instead of a flag.\n14\t\n15\tContract exposed to cards / tests\n16\t----------------------------------\n17\t\n18\t* :func:`set_miracle_cost` — stamp a :class:`~engine.types.ManaCost` (the\n19\t  miracle/alternative cost) onto a card and mark it ``has_miracle = True``.\n20\t* :func:`clear_miracle_cost` — remove the stamp (used when the granting\n21\t  source leaves the battlefield / the card leaves the hand).\n22\t* :func:`get_miracle_cost` — read the assigned miracle cost (``None`` if the\n23\t  card has no miracle).\n24\t* :func:`is_first_draw_this_turn` — first-card-drawn-this-turn gating, reading\n25\t  the ``player.cards_drawn_this_turn`` counter the draw step maintains.\n26\t* :func:`can_miracle_cast` — ``True`` iff the just-drawn card has a miracle\n27\t  cost AND it is the first card drawn this turn.\n28\t* :func:`derive_miracle_cost` — DYNAMICALLY compute the miracle cost a just-drawn\n29\t  card has *right now*, by consulting active grants (permanents on the drawer's\n30\t  battlefield that expose a ``miracle_cost(game, card)`` grant method, e.g. a\n31\t  Lorehold). This is what makes miracle fire on a naturally-drawn card with no\n32\t  manual pre-stamping, and what makes the grant non-sticky: when no granter\n33\t  applies the derived cost is ``None`` even if a stale stamp is present.\n34\t* :func:`offer_miracle` — the draw-time hook: if the card may be miracle-cast\n35\t  and the controller says yes (``choose_yes_no``), cast it for the miracle\n36\t  cost as an alternative cost via :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`.\n37\t\n38\tThe miracle cost is paid as a normal mana cost (just a *different* cost), so\n39\tthe alternative-cost cast path pays from the player's mana pool.\n40\t\"\"\"\n41\t\n42\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n43\t\n44\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n45\t\n46\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n47\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n48\t    from engine.player import Player\n49\t    from engine.types import ManaCost\n50\t\n51\t\n52\t# Attribute name used to stamp the miracle cost onto a card.\n53\t_MIRACLE_COST_ATTR = \"miracle_cost\"\n54\t\n55\t\n56\tdef set_miracle_cost(card: Any, cost: \"ManaCost\") -> None:\n57\t    \"\"\"Assign *cost* as *card*'s miracle (alternative) cost.\n58\t\n59\t    Sets both ``card.miracle_cost`` and a ``card.has_miracle`` boolean flag\n60\t    so callers can detect the grant without a ``None`` comparison.\n61\t    \"\"\"\n62\t    setattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, cost)\n63\t    card.has_miracle = True\n64\t\n65\t\n66\tdef clear_miracle_cost(card: Any) -> None:\n67\t    \"\"\"Remove any miracle cost previously assigned to *card*.\"\"\"\n68\t    if hasattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR):\n69\t        try:\n70\t            delattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR)\n71\t        except AttributeError:\n72\t            setattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, None)\n73\t    card.has_miracle = False\n74\t\n75\t\n76\tdef get_miracle_cost(card: Any) -> \"ManaCost | None\":\n77\t    \"\"\"Return *card*'s assigned miracle cost, or ``None`` if it has none.\"\"\"\n78\t    return getattr(card, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, None)\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef derive_miracle_cost(\n82\t    game: \"GameState\", player: \"Player\", card: Any\n83\t) -> \"ManaCost | None\":\n84\t    \"\"\"Dynamically compute the miracle cost *card* has *right now* for *player*.\n85\t\n86\t    This is the authoritative, non-sticky source of a card's miracle cost at\n87\t    draw time.  It consults the active grants in play rather than relying solely\n88\t    on a pre-applied (and potentially stale) stamp:\n89\t\n90\t    * Every permanent on *player*'s battlefield that exposes a callable\n91\t      ``miracle_cost(game, card)`` grant method is asked whether it grants a\n92\t      miracle cost to *card* (e.g. Lorehold grants ``{2}`` to instant/sorcery\n93\t      cards in its controller's hand).  The first non-``None`` result wins.\n94\t    * If a grant applies, the stamp is (re)synchronised onto the card via\n95\t      :func:`set_miracle_cost` so downstream readers stay consistent, and the\n96\t      cost is returned.\n97\t    * If NO grant applies, any previously-applied stamp is cleared via\n98\t      :func:`clear_miracle_cost` and ``None`` is returned.  This is what makes\n99\t      the grant end when the granter leaves play (or the card leaves the hand):\n100\t      a card stamped earlier no longer offers miracle once no granter is active.\n101\t\n102\t    The drawn *card* is in *player*'s hand at draw time, so battlefield grants\n103\t    scoped to \"instant/sorcery cards in your hand\" (like Lorehold's) see it.\n104\t    \"\"\"\n105\t    granted: \"ManaCost | None\" = None\n106\t    battlefield = game.get_battlefield(player)\n107\t    for permanent in battlefield.get_all():\n108\t        grant = getattr(permanent, _MIRACLE_COST_ATTR, None)\n109\t        if not callable(grant):\n110\t            continue\n111\t        try:\n112\t            cost = grant(game, card)\n113\t        except TypeError:\n114\t            # Not a (game, card) grant method — skip defensively.\n115\t            continue\n116\t        if cost is not None:\n117\t            granted = cost\n118\t            break\n119\t\n120\t    if granted is not None:\n121\t        set_miracle_cost(card, granted)\n122\t        return granted\n123\t\n124\t    # No active granter: drop any stale stamp so the grant is not sticky.\n125\t    if get_miracle_cost(card) is not None:\n126\t        clear_miracle_cost(card)\n127\t    return None\n128\t\n129\t\n130\tdef _is_active_player(game: \"GameState\", player: \"Player\") -> bool:\n131\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *player* is the game's current active player.\n132\t\n133\t    Miracle's offer is presented on the drawing player's own turn (their draw\n134\t    step or a draw effect they control on their turn).  Draws taken during\n135\t    another player's turn (e.g. a loot effect resolving on an opponent's\n136\t    upkeep) are not offered a miracle cast here.  When the game exposes no\n137\t    active-player information we conservatively treat the draw as eligible.\n138\t    \"\"\"\n139\t    active = getattr(game, \"active_player\", None)\n140\t    if active is None:\n141\t        return True\n142\t    return active is player\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef is_first_draw_this_turn(player: \"Player\") -> bool:\n146\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if at most one card has been drawn by *player* this turn.\n147\t\n148\t    Miracle keys off \"the first card you've drawn this turn\".  The draw helper\n149\t    (:func:`engine.game.draw_card`) increments ``player.cards_drawn_this_turn``\n150\t    *before* firing the draw trigger, so when this is evaluated at draw time the\n151\t    counter reads ``1`` for the first draw of the turn.\n152\t    \"\"\"\n153\t    count = getattr(player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0)\n154\t    return count <= 1\n155\t\n156\t\n157\tdef can_miracle_cast(player: \"Player\", card: Any) -> bool:\n158\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* may be miracle-cast as it is drawn.\n159\t\n160\t    Requires both that *card* carries an assigned miracle cost and that it is\n161\t    the first card *player* has drawn this turn.\n162\t    \"\"\"\n163\t    if get_miracle_cost(card) is None:\n164\t        return False\n165\t    return is_first_draw_this_turn(player)\n166\t\n167\t\n168\tdef offer_miracle(game: \"GameState\", player: \"Player\", card: Any) -> bool:\n169\t    \"\"\"Draw-time miracle hook — offer to cast the just-drawn *card* for miracle.\n170\t\n171\t    Returns ``True`` if the card was miracle-cast (put on the stack), ``False``\n172\t    otherwise.  No-op (returns ``False``) when the card has no miracle cost or\n173\t    it is not the first card drawn this turn.\n174\t\n175\t    The optionality is driven by ``player.choose_yes_no`` (the \"you may\"\n176\t    clause).  On a yes, the card is cast for its miracle cost via the\n177\t    alternative-cost cast path.\n178\t\n179\t    The miracle cost is derived DYNAMICALLY from the grants active right now\n180\t    (see :func:`derive_miracle_cost`), so a naturally-drawn card gets the offer\n181\t    with no manual pre-stamping, and a stale stamp left over from a granter that\n182\t    has since left play does NOT produce an offer.\n183\t\n184\t    The offer is scoped to the *active player*'s own draw (their draw step / a\n185\t    draw effect on their turn).  Draws taken on another player's turn — e.g. a\n186\t    looting effect that resolves during an opponent's upkeep — do not present a\n187\t    miracle offer here.\n188\t    \"\"\"\n189\t    if not _is_active_player(game, player):\n190\t        return False\n191\t\n192\t    cost = derive_miracle_cost(game, player, card)\n193\t    if cost is None:\n194\t        return False\n195\t    if not is_first_draw_this_turn(player):\n196\t        return False\n197\t\n198\t    name = getattr(card, \"name\", \"card\")\n199\t    if hasattr(player, \"choose_yes_no\"):\n200\t        if not player.choose_yes_no(f\"Cast {name!r} for its miracle cost?\"):\n201\t            return False\n202\t\n203\t    from engine.casting import cast_spell_alternative, CastingError\n204\t\n205\t    try:\n206\t        cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, cost)\n207\t    except CastingError:\n208\t        return False\n209\t    return True\n210\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EXUd8sdvZTu54EM9DsV9js","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"2acc45c9-6cd9-4a59-a4ae-aa5dc0da6951","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:07:21.028Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
