{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019EZYUhLjqQ2HBdjQGSZVV5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013zzM2C83D1XXkrX7FDDXRy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## Card (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n`WitherbloomTheBalancer` subclasses `Creature` (mirrors the SOS Elder Dragon\nprecedent in sos_226). Static data set via `kwargs.setdefault`: `{6}{B}{G}`,\n5/5, Legendary supertype, `{Elder, Dragon}` subtypes, `Keyword.FLYING |\nKeyword.DEATHTOUCH`, `colors={BLACK, GREEN}`, rules text carrying the Affinity\nreminder (Affinity is intentionally NOT a `Keyword` enum member — the enum is\npinned at 16).\n\n### Own Affinity for creatures\n`cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of creatures the controller controls\non the battlefield (`_count_creatures_controlled`), counting Witherbloom itself\nonce it is on the battlefield, excluding opponents' creatures and noncreature\npermanents. The engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps this to the generic\nportion of the mana cost (already-existing behavior), satisfying the\nclamp-to-{6} tests.\n\n### Granted affinity (ability #3)\nExposed as an additive grant method\n`affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, spell, controller) -> int`. It returns the\ncontroller's creature count for the controller's instant/sorcery spells, and 0\notherwise (wrong controller, or non-instant/sorcery spell). This is the\ndynamic-derivation analogue of the miracle grant in `engine/miracle.py`.\n\n## Engine change (`engine/casting.py`, additive)\n`get_cost_reduction` now additively folds in `_granted_cost_reduction`, a new\nhelper that walks the controller's battlefield and sums the result of any\npermanent exposing a callable `affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, card,\ncontroller)`. This makes the granted affinity reach `get_cost_reduction` for\nspells that do NOT themselves implement `cost_reduction` (e.g. a vanilla\n`Instant`), and through the real `cast_spell` pipeline it reduces\n`card.mana_spent`.\n\n### How the grant reaches `get_cost_reduction`\nFor any spell being cast, `get_cost_reduction` reads `card.cost_reduction`\n(intrinsic) AND then queries battlefield granters via\n`_granted_cost_reduction`. Because the grant lives on a battlefield permanent\n(Witherbloom), it only functions while Witherbloom is on the battlefield\n(negative-guard test passes: no Witherbloom -> no grant). Scope (controller-only,\ninstant/sorcery-only) is enforced inside `affinity_for_creatures_grant`.\n\n### No double-counting\n- The grant method scopes itself to instant/sorcery spells, so when querying\n  Witherbloom's own cost (a creature spell), the grant returns 0 — only its\n  intrinsic `cost_reduction` applies.\n- During casting, Witherbloom is on the stack (not the battlefield), so its own\n  grant is never consulted for its own cast.\n- In the current single-source SOS model only one such granter exists, so there\n  is no inter-grant double counting.\n\n## Blast radius / safety\nChange is purely additive: a new helper plus one summation line. Existing\nsingle-card self-reduction behavior is preserved (the grant sum is 0 when no\ngranter is present). Full suites pass: `cards/sos/sos_245` (24),\n`engine_tests/`, `cards/fdn/`, `cards/sos/` — 1432 passed total. No engine\nsymbols renamed/moved/deleted; no test files modified.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone. Affinity surfaced via `cost_reduction` + rules text (not a Keyword),\nconsistent with KEY_DECISIONS conventions for non-enum mechanics.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":219,"cache_read_input_tokens":58570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":219,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EXUd8sdvZTu54EM9DsV9js","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"091bae81-e990-464d-9b80-ada0fdcf20bc","request_id":"req_011CbcWmJXRiKSzn8Mcc7eM4","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
