{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EXUd8sdvZTu54EM9DsV9js","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"IMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: 2\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: Witherbloom implemented as a Creature with affinity-for-creatures cost_reduction plus an additive affinity_for_creatures_grant; get_cost_reduction now folds in battlefield grants so the granted affinity reaches the cost query and real cast pipeline. All 24 card tests pass; engine_tests + cards/fdn + cards/sos all green (1432 passed)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acde2f771168e800f (use SendMessage with to: 'acde2f771168e800f' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 62544\ntool_uses: 26\nduration_ms: 129693</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"14d3a9f4-4852-4795-8037-3cd4e35b5b04","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:09:22.990Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are implementing a Magic: The Gathering card (TDD green phase), with additive engine support if needed.\n\nCARD: sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer ({6}{B}{G} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5)\n- \"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\"\n- \"Flying, deathtouch\"\n- \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n\n- Spec: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_spec.json\n- Implementation file you complete: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py\n- Test file (already written — you MUST NOT modify it): /workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py\n- Test rationale (READ — explains the contracts the tests assert): /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md\n\nKEY CONTRACTS THE TESTS ASSERT (must satisfy):\n- Static: 5/5, Flying, Deathtouch, Legendary, Elder Dragon, colors {BLACK, GREEN}. (Affinity is NOT a Keyword enum member — engine pins len(Keyword)==16; surface it via cost_reduction + rules text. Flying/Deathtouch ARE enum members.)\n- Self Affinity for creatures: `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of creatures the controller controls (counting itself when on the battlefield; excluding opponents' creatures and noncreature permanents). The engine `get_cost_reduction` clamps to the generic portion.\n- Granted affinity (ability #3): while Witherbloom is on the battlefield, the controller's INSTANT/SORCERY spells also get affinity for creatures — visible through the canonical `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` query AND through a real `cast_spell` (observed via `card.mana_spent`). Scope: only the controller's spells, only instants/sorceries, only while Witherbloom is on the battlefield. Opponent spells and creature spells get 0.\n\nREFERENCES (read for API discovery — rich docstrings):\n- engine/card.py (cost_reduction hook), engine/casting.py (get_cost_reduction, cast_spell, mana_spent), engine/types.py\n- FDN 6 (Claws Out) — in-repo precedent for the affinity self-reduction pattern. KEY_DECISIONS.md (card colors; mana_spent; the miracle dynamic-grant pattern in engine/miracle.py is a good model for how a battlefield permanent can grant a cost effect to the controller's spells).\n- RULEBOOK.txt (grep, don't read whole) for Affinity (702.41).\n\nNOTE ON THE GRANT: get_cost_reduction is called for ANY spell being cast. For ability #3, the granted reduction must reach get_cost_reduction for the controller's instant/sorcery spells. Consider having get_cost_reduction (or the cost_reduction query path) also consult active \"affinity granters\" on the controller's battlefield (a dynamic-derivation approach, analogous to the miracle grant in engine/miracle.py), so the grant works for spells that don't themselves implement cost_reduction. Keep it scoped and avoid double-counting if a spell both has its own affinity and is granted it. Make additive engine changes as needed; do not break existing get_cost_reduction behavior or other SOS/FDN cards' cost reduction.\n\nENGINE RULES (from AGENTS.md):\n- Additive only: may add methods/classes/helpers/files, modify existing function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; MUST NOT break engine_tests pinned counts; MUST NOT modify test files.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Read spec, test file, rationale.\n2. Implement the card so ALL 24 tests in tests.py pass.\n3. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`, `pytest engine_tests/`, `pytest cards/fdn/`, `pytest cards/sos/` to confirm nothing breaks (cost-reduction changes are high blast-radius).\n4. If a test is genuinely WRONG, do NOT modify it — return DISPUTE with details.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Implementation to /workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py (+ any engine changes).\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff — `git diff` of all changes.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md — what you did, how the granted affinity reaches get_cost_reduction, engine changes, any spec deviations.\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-files.txt — modified files.\n- Upsert this card's entry into /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json (match by card: \"sos_245\"). Keep other entries intact.\n\nReturn either IMPL_DONE (files_changed, tests_passing, diff_path, rationale_path, notes) or DISPUTE (tests_failing, disputed_tests, dispute_path, notes) exactly as specified.","agentId":"acde2f771168e800f","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"IMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: 2\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: Witherbloom implemented as a Creature with affinity-for-creatures cost_reduction plus an additive affinity_for_creatures_grant; get_cost_reduction now folds in battlefield grants so the granted affinity reaches the cost query and real cast pipeline. All 24 card tests pass; engine_tests + cards/fdn + cards/sos all green (143