{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013qdeU96y331KZ9KZjjAQDN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n2\t\n3\t## Card (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n4\t`WitherbloomTheBalancer` subclasses `Creature` (mirrors the SOS Elder Dragon\n5\tprecedent in sos_226). Static data set via `kwargs.setdefault`: `{6}{B}{G}`,\n6\t5/5, Legendary supertype, `{Elder, Dragon}` subtypes, `Keyword.FLYING |\n7\tKeyword.DEATHTOUCH`, `colors={BLACK, GREEN}`, rules text carrying the Affinity\n8\treminder (Affinity is intentionally NOT a `Keyword` enum member — the enum is\n9\tpinned at 16).\n10\t\n11\t### Own Affinity for creatures\n12\t`cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of creatures the controller controls\n13\ton the battlefield (`_count_creatures_controlled`), counting Witherbloom itself\n14\tonce it is on the battlefield, excluding opponents' creatures and noncreature\n15\tpermanents. The engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps this to the generic\n16\tportion of the mana cost (already-existing behavior), satisfying the\n17\tclamp-to-{6} tests.\n18\t\n19\t### Granted affinity (ability #3)\n20\tExposed as an additive grant method\n21\t`affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, spell, controller) -> int`. It returns the\n22\tcontroller's creature count for the controller's instant/sorcery spells, and 0\n23\totherwise (wrong controller, or non-instant/sorcery spell). This is the\n24\tdynamic-derivation analogue of the miracle grant in `engine/miracle.py`.\n25\t\n26\t## Engine change (`engine/casting.py`, additive)\n27\t`get_cost_reduction` now additively folds in `_granted_cost_reduction`, a new\n28\thelper that walks the controller's battlefield and sums the result of any\n29\tpermanent exposing a callable `affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, card,\n30\tcontroller)`. This makes the granted affinity reach `get_cost_reduction` for\n31\tspells that do NOT themselves implement `cost_reduction` (e.g. a vanilla\n32\t`Instant`), and through the real `cast_spell` pipeline it reduces\n33\t`card.mana_spent`.\n34\t\n35\t### How the grant reaches `get_cost_reduction`\n36\tFor any spell being cast, `get_cost_reduction` reads `card.cost_reduction`\n37\t(intrinsic) AND then queries battlefield granters via\n38\t`_granted_cost_reduction`. Because the grant lives on a battlefield permanent\n39\t(Witherbloom), it only functions while Witherbloom is on the battlefield\n40\t(negative-guard test passes: no Witherbloom -> no grant). Scope (controller-only,\n41\tinstant/sorcery-only) is enforced inside `affinity_for_creatures_grant`.\n42\t\n43\t### No double-counting\n44\t- The grant method scopes itself to instant/sorcery spells, so when querying\n45\t  Witherbloom's own cost (a creature spell), the grant returns 0 — only its\n46\t  intrinsic `cost_reduction` applies.\n47\t- During casting, Witherbloom is on the stack (not the battlefield), so its own\n48\t  grant is never consulted for its own cast.\n49\t- In the current single-source SOS model only one such granter exists, so there\n50\t  is no inter-grant double counting.\n51\t\n52\t## Blast radius / safety\n53\tChange is purely additive: a new helper plus one summation line. Existing\n54\tsingle-card self-reduction behavior is preserved (the grant sum is 0 when no\n55\tgranter is present). Full suites pass: `cards/sos/sos_245` (24),\n56\t`engine_tests/`, `cards/fdn/`, `cards/sos/` — 1432 passed total. No engine\n57\tsymbols renamed/moved/deleted; no test files modified.\n58\t\n59\t## Spec deviations\n60\tNone. Affinity surfaced via `cost_reduction` + rules text (not a Keyword),\n61\tconsistent with KEY_DECISIONS conventions for non-enum mechanics.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"f095b69e-518f-4420-9583-bdbde8fd5787","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:09:26.108Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## Card (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n`WitherbloomTheBalancer` subclasses `Creature` (mirrors the SOS Elder Dragon\nprecedent in sos_226). Static data set via `kwargs.setdefault`: `{6}{B}{G}`,\n5/5, Legendary supertype, `{Elder, Dragon}` subtypes, `Keyword.FLYING |\nKeyword.DEATHTOUCH`, `colors={BLACK, GREEN}`, rules text carrying the Affinity\nreminder (Affinity is intentionally NOT a `Keyword` enum member — the enum is\npinned at 16).\n\n### Own Affinity for creatures\n`cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of creatures the controller controls\non the battlefield (`_count_creatures_controlled`), counting Witherbloom itself\nonce it is on the battlefield, excluding opponents' creatures and noncreature\npermanents. The engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps this to the generic\nportion of the mana cost (already-existing behavior), satisfying the\nclamp-to-{6} tests.\n\n### Granted affinity (ability #3)\nExposed as an additive grant method\n`affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, spell, controller) -> int`. It returns the\ncontroller's creature count for the controller's instant/sorcery spells, and 0\notherwise (wrong controller, or non-instant/sorcery spell). This is the\ndynamic-derivation analogue of the miracle grant in `engine/miracle.py`.\n\n## Engine change (`engine/casting.py`, additive)\n`get_cost_reduction` now additively folds in `_granted_cost_reduction`, a new\nhelper that walks the controller's battlefield and sums the result of any\npermanent exposing a callable `affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, card,\ncontroller)`. This makes the granted affinity reach `get_cost_reduction` for\nspells that do NOT themselves implement `cost_reduction` (e.g. a vanilla\n`Instant`), and through the real `cast_spell` pipeline it reduces\n`card.mana_spent`.\n\n### How the grant reaches `get_cost_reduction`\nFor any spell being cast, `get_cost_reduction` reads `card.cost_reduction`\n(intrinsic) AND then queries battlefield granters via\n`_granted_cost_reduction`. Because the grant lives on a battlefield permanent\n(Witherbloom), it only functions while Witherbloom is on the battlefield\n(negative-guard test passes: no Witherbloom -> no grant). Scope (controller-only,\ninstant/sorcery-only) is enforced inside `affinity_for_creatures_grant`.\n\n### No double-counting\n- The grant method scopes itself to instant/sorcery spells, so when querying\n  Witherbloom's own cost (a creature spell), the grant returns 0 — only its\n  intrinsic `cost_reduction` applies.\n- During casting, Witherbloom is on the stack (not the battlefield), so its own\n  grant is never consulted for its own cast.\n- In the current single-source SOS model only one such granter exists, so there\n  is no inter-grant double counting.\n\n## Blast radius / safety\nChange is purely additive: a new helper plus one summation line. Existing\nsingle-card self-reduction behavior is preserved (the grant sum is 0 when no\ngranter is present). Full suites pass: `cards/sos/sos_245` (24),\n`engine_tests/`, `cards/fdn/`, `cards/sos/` — 1432 passed total. No engine\nsymbols renamed/moved/deleted; no test files modified.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone. Affinity surfaced via `cost_reduction` + rules text (not a Keyword),\nconsistent with KEY_DECISIONS conventions for non-enum mechanics.\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}}}
