{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRBQwTtzkom35soNdSiLbW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, cross-run conventions and decisions.\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t## Engine: spell resolution → graveyard is a replaceable move (sos_1)\n7\t`engine/casting._resolve_spell` now routes a resolving non-permanent spell's\n8\tstack→graveyard move through the replacement manager via the additive\n9\t`SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`,\n10\tin `engine/events.py`). Cards needing \"if this spell would go to the graveyard,\n11\texile/do X instead\" should register a `ReplacementEffect` keyed to the spell that\n12\tmatches `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` and rewrites `destination`. Default\n13\tbehavior (no matching replacement → graveyard) is unchanged.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: converge (sos_4)\n16\tConverge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast = `len(set(self.colors_spent))`.\n17\tThe engine records `colors_spent` during payment (FDN 205 convention). Initialize\n18\t`self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__` so an unpaid/empty cast yields X=0 and a\n19\tsafe no-op resolution. \"Any target\" filter: a player (`hasattr(obj,\"life\")`) OR a\n20\tpermanent whose `card_types` intersects {CREATURE, PLANESWALKER} (engine/types.py\n21\thas no BATTLE type).\n22\t\n23\t## Engine: card/token colors + Prepared mechanic (sos_13)\n24\t- `CardImpl`/`Creature` now carry a `colors: set[Color]` attribute. Pass `colors`\n25\t  explicitly for tokens (no mana cost); otherwise it derives from the mana cost's\n26\t  colored/hybrid pips (`_colors_from_mana_cost` in engine/card.py). `engine/game.create_token`\n27\t  accepts/sets token colors.\n28\t- `engine/protection.get_colors` treats a present-but-EMPTY `colors` set as \"no\n29\t  explicit color info\" and falls through to mana-cost / `.color` derivation\n30\t  (so colorless cards carrying an empty set don't mask derivation).\n31\t- **Prepared** mechanic is NOT a `Keyword` enum member (engine_tests/test_types.py\n32\t  pins `len(Keyword) == 16`). Surface it via a `card.is_prepared` bool + rules text.\n33\t  The prepared cast loop is driven by additive `engine.casting.cast_prepared_spell(game, permanent, targets=None)`:\n34\t  copies the `prepare_spell`, exiles the copy, clears `is_prepared`, free-casts it.\n35\t  Expose the inset face as `card.prepare_spell` (aliases `prepared_spell`/`other_face`).\n36\t\n37\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking + beginning-of-main-phase trigger (sos_57)\n38\t- `ManaPool.last_payment_total` (read-only property) records the TOTAL quantity of\n39\t  mana paid on the last payment (alongside the existing `last_payment_colors`).\n40\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell` persists it onto the spell as `card.mana_spent`\n41\t  (diverges from CMC for X / cost-reduced spells). Cards reading mana spent should\n42\t  use `spell.mana_spent`, falling back to `mana_cost.cmc` for stack-placed spells.\n43\t- `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fields: `player`, `phase`) is\n44\t  fired in `engine.turn.run_turn` at the start of each main phase\n45\t  (PRECOMBAT_MAIN / POSTCOMBAT_MAIN when `game.step is None`), mirroring the\n46\t  BeginningOfUpkeep firing pattern. Use it for begin-of-main-phase delayed effects;\n47\t  scope the trigger condition to `event.player is controller` and make one-shot\n48\t  delayed effects unregister themselves after firing.\n49\t\n50\t## Engine: surveil / coin flip / skip-turns (sos_97)\n51\t- `engine.game.surveil(game, player, amount)`: looks at exactly the top `amount`\n52\t  library cards, asks `player.choose_yes_no` per card (True = keep on top in\n53\t  original order, False = move to graveyard).\n54\t- `engine.game.flip_coin(game)`: returns heads via `random.random() < 0.5`\n55\t  (patch `random.random`/`choice`/`randint` to force outcomes in tests).\n56\t- `engine.game.skip_turns(game, player, count)`: records the skip count on\n57\t  `player.skipped_turns` and `game.skipped_turns[seat]`. `GameState.advance_phase`\n58\t  consumes it via the additive `_consume_skipped_turns()` helper — symmetric to\n59\t  the existing `extra_turns` FIFO: when rotation would make a skipped seat active,\n60\t  decrement its counter and advance again. No-op when `skipped_turns` is empty\n61\t  (existing behavior unchanged).\n62\t\n63\t## Engine: miracle mechanic + alternative-cost casting (sos_201)\n64\t- Miracle is NOT a Keyword enum member (engine_tests pins len(Keyword)==16). It is\n65\t  modelled in `engine/miracle.py`: set/get/clear_miracle_cost (stamp helpers),\n66\t  `is_first_draw_this_turn(player)` (reads `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`, reset to\n67\t  0 at the untap step in engine/turn.py), `derive_miracle_cost(game, player, card)`\n68\t  (DYNAMICALLY queries the drawer's battlefield for permanents exposing a callable\n69\t  `miracle_cost(game, card)` grant — e.g. Lorehold), and `offer_miracle`.\n70\t- `engine.game.draw_card` calls `offer_miracle` on every draw; the grant is derived\n71\t  dynamically (not a sticky stamp) so it ends when the granter leaves play, and a\n72\t  naturally-drawn card gets the offer with no pre-stamping. Scoped to the active\n73\t  player's own draw.\n74\t- A miracle/alternative-cost grant on a permanent is exposed as a\n75\t  `miracle_cost(game, card) -> ManaCost | None` method returning the cost for\n76\t  controller-hand instants/sorceries.\n77\t- `engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, alternative_cost, from_zone=HAND)`:\n78\t  mirrors the normal cast pipeline but pays an explicit alternative cost (no cost\n79\t  reduction applied) and skips sorcery/instant timing. Use for alternative-cost\n80\t  mechanics (miracle, etc.).\n81\t\n82\t## Engine: cast_spell now fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent + casualty (sos_226)\n83\t- `engine.casting.cast_spell` now fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (via the additive\n84\t  `_fire_spell_cast_event`) AFTER the spell's StackObject is pushed. Previously the\n85\t  event existed but was never fired by the cast pipeline. Any \"whenever you cast an\n86\t  instant/sorcery\" or cast-time grant can now rely on it firing through a real cast.\n87\t  `cast_spell_free` / `cast_spell_alternative` are intentionally left NOT firing it.\n88\t- Casualty modelled as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (scoped to the\n89\t  controller's instant/sorcery spells, only while the granter is on the\n90\t  battlefield): on resolve, optional `choose_yes_no`, sacrifice a power>=1 creature,\n91\t  then `engine.stack.copy_spell(..., new_targets=...)` to copy with optional new\n92\t  targets (chosen via `choose_target` per target requirement).\n93\t- KNOWN rules-fidelity gap: casualty excludes the source creature itself from\n94\t  eligible sacrifices (forced by the pinned test design). See RUN_DECISIONS.md.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018LVqqkhmpevT52yENkiaDb","session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"dca2be2a-fdc6-42c2-822f-0a4c62140544","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:09:44.807Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_245 implementation"}
