{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QjWyK9jPmgpzJwHGWV2k9r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RVja8Vzwsa5mnamKhCjKig","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> KEY_DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Engine: granted cost reduction via battlefield permanents (sos_245)\n`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` now folds in `_granted_cost_reduction`, which\nwalks the SPELL CONTROLLER's battlefield and sums the result of any permanent\nexposing a callable `affinity_for_creatures_grant(game, card, controller) -> int`\n(returns 0 for ineligible spells). This lets a battlefield permanent grant a cost\nreduction to the controller's spells (e.g. \"instant and sorcery spells you cast\nhave affinity for creatures\") even when the spell itself implements no\ncost_reduction. The combined reduction is still clamped to the generic portion;\nsum is 0 when no granter is present (existing behavior preserved). Pattern is the\ncost-reduction analogue of the dynamic miracle grant (engine/miracle.py).\nEOF\ngit add cards/sos/sos_245/ engine/casting.py FILES_MODIFIED.json KEY_DECISIONS.md RUN_DECISIONS.md && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat: implement card sos_245\n\nWitherbloom, the Balancer: 5/5 Flying/Deathtouch Elder Dragon with affinity\nfor creatures, granting that affinity to the controller's instant/sorcery\nspells. Extends engine.casting.get_cost_reduction to fold in cost-reduction\ngrants from battlefield permanents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Log convention and commit sos_245"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":221,"cache_read_input_tokens":146900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":221},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":nu