{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZEVTuyrysYRDGxcUaYPui","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no API for tagging produced mana with a spend restriction or for querying/enforcing how mana may be spent. The FDN reference card Secluded Courtyard (cards/fdn/fdn_267/card_impl.py) documents this same restriction as unenforced ('ENGINE LIMITATION: The engine does not support conditional mana spending restrictions').\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An engine mana-tagging surface (e.g. ManaPool entries carrying a spend-restriction predicate, and a payment path that filters restricted mana by the spell/ability being paid for) so a test could assert the restricted mana is usable only for instant/sorcery casts.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"...it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\"\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The +1/+0 cast trigger is an ability granted to the permanent only while it is animated. The spec does not pin a stable observable surface for the grant (it is not a printed Keyword and its trigger-registration shape is an internal implementation detail), so asserting it would test the implementation rather than the card's contract. The animation itself (becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature, still a land) IS tested.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A documented, stable hook for the granted cast trigger while animated (e.g. registering a controller-scoped SpellCastTriggeredEvent only while CREATURE is in card_types, observable via the trigger_manager or via the creature's power increasing by 1 per instant/sorcery cast this turn) that the Implementer commits to as part of the contract.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"3153cf5a-9f39-41a5-ad04-f6579855cd6d","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:13:48.220Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n    \"requirement\": \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no API for tagging produced mana with a spend restriction or for querying/enforcing how mana may be spent. The FDN reference card Secluded Courtyard (cards/fdn/fdn_267/card_impl.py) documents this same restriction as unenforced ('ENGINE LIMITATION: The engine does not support conditional mana spending restrictions').\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An engine mana-tagging surface (e.g. ManaPool entries carrying a spend-restriction predicate, and a payment path that filters restricted mana by the spell/ability being paid for) so a test could assert the restricted mana is usable only for instant/sorcery casts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n    \"requirement\": \"...it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\"\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The +1/+0 cast trigger is an ability granted to the permanent only while it is animated. The spec does not pin a stable observable surface for the grant (it is not a printed Keyword and its trigger-registration shape is an internal implementation detail), so asserting it would test the implementation rather than the card's contract. The animation itself (becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature, still a land) IS tested.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A documented, stable hook for the granted cast trigger while animated (e.g. registering a controller-scoped SpellCastTriggeredEvent only while CREATURE is in card_types, observable via the trigger_manager or via the creature's power increasi