{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GRmp2mCiduvs6E8a6ZDCRk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n2\t\n3\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n4\t\n5\tGreat Hall of the Biblioplex is a Land with three abilities:\n6\t\n7\t- `{T}: Add {C}.`\n8\t- `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.`\n9\t- `{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n10\t\n11\tTests are organized into three classes and drive the engine's stable ability\n12\tsurfaces directly (`get_mana_abilities`, `get_activated_abilities`) — the same\n13\tpattern the FDN land references use (Plains / FDN 272, Secluded Courtyard /\n14\tFDN 267).\n15\t\n16\t### TestGreatHallProperties — static card data\n17\t- `test_name` / `test_is_land` / `test_has_land_card_type` — identity and base type.\n18\t- `test_is_not_a_creature_by_default` — guards against an implementation that wrongly types it as a creature before the `{5}` ability is used.\n19\t- `test_has_no_mana_cost` — lands have no mana cost.\n20\t- `test_is_colorless` — no colored pips anywhere, so `colors` is empty (the card's color line is `[]`).\n21\t- `test_cannot_be_cast` — lands are played, not cast (`can_cast` is `False`).\n22\t\n23\t### TestGreatHallManaAbilities — the two mana abilities\n24\t- `test_exposes_two_mana_abilities` — exactly two `ManaAbility` instances.\n25\t- `test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless` / `test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land` / `test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped` — the `{T}: Add {C}` ability taps the land and yields one colorless; a tapped land cannot pay the tap cost.\n26\t- `test_any_color_ability_pays_one_life` / `test_any_color_ability_adds_chosen_color` / `test_any_color_ability_taps_the_land` — the second ability pays 1 life, taps, and produces one mana of the controller's chosen color (color choice scripted via `DeterministicPlayer`).\n27\t- `test_any_color_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped` — a tapped land cannot activate the second ability, and a failed activation does not drain life.\n28\t\n29\t### TestGreatHallAnimation — the `{5}` animation ability\n30\t- `test_exposes_one_activated_ability` — exactly one `ActivatedAbility`.\n31\t- `test_animation_cost_consumes_five_generic_mana` / `test_animation_cost_fails_without_mana` — the cost consumes 5 generic mana and fails when only 4 is available.\n32\t- `test_becomes_a_creature` / `test_is_still_a_land_after_animation` — after activation (and a continuous-effect recompute) the permanent gains the CREATURE type but retains LAND (\"It's still a land\").\n33\t- `test_becomes_two_four` — power/toughness become 2/4.\n34\t- `test_becomes_a_wizard` — gains the Wizard subtype.\n35\t- `test_animation_guarded_when_already_a_creature` — the \"If this land isn't a creature\" guard: activating a second time while already a creature must not double the P/T or otherwise stack.\n36\t\n37\t## Edge cases covered\n38\t- Tapped-source cost failure for both mana abilities (and no life loss on a failed any-color activation).\n39\t- Insufficient mana for the `{5}` ability.\n40\t- The \"isn't a creature\" conditional guard against re-animation stacking.\n41\t- LAND type retained alongside CREATURE after animation.\n42\t\n43\t## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n44\t- **\"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\"** The engine has\n45\t  no surface for tagging mana with a spend restriction; the FDN reference card\n46\t  Secluded Courtyard (FDN 267) explicitly documents this as an engine\n47\t  limitation. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n48\t- **The granted \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature\n49\t  gets +1/+0 until end of turn\" trigger on the animated creature.** This is a\n50\t  granted ability that only exists while animated; its registration shape is an\n51\t  internal implementation detail not pinned by the spec, so asserting it would\n52\t  test the implementation rather than the contract. Recorded in\n53\t  `untestable.json` so the Coordinator can decide whether to add a stable hook.\n54\t- Summoning-sickness interaction (a freshly animated manland can't attack the\n55\t  turn it was animated unless under your control since your most recent turn\n56\t  began) — this is general engine behavior, not card-specific, and out of scope.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ed3988e-944a-4908-bc92-4f8937d76445","uuid":"9097b0cd-b9e9-4d18-bf78-66f81fbf4720","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:14:03.365Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n\nGreat Hall of the Biblioplex is a Land with three abilities:\n\n- `{T}: Add {C}.`\n- `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.`\n- `{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n\nTests are organized into three classes and drive the engine's stable ability\nsurfaces directly (`get_mana_abilities`, `get_activated_abilities`) — the same\npattern the FDN land references use (Plains / FDN 272, Secluded Courtyard /\nFDN 267).\n\n### TestGreatHallProperties — static card data\n- `test_name` / `test_is_land` / `test_has_land_card_type` — identity and base type.\n- `test_is_not_a_creature_by_default` — guards against an implementation that wrongly types it as a creature before the `{5}` ability is used.\n- `test_has_no_mana_cost` — lands have no mana cost.\n- `test_is_colorless` — no colored pips anywhere, so `colors` is empty (the card's color line is `[]`).\n- `test_cannot_be_cast` — lands are played, not cast (`can_cast` is `False`).\n\n### TestGreatHallManaAbilities — the two mana abilities\n- `test_exposes_two_mana_abilities` — exactly two `ManaAbility` instances.\n- `test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless` / `test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land` / `test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped` — the `{T}: Add {C}` ability taps the land and yields one colorless; a tapped land cannot pay the tap cost.\n- `test_any_color_ability_pays_one_life` / `test_any_color_ability_adds_chosen_color` / `test_any_color_ability_taps_the_land` — the second ability pays 1 life, taps, and produces one mana of the controller's chosen color (color choice scripted via `DeterministicPlayer`).\n- `test_any_color_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped` — a tapped land cannot activate the second ability, and a failed activation does not drain life.\n\n### TestGreatHallAnimation — the `{5}` animation ability\n- `test_exposes_one_activated_ability` — exactly one `ActivatedAbility`.\n- `test_animation_cost_consumes_five_generic_mana` / `test_animation_cost_fails_without_mana` — the cost consumes 5 generic mana and fails when only 4 is available.\n- `test_becomes_a_creature` / `test_is_still_a_land_after_animation` — after activation (and a continuous-effect recompute) the permanent gains the CREATURE type but retains LAND (\"It's still a land\").\n- `test_becomes_two_four` — power/toughness become 2/4.\n- `test_becomes_a_wizard` — gains the Wizard subtype.\n- `test_animation_guarded_when_already_a_creature` — the \"If this land isn't a creature\" guard: activating a second time while already a creature must not double the P/T or otherwise stack.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Tapped-source cost failure for both mana abilities (and no life loss on a failed any-color activation).\n- Insufficient mana for the `{5}` ability.\n- The \"isn't a creature\" conditional guard against re-animation stacking.\n- LAND type retained alongside CREATURE after animation.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n- **\"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\"** The engine has\n  no surface for tagging mana with a spend restriction; the FDN reference card\n  Secluded Courtyard (FDN 267) explicitly documents this as an engine\n  limitation. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **The granted \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature\n  gets +1/+0 until end of turn\" trigger on the animated creature.** This is a\n  granted ability that only exists while animated; its registration shape is an\n  internal implementation detail not pinned by the spec, so asserting it would\n  test the implementation rather than the contract. Recorded in\n  `untestable.json` so the Coordinator can decide whether to add a stable hook.\n- Summoning-sickness interaction (a freshly animated manland can't attack the\n  turn it was animated unless under your control since your most recent turn\n  began) — this is general engine behavior, not card-specific, and out of scope.\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
